// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — 詞類變化 Word Formation (tools/wordform/build.py)
window.WF_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"absolute – adjust · 15 字族 · 33 題","cards":[{"w":"absolute","p":"adj.","d":"complete and total; without any limit","c":"絕對的；完全的","s":"The cave was in absolute darkness when we turned off our torches, and we could not even see our own hands.","t":"當我們關掉手電筒時，洞穴裡一片完全的黑暗，而我們甚至看不到自己的手。"},{"w":"absolutely","p":"adv.","d":"completely; used to agree strongly","c":"絕對地；完全地","s":"The view from the top of Hehuan Mountain at sunrise was absolutely amazing.","t":"日出時從合歡山頂看出去的景色絕對令人驚豔。"},{"w":"absoluteness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being complete or total","c":"絕對性","s":"The view from the top of Hehuan Mountain at sunrise was absolutely amazing.","t":"日出時從合歡山頂看出去的景色絕對令人驚豔。"},{"w":"abundant","p":"adj.","d":"existing in large amounts; more than enough","c":"豐富的；大量的","s":"Information is abundant online, but good judgement is rare, so students must learn to choose the best sources.","t":"網路上的資訊豐富,但良好的判斷力卻很少見,所以學生必須學會選擇最好的資料來源。"},{"w":"abundance","p":"n.","d":"a very large amount of something","c":"豐富；大量","s":"There is an abundance of fish around the protected reef, so local divers earn more money from tourists than before.","t":"受保護的珊瑚礁周圍有大量的魚,所以當地潛水員從遊客身上賺的錢比以前多。"},{"w":"abundantly","p":"adv.","d":"in large amounts; more than enough","c":"大量地；非常","s":"Rain falls abundantly in northern Taiwan during the winter.","t":"北台灣冬季雨量豐沛。"},{"w":"abuse","p":"v./n.","d":"cruel or violent treatment of a person or animal","c":"虐待；濫用","s":"Drug abuse can cause serious damage to a teenager's brain.","t":"濫用藥物會對青少年的大腦造成嚴重傷害。"},{"w":"abused","p":"adj.","d":"treated cruelly or badly","c":"受虐的","s":"The coach was fired after parents complained about his abusive language toward the players.","t":"教練因家長投訴他對球員出言辱罵而被解雇。"},{"w":"abusive","p":"adj.","d":"using cruel words or violence toward someone","c":"虐待的；辱罵的","s":"The coach was fired after parents complained about his abusive language toward the players.","t":"教練因家長投訴他對球員出言辱罵而被解雇。"},{"w":"abuser","p":"n.","d":"a person who treats someone cruelly","c":"施虐者","s":"The coach was fired after parents complained about his abusive language toward the players.","t":"教練因家長投訴他對球員出言辱罵而被解雇。"},{"w":"accelerate","p":"v.","d":"to go faster; to make something happen sooner","c":"加速","s":"Don't accelerate when the traffic light turns yellow; slow down instead.","t":"黃燈時不要加速，應該減速。"},{"w":"acceleration","p":"n.","d":"the process of going faster","c":"加速；加速度","s":"The acceleration during launch pushed the astronauts back into their seats, and they felt three times heavier than usual.","t":"發射時的加速把太空人壓回座位上，而他們覺得自己比平常重了三倍。"},{"w":"accelerator","p":"n.","d":"a short programme that helps start-ups grow very fast","c":"油門","s":"After joining a three-month accelerator in Singapore, the team improved its app and met many investors.","t":"在加入新加坡一個為期三個月的加速器計畫後，團隊改進了他們的應用程式並結識許多投資人。"},{"w":"access","p":"n./v.","d":"the right or chance to use, enter, or see something","c":"使用權；進入；存取","s":"Students can get free access to the library's online database with their student ID.","t":"學生可以用學生證免費使用圖書館的線上資料庫。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"easy to reach, enter, or use","c":"可取得的；可進入的","s":"AI reading tools make books more accessible to blind students, because the computer can read every page aloud.","t":"人工智慧閱讀工具讓盲人學生更容易取得書籍,因為電腦能把每一頁都朗讀出來。"},{"w":"inaccessible","p":"adj.","d":"impossible or very difficult to reach","c":"無法進入的","s":"After the typhoon, many mountain villages in Hualien became inaccessible because the roads were destroyed.","t":"颱風過後，花蓮許多山區村落因道路損毀而無法進入。"},{"w":"accessibility","p":"n.","d":"how easy something is to reach, use or understand","c":"可及性","s":"The museum improved the accessibility of its website, so blind visitors can now listen to every page with a screen reader.","t":"博物館改善了網站的易用性，所以視障訪客現在能用螢幕閱讀器聆聽每一頁。"},{"w":"accommodate","p":"v.","d":"to provide enough space or rooms for people","c":"容納；提供住宿","s":"The hall can accommodate up to 300 guests.","t":"這個大廳可以容納多達300名賓客。"},{"w":"accommodation","p":"n.","d":"a place to stay or live","c":"住處；膳宿","s":"We booked our accommodation in Kenting three months before the holiday.","t":"我們在假期前三個月就訂好了墾丁的住宿。"},{"w":"accommodating","p":"adj.","d":"willing to help and to do what others ask","c":"樂於助人的；隨和的","s":"Our host in Tainan was very accommodating and even drove us to the train station.","t":"我們在台南的房東非常樂於助人，甚至開車送我們去火車站。"},{"w":"accomplish","p":"v.","d":"to finish something successfully","c":"完成；達成","s":"The village accomplish its goal of using only solar power, and other towns are now asking how they did it.","t":"這個村莊達成了只使用太陽能的目標,其他城鎮現在都在詢問他們是怎麼做到的。"},{"w":"accomplishment","p":"n.","d":"something achieved with effort","c":"成就；完成","s":"Opening a second shop was a great accomplishment for the young couple, and they celebrated with their staff.","t":"開第二家店對這對年輕夫妻來說是一項了不起的成就，而他們和員工一起慶祝。"},{"w":"accomplished","p":"adj.","d":"very skilled at something","c":"有造詣的；熟練的","s":"Working together, the volunteers accomplished their goal of cleaning the whole beach in one morning.","t":"志工們齊心協力，一個早上就達成了把整片海灘清乾淨的目標。"},{"w":"accurate","p":"adj.","d":"correct and exact","c":"準確的","s":"The measurements need to be accurate to ensure the experiment's success.","t":"測量需要準確以確保實驗的成功。"},{"w":"accurately","p":"adv.","d":"in a correct and exact way","c":"準確地","s":"He accurately predicted the outcome of the election.","t":"他準確地預測了選舉的結果。"},{"w":"accuracy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being correct and exact","c":"準確度","s":"In archery, accuracy is more important than strength.","t":"射箭時，準確度比力量重要。"},{"w":"inaccurate","p":"adj.","d":"not correct","c":"不準確的","s":"The weather app is not very reliable; its forecasts are often inaccurate.","t":"這天氣 app 不太可靠，預報常常不準。"},{"w":"achieve","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in doing something after trying hard","c":"達成；實現","s":"To succeed in this field, you must achieve a balance between work and relaxation.","t":"要在這個領域取得成功，您必須實現工作和放鬆之間的平衡。"},{"w":"achievement","p":"n.","d":"something good you succeed in doing after hard work","c":"成就","s":"Winning the medal was a significant achievement for the athlete.","t":"對於運動員來說，獲得這枚獎牌是一個重要的成就。"},{"w":"achievable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to do or reach","c":"可達成的","s":"Set yourself goals that are achievable, like reading one English book a month.","t":"給自己設定可以達成的目標，例如每個月讀一本英文書。"},{"w":"achiever","p":"n.","d":"a person who succeeds in reaching goals","c":"成功者","s":"As a high achiever, Brian gets top grades and also plays on the school volleyball team.","t":"身為表現優異的人，Brian 成績頂尖又是校排球隊員。"},{"w":"acknowledge","p":"v.","d":"to accept or admit that something is true","c":"承認；致謝","s":"It's important to acknowledge one's mistakes and learn from them.","t":"承認自己的錯誤並從中學習是很重要的。"},{"w":"acknowledgment","p":"n.","d":"a message saying that something was received","c":"承認；確認（亦作 acknowledgement）","s":"A: We sent the signed contract to the law firm by express mail on Tuesday, but nobody there has told us whether they received it. B: Let's call their office this morning and ask them to send us a written acknowledgment of receipt, so we have proof that the documents arrived safely.","t":"A：我們星期二用快遞把簽好的合約寄給律師事務所，但那邊還沒有人告訴我們是否收到了。 B：我們今天早上打電話到他們辦公室，請他們寄給我們一份書面的收件【確認】，這樣我們就有文件安全送達的證明。"},{"w":"acknowledged","p":"adj.","d":"generally accepted as true or good","c":"公認的","s":"It is widely acknowledged that enough sleep helps students learn better.","t":"普遍公認充足睡眠能幫助學生學得更好。"},{"w":"actual","p":"adj.","d":"real; existing in fact","c":"實際的；真正的","s":"The actual cost of the school trip turned out to be much higher than the teacher had planned.","t":"校外教學的實際花費結果比老師原先計畫的高很多。"},{"w":"actually","p":"adv.","d":"in fact; really","c":"事實上；其實","s":"Everyone thought the quiet new student was shy, but he was actually just tired from his long trip.","t":"大家以為那位安靜的新同學很害羞，但他其實只是長途旅行後累了。"},{"w":"actuality","p":"n.","d":"the real facts of a situation","c":"現實；實際情況","s":"Everyone thought the quiet new student was shy, but he was actually just tired from his long trip.","t":"大家以為那位安靜的新同學很害羞，但他其實只是長途旅行後累了。"},{"w":"adapt","p":"v.","d":"to change so that you fit a new situation","c":"適應；改編","s":"It took Mei a few months to adapt to life in a new school in Taichung.","t":"小梅花了幾個月才適應台中新學校的生活。"},{"w":"adaptation","p":"n.","d":"a film or play made from a book or story","c":"改編作品；適應","s":"The adaptation of the classic novel into a movie was a huge success.","t":"將經典小說改編成電影是一個巨大的成功。"},{"w":"adaptable","p":"adj.","d":"able to change to suit new situations","c":"適應力強的","s":"Cats are highly adaptable animals that can live in apartments or on farms.","t":"貓是適應力很強的動物，能住在公寓也能住在農場。"},{"w":"add","p":"v.","d":"to put something with another thing to increase the size or amount","c":"增加","s":"Don't forget to add some salt to the soup.","t":"別忘了在湯裡加點鹽。"},{"w":"addition","p":"n.","d":"the process of adding numbers together","c":"增加；附加物","s":"A: My son's teacher says he makes too many careless mistakes on his homework, even though he understands the lessons quite well. B: Maybe he could practice simple addition with real shopping receipts at home, because counting prices from the supermarket often makes math feel more useful and fun for kids.","t":"A：我兒子的老師說他作業上粗心的錯誤太多，雖然他上課內容理解得還不錯。 B：也許他可以在家用真實的購物收據練習簡單的【加法】，因為計算超市的價格常常讓孩子覺得數學更實用、更有趣。"},{"w":"additional","p":"adj.","d":"extra or more","c":"額外的","s":"The factory needed additional power for its new machines, so it installed solar panels on all its roofs.","t":"工廠的新機器需要額外的電力，所以它在所有屋頂上都裝了太陽能板。"},{"w":"additionally","p":"adv.","d":"used to add another point","c":"此外","s":"The library is open late. Additionally, it offers free Wi-Fi.","t":"圖書館開到很晚，此外還提供免費 Wi-Fi。"},{"w":"addict","p":"n.","d":"a person who cannot stop doing or taking something","c":"成癮者","s":"My brother jokes that he is a coffee addict because he cannot start his morning without at least two cups.","t":"我哥哥開玩笑說他是咖啡癮君子，因為他早上至少要喝兩杯才能開始一天。"},{"w":"addicted","p":"adj.","d":"unable to stop doing or using something","c":"上癮的","s":"A: My teenage son spends almost six hours a day on video apps, even during dinner, so do you think I should be worried about his habits? B: Yes, he may be getting addicted to them, so you could set a daily time limit and plan more outdoor activities with him on weekends.","t":"A：我十幾歲的兒子每天花將近六小時在影片應用程式上，連吃晚餐時也一樣，你覺得我該擔心他的習慣嗎？ B：是的，他可能漸漸對它們【上癮】了，所以你可以設定每日使用時間上限，並在週末多安排一些戶外活動陪他。"},{"w":"addiction","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being able to stop doing or taking something","c":"上癮","s":"Internet addiction is becoming a serious problem among teenagers.","t":"網路成癮在青少年中逐漸成為嚴重問題。"},{"w":"addictive","p":"adj.","d":"making you want more and more of it","c":"使人上癮的","s":"Mobile games can be very addictive, so set a time limit.","t":"手機遊戲很容易讓人上癮，所以要設時間限制。"},{"w":"adjust","p":"v.","d":"to change something a little so it works better","c":"調整；適應","s":"Before driving, always adjust the mirrors so you can see the cars behind you.","t":"開車前務必調整後照鏡，才能看到後方車輛。"},{"w":"adjustment","p":"n.","d":"a small change made to improve something","c":"調整","s":"The pilot made a small adjustment to the spacecraft's path, and it entered the moon's orbit perfectly.","t":"駕駛員對太空船的航道做了一個小小的調整，而它完美地進入了月球軌道。"},{"w":"adjustable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed to suit different needs","c":"可調整的","s":"This desk is adjustable, so both short and tall students can use it comfortably.","t":"這張書桌可調整高度，所以高矮的學生都能舒適使用。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"admire – apologize · 15 字族 · 39 題","cards":[{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to respect or approve of someone or their behavior","c":"欽佩；欣賞","s":"Students around the world deeply admire Mother Teresa for her lifelong selfless dedication to the poor.","t":"全世界的學生都深深欽佩德蕾莎修女一生對窮人的無私奉獻。"},{"w":"admiration","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great respect and liking","c":"欽佩","s":"The crowd watched the young pianist with great admiration.","t":"群眾滿懷欽佩地看著那位年輕鋼琴家。"},{"w":"admirable","p":"adj.","d":"deserving respect and praise","c":"令人欽佩的","s":"The way Tina takes care of her sick grandmother is truly admirable.","t":"Tina 照顧生病奶奶的方式真的令人欽佩。"},{"w":"admirer","p":"n.","d":"a person who likes and respects someone very much","c":"仰慕者","s":"The famous writer has thousands of admirers around the world, and many of them wait for hours to get her signature.","t":"這位知名作家在世界各地有成千上萬的欽佩者，許多人等好幾個小時只為了她的簽名。"},{"w":"adventure","p":"n.","d":"an exciting and unusual experience","c":"冒險；奇遇","s":"Our trip to Green Island was a real adventure.","t":"我們的綠島之旅真是一場冒險。"},{"w":"adventurous","p":"adj.","d":"willing to take risks or try out new experiences","c":"愛冒險的","s":"Tom is not very adventurous; he always orders the same food.","t":"湯姆不太愛冒險，他總是點一樣的食物。"},{"w":"adventurer","p":"n.","d":"a person who looks for exciting experiences","c":"冒險家","s":"The young adventurer sailed around the world alone.","t":"那位年輕冒險家獨自環航世界。"},{"w":"adventurously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is brave and willing to try new things","c":"冒險地","s":"Our trip to Green Island was a real adventure.","t":"我們的綠島之旅真是一場冒險。"},{"w":"advise","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone what you think they should do","c":"建議；勸告","s":"The doctor advised him to stop smoking.","t":"醫生勸他戒菸。"},{"w":"advice","p":"n.","d":"an opinion about what someone should do","c":"建議（不可數）","s":"My homeroom teacher gave me some useful advice about choosing a university.","t":"導師給了我一些選大學的實用建議。"},{"w":"adviser","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to give advice","c":"顧問（亦作 advisor）","s":"Before choosing her elective courses, Jenny made an appointment with her school adviser.","t":"選修課程前，珍妮和學校的輔導顧問約了時間。"},{"w":"advisable","p":"adj.","d":"sensible and worth doing","c":"明智的；可取的","s":"It is advisable to see a doctor before starting hard training, especially if you have not exercised for years.","t":"開始激烈訓練前去看醫生是明智的，尤其如果你已經好幾年沒運動。"},{"w":"agent","p":"n.","d":"a person who acts for another person or company","c":"代理人；仲介","s":"A real estate agent showed us three apartments near the school.","t":"一位房仲帶我們看了學校附近的三間公寓。"},{"w":"agency","p":"n.","d":"a business or office that provides a service for people","c":"代理機構","s":"My parents booked our trip to Japan through a travel agency because they did not want to plan every hotel themselves.","t":"我爸媽透過旅行社訂了我們的日本之旅，因為他們不想自己規劃每一家飯店。"},{"w":"agents","p":"n. pl.","d":"people who act or do business for others","c":"代理人","s":"Secret agents in spy movies always have cool gadgets.","t":"間諜電影裡的特務總有很酷的道具。"},{"w":"aim","p":"n./v.","d":"to point or direct a weapon or effort; a purpose or intention","c":"目標；瞄準；以…為目標","s":"Our class's aim this semester is to read ten English novels together.","t":"我們班這學期的目標是一起讀十本英文小說。"},{"w":"aimless","p":"adj.","d":"without a purpose or goal","c":"無目標的","s":"After losing his job, he felt that his life had become aimless and empty.","t":"失業後，他覺得人生變得沒有目標又空虛。"},{"w":"aimlessly","p":"adv.","d":"without a clear purpose or plan","c":"漫無目的地","s":"With no plans for the weekend, Kevin wandered aimlessly around Ximending all afternoon.","t":"週末沒有計畫，Kevin 整個下午在西門町漫無目的地閒晃。"},{"w":"alert","p":"adj./v./n.","d":"watching carefully and ready to notice anything","c":"警覺的；機警的；警告；提醒；警報；警戒","s":"The whole city was on high alert after the earthquake warning.","t":"地震警報後，整座城市進入高度戒備。"},{"w":"alertness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being quick to notice things","c":"警覺性","s":"Drinking coffee can increase your alertness in the morning, but too much may keep you up at night.","t":"喝咖啡可以提高早上的警覺性，但喝太多可能讓你晚上睡不著。"},{"w":"allergy","p":"n.","d":"a medical condition in which the body reacts badly to something","c":"過敏","s":"My allergy to cat hair makes my eyes red and itchy.","t":"我對貓毛過敏，眼睛會又紅又癢。"},{"w":"allergic","p":"adj.","d":"having a bad physical reaction to a food, animal, or substance","c":"過敏的","s":"My brother is so allergic to shrimp that he can't eat at seafood restaurants.","t":"我哥哥對蝦子嚴重過敏，不能去海鮮餐廳吃飯。"},{"w":"alternate","p":"v./adj.","d":"happening in turns; every other","c":"輪流；交替的","s":"We take turns cleaning the room on alternate days.","t":"我們隔天輪流打掃房間。"},{"w":"alternative","p":"n./adj.","d":"something you can choose instead of another thing","c":"替代方案；替代的","s":"If the MRT is too crowded, an alternative way to get to school is by YouBike.","t":"如果捷運太擠，另一個去學校的方式是騎 YouBike。"},{"w":"alternatively","p":"adv.","d":"used to suggest another choice","c":"或者","s":"You can take the train; alternatively, you can drive if you leave early.","t":"你可以搭火車；或者，如果早點出發也可以開車。"},{"w":"alternately","p":"adv.","d":"one after the other, again and again","c":"輪流地","s":"The twins alternately walk the dog every morning; one day it's Mia, the next day it's Max.","t":"雙胞胎每天早上輪流遛狗，一天是 Mia，隔天是 Max。"},{"w":"amaze","p":"v.","d":"to surprise someone very much","c":"使驚奇","s":"The total solar eclipse amazed millions of people around the world.","t":"全日食令世界各地的數百萬人感到驚奇。"},{"w":"amazed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or showing great surprise or wonder","c":"（人）感到驚奇的","s":"We were amazed at how quickly the robot solved the Rubik's Cube.","t":"我們對機器人解魔術方塊的速度感到驚奇。"},{"w":"amazing","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising, especially in a way you like or admire","c":"令人驚奇的","s":"The progress in AI development is amazing!","t":"人工智能發展的進步令人驚嘆！"},{"w":"amazement","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great surprise or wonder (uncountable)","c":"驚奇","s":"Oliver looked up at the towering Eiffel Tower in Paris with a look of pure amazement on his face.","t":"奧利佛臉上帶著純粹驚奇讚嘆的神情仰望著巴黎高聳的艾菲爾鐵塔。"},{"w":"amazingly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very surprising way","c":"驚人地","s":"The old temple has been amazingly well preserved after three hundred years.","t":"這座古廟三百年後仍保存得驚人地完好。"},{"w":"amuse","p":"v.","d":"to make someone laugh or smile","c":"逗樂","s":"My little brother tried to amuse the baby by making funny faces, and soon the whole family was laughing too.","t":"我弟弟做鬼臉想逗寶寶笑，很快全家人也都笑了。"},{"w":"amusement","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being entertained or made to laugh","c":"娛樂；樂趣","s":"We spent the whole day at an amusement park in Taichung.","t":"我們在台中的遊樂園玩了一整天。"},{"w":"amused","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you think something is funny","c":"被逗樂的","s":"The clown's tricks amused the children at the birthday party.","t":"小丑的把戲逗樂了生日派對上的孩子。"},{"w":"amusing","p":"adj.","d":"funny and enjoyable","c":"有趣的","s":"Grandma told us an amusing story about her school days.","t":"奶奶講了一個她求學時的趣事。"},{"w":"analyze","p":"v.","d":"to study something carefully in order to understand it","c":"分析","s":"After examining the data, he needs to analyze the results for trends.","t":"在檢查資料後，他需要分析趨勢結果。"},{"w":"analysis","p":"n.","d":"a careful study of something to understand it","c":"分析","s":"His analysis of the novel was insightful and thorough.","t":"他對小說的分析既有洞見又全面。"},{"w":"analyst","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to study information carefully and explain it","c":"分析師","s":"My brother works as a data analyst at a bank.","t":"我哥哥在銀行擔任資料分析師。"},{"w":"analytical","p":"adj.","d":"using careful thinking to study or understand something","c":"分析的","s":"Math helps students develop analytical thinking skills.","t":"數學幫助學生發展分析思考的能力。"},{"w":"announce","p":"v.","d":"to make a public or formal declaration about a fact, event, or intention","c":"宣布","s":"The school principal was very pleased to announce that our baseball team had won the national championship.","t":"校長非常高興地宣布，我們學校的棒球隊贏得了全國冠軍。"},{"w":"announcement","p":"n.","d":"a public or formal statement about a fact, occurrence, or intention","c":"宣布；公告","s":"Please listen carefully to the announcement about the fire drill this morning.","t":"請仔細聆聽今早關於消防演習的公告。"},{"w":"announcer","p":"n.","d":"a person who reads news or gives information on radio or TV","c":"播報員","s":"The announcer at the train station said our train would be twenty minutes late.","t":"火車站的廣播員說我們的火車會誤點二十分鐘。"},{"w":"anticipate","p":"v.","d":"to expect that something will happen","c":"預期；期待","s":"We didn't anticipate so many visitors, so the food ran out in an hour.","t":"我們沒預料到會來這麼多訪客，所以食物一小時就沒了。"},{"w":"anticipation","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of excitement about something that will happen","c":"期待；預期","s":"The anticipation for the new product release is building up.","t":"新產品發布的預期正在積聚。"},{"w":"anticipated","p":"adj.","d":"expected","c":"備受期待的","s":"The most anticipated movie of the summer finally hit theaters on Friday.","t":"今夏最受期待的電影終於在週五上映。"},{"w":"anxious","p":"adj.","d":"feeling worried or nervous","c":"焦慮的；渴望的","s":"Lily was so anxious about her test results that she couldn't sleep.","t":"莉莉非常擔心考試成績，以致睡不著。"},{"w":"anxiety","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry or fear about what may happen","c":"焦慮","s":"Talking to a counselor can help students reduce exam anxiety.","t":"和輔導老師談話可幫助學生減輕考試焦慮。"},{"w":"anxiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a worried way","c":"焦慮地","s":"The parents waited anxiously outside the operating room for news.","t":"父母在手術室外焦急地等待消息。"},{"w":"anxieties","p":"n. pl.","d":"worries or things that make you nervous","c":"憂慮之事","s":"Lily was so anxious about her test results that she couldn't sleep.","t":"莉莉非常擔心考試成績，以致睡不著。"},{"w":"apologize","p":"v.","d":"to express regret for something that one has done wrong","c":"道歉","s":"The polite young gentleman walked over to apologize sincerely to the lady for spilling cold tea on her coat.","t":"這位有禮貌的年輕紳士走上前去，真誠地向那位女士道歉，因為他不小心把冰茶潑到了她的外套上。"},{"w":"apology","p":"n.","d":"words that say you are sorry for something you did","c":"道歉","s":"The restaurant manager offered us an apology and a free dessert after we waited forty minutes for our food.","t":"我們等了四十分鐘才上菜之後，餐廳經理向我們道歉並送了免費甜點。"},{"w":"apologetic","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you are sorry about something","c":"表示歉意的","s":"The bus driver gave the waiting passengers an apologetic smile for being late.","t":"公車司機因遲到對等候的乘客露出抱歉的微笑。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"appeal – average · 15 字族 · 36 題","cards":[{"w":"appeal","p":"v./n.","d":"to attract or interest; to ask a higher court to change a decision","c":"吸引；呼籲；吸引力","s":"The game's simple design appeals to people of all ages.","t":"這款遊戲的簡單設計吸引各年齡層的人。"},{"w":"appealing","p":"adj.","d":"attractive or interesting","c":"吸引人的","s":"The idea of a long weekend at the beach is very appealing.","t":"在海邊度過長週末的想法非常吸引人。"},{"w":"appear","p":"v.","d":"to become visible or come into sight","c":"出現；似乎","s":"A bright rainbow began to appear in the sky after the rain stopped.","t":"雨停後，天空開始出現一道明亮的彩虹。"},{"w":"appearance","p":"n.","d":"the act of arriving or being seen; the way someone looks","c":"外表；出現","s":"Never judge people by their appearance; a quiet classmate may be the kindest person you know.","t":"別以貌取人；一個安靜的同學可能是你認識最善良的人。"},{"w":"disappear","p":"v.","d":"to cease to be visible; to vanish from sight","c":"消失","s":"The huge ship sailed slowly toward the distant horizon, and it finally seemed to disappear completely into the thick coastal fog.","t":"那艘巨大的輪船緩緩駛向遠方的地平線，最後似乎完全【消失】在濃厚的沿海霧氣之中。"},{"w":"disappearance","p":"n.","d":"an unexpected event in which someone or something vanishes completely","c":"消失","s":"Police investigators conducted a thorough study to solve the mysterious disappearance of the wealthy business executive.","t":"警方調查人員展開了一項徹底的研究，以解決這位富有企業高階主管的神秘失蹤案。"},{"w":"apply","p":"v.","d":"to ask officially for a job, a place, etc.","c":"申請；塗抹；應用","s":"You should apply sunscreen every two hours at the beach.","t":"在海邊你應該每兩小時擦一次防曬乳。"},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a written request for a job, a place at a school, etc.","c":"申請（書）；應用","s":"Please send your application before the end of March.","t":"請在三月底前寄出你的申請書。"},{"w":"applicant","p":"n.","d":"a person who asks for a job, a place at a school, etc.","c":"申請人","s":"More than two hundred applicants applied for only five jobs.","t":"超過兩百名應徵者應徵僅五個職缺。"},{"w":"appoint","p":"v.","d":"to choose someone for a job or position","c":"任命；約定","s":"The board will appoint a new chief executive next month, and many people expect it to be a woman.","t":"董事會將在下個月任命一位新執行長，而許多人預期會是一位女性。"},{"w":"appointment","p":"n.","d":"an arranged time to meet a doctor or other person","c":"約會；預約；任命","s":"I made an appointment with the dentist online, so I did not have to wait in line at the clinic.","t":"我在網路上和牙醫預約了時間,所以不必在診所排隊等候。"},{"w":"appointed","p":"adj.","d":"chosen officially for a job; (of a time) agreed in advance","c":"指定的","s":"Ms. Chen was appointed as the new principal of our school.","t":"陳女士被任命為我們學校的新校長。"},{"w":"approach","p":"v./n.","d":"a way of doing or dealing with something","c":"接近；方法","s":"The new approach to teaching has received mixed feedback.","t":"新的教學方法收到了不同的回饋。"},{"w":"approachable","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and incredibly easy to talk to in person.","c":"平易近人的","s":"Students love Ms. Lee because she is friendly and approachable.","t":"學生們喜歡李老師，因為她友善又平易近人。"},{"w":"approaching","p":"adj.","d":"coming closer in space or time; happening very soon","c":"即將到來的","s":"With the approaching exam, the library was full of students every evening.","t":"隨著考試即將來臨，圖書館每晚都擠滿學生。"},{"w":"architect","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to design buildings","c":"建築師","s":"Taipei 101 was designed by a Taiwanese architect named C.Y. Lee.","t":"台北101是由一位名叫李祖原的台灣建築師設計的。"},{"w":"architecture","p":"n.","d":"the art of designing buildings; the style of a building","c":"建築；建築學","s":"Tainan is full of old temples and Japanese-era houses, so visitors who love architecture can spend days exploring the city.","t":"台南到處都是古老廟宇和日治時期的房子，所以喜愛建築的遊客可以花好幾天探索這座城市。"},{"w":"architectural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the design of buildings","c":"建築的","s":"The old red-brick buildings in Dadaocheng show an interesting mix of Western and Chinese architectural styles.","t":"大稻埕的老紅磚建築呈現中西建築風格的有趣融合。"},{"w":"arrange","p":"v.","d":"to plan, prepare, or organize something in advance","c":"安排；排列","s":"Our school counselor will gladly arrange a private face-to-face consultation for parents who need advice on university admissions.","t":"我們的學校輔導老師會很樂意為需要大學入學建議的家長安排私人的面對面諮詢。"},{"w":"arrangement","p":"n.","d":"an agreement about how something will be done","c":"安排；布置","s":"The two shops have an arrangement to share delivery drivers, so both of them save money every month.","t":"兩家店有一項共用送貨司機的協議，所以雙方每個月都能省錢。"},{"w":"arranged","p":"adj.","d":"planned or organized beforehand","c":"安排好的","s":"The flower shop owner arranged the roses and lilies beautifully in a glass vase.","t":"花店老闆把玫瑰和百合漂亮地插在玻璃花瓶裡。"},{"w":"arrest","p":"v./n.","d":"to stop something from continuing; to catch attention","c":"逮捕","s":"The police are ready to arrest the man as soon as he leaves the building.","t":"那名男子一離開大樓，警方就準備逮捕他。"},{"w":"arrested","p":"adj.","d":"taken away by the police","c":"被逮捕的","s":"Two students were among the people arrested at the protest.","t":"在抗議活動中被捕的人當中有兩名學生。"},{"w":"arresting","p":"adj.","d":"very interesting or attractive; catching attention","c":"引人注目的","s":"The police are ready to arrest the man as soon as he leaves the building.","t":"那名男子一離開大樓，警方就準備逮捕他。"},{"w":"assign","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a job or task to do","c":"分派；指派","s":"The project manager will assign tasks to each team member based on their expertise and availability.","t":"項目經理將根據每個團隊成員的專業知識和可用性分配任務。"},{"w":"assignment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work given to someone","c":"作業；任務","s":"The assignment required a deep understanding of the subject matter and collaboration among team members.","t":"任務要求對主題內容有深刻的理解並需要團隊成員之間的合作。"},{"w":"assigned","p":"adj.","d":"given as a job or task","c":"被指派的","s":"The teacher assigned each group a different country to research.","t":"老師分派給每一組一個不同的國家去研究。"},{"w":"assist","p":"v.","d":"to help someone","c":"協助","s":"Can you assist me with this task?","t":"你能協助我完成這項任務嗎？"},{"w":"assistance","p":"n.","d":"help or support","c":"協助","s":"If you need any assistance finding a book, please ask the librarian at the front desk.","t":"如果你需要協助找書，請洽前台的圖書館員。"},{"w":"assistant","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps someone in a higher position with their work","c":"助理","s":"The general manager hired a bilingual assistant to organize business meetings, reply to client emails, and book flight tickets.","t":"總經理僱用了一位雙語助手來安排商務會議、回覆客戶電子郵件以及訂購機票。"},{"w":"associate","p":"v.","d":"to connect one thing with another in your mind","c":"聯想；把…聯繫在一起","s":"Many people associate the smell of rice dumplings with the Dragon Boat Festival.","t":"很多人一聞到粽子香就會聯想到端午節。"},{"w":"associated","p":"adj.","d":"connected with something","c":"有關聯的","s":"Many people associate the smell of rice dumplings with the Dragon Boat Festival.","t":"很多人一聞到粽子香就會聯想到端午節。"},{"w":"association","p":"n.","d":"a connection between two things","c":"聯想；協會","s":"The Taiwan Badminton Association held a training camp for young players this summer.","t":"中華民國羽球協會今年夏天為年輕選手舉辦了訓練營。"},{"w":"astonish","p":"v.","d":"to surprise someone very much","c":"使驚訝","s":"The young girl's paintings astonish the judges, because nobody expected such skill from a ten-year-old.","t":"這位小女孩的畫作讓評審大為驚訝,因為沒人預料到一個十歲孩子有如此技巧。"},{"w":"astonished","p":"adj.","d":"very surprised","c":"（人）感到驚訝的","s":"We were astonished to learn that the tiny shop had been selling beef noodles for over sixty years.","t":"得知那家小店已經賣了六十多年的牛肉麵，我們很驚訝。"},{"w":"astonishing","p":"adj.","d":"very surprising","c":"令人驚訝的","s":"The magician's final trick was so astonishing that the whole audience stood up and clapped.","t":"魔術師最後的把戲太驚人了，全場觀眾都起立鼓掌。"},{"w":"astonishment","p":"n.","d":"very great surprise","c":"驚訝","s":"To the astonishment of her parents, the five-year-old girl read the whole newspaper article aloud without a single mistake.","t":"令父母驚訝的是，那個五歲的女孩把整篇報紙文章大聲唸完，一個錯都沒有。"},{"w":"attract","p":"v.","d":"to make someone or something come near or be interested","c":"吸引","s":"The light attracted hundreds of insects.","t":"燈光吸引了數百隻昆蟲。"},{"w":"attraction","p":"n.","d":"an interesting place that people visit","c":"吸引力；景點","s":"The attraction between the Earth and the moon causes ocean tides, so fishermen pay close attention to the moon's phases.","t":"地球和月球之間的吸引力造成海洋潮汐，所以漁民非常注意月亮的盈虧。"},{"w":"attractive","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant to look at; interesting enough to want","c":"有吸引力的","s":"Her attractive smile and friendly personality made her instantly likable to everyone she met.","t":"她迷人的微笑和友好的個性使她在遇到的每個人中都受歡迎。"},{"w":"unattractive","p":"adj.","d":"not pleasant to look at","c":"沒有吸引力的","s":"The old park looked dull and unattractive until volunteers painted colorful murals on its walls.","t":"在志工於牆上畫上彩色壁畫之前，這座舊公園看起來單調又不吸引人。"},{"w":"automatic","p":"adj.","d":"working by itself","c":"自動的","s":"The automatic doors opened as we approached the building.","t":"當我們走近大廈時，自動門打開了。"},{"w":"automatically","p":"adv.","d":"by itself, without a person","c":"自動地","s":"The system automatically updates to ensure optimal performance.","t":"系統自動更新以確保最佳性能。"},{"w":"automate","p":"v.","d":"to make a machine or computer do a job without people","c":"使自動化","s":"Many banks now automate simple customer questions with smart software, so staff can spend more time on difficult problems.","t":"許多銀行現在用智慧軟體將簡單的顧客問題自動化,因此員工能花更多時間處理困難的問題。"},{"w":"automation","p":"n.","d":"the use of machines and computers to do work","c":"自動化","s":"Robots and automation have replaced many jobs in factories.","t":"機器人與自動化已取代工廠裡的許多工作。"},{"w":"average","p":"n./adj./v.","d":"the usual amount, found by adding and dividing","c":"平均數；平均的；一般的；平均為…","s":"My grades this semester were above average, but I still want to do better.","t":"我這學期的成績高於平均，但我還是想做得更好。"},{"w":"on average","p":"phr.","d":"usually; as a normal amount","c":"平均而言","s":"_____ _____, students in our class spend about two hours on homework every night, but some spend much more time.","t":""}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"awake – captive · 15 字族 · 37 題","cards":[{"w":"awake","p":"adj./v.","d":"not sleeping","c":"醒著的；醒來（awoke, awoken）","s":"Coffee helps me stay awake during long study nights before exams.","t":"考前熬夜念書時，咖啡幫助我保持清醒。"},{"w":"awaken","p":"v.","d":"to wake up; to make someone feel something for the first time","c":"喚醒；喚起","s":"The trip to the mountains helped awaken my interest in birds, and now I carry a small guidebook everywhere I go.","t":"那趟山區之旅喚醒了我對鳥類的興趣，現在我走到哪裡都帶著一本小圖鑑。"},{"w":"awakening","p":"n.","d":"the moment when you suddenly understand something","c":"覺醒；醒悟","s":"Failing the first math test was a rude awakening for Leo, who had thought high school would be easy.","t":"第一次數學考試不及格讓原以為高中很輕鬆的 Leo 猛然醒悟。"},{"w":"aware","p":"adj.","d":"knowing that something exists or is happening","c":"知道的；察覺的","s":"Are you aware that the MRT station will close early tonight?","t":"你知道捷運站今晚會提早關閉嗎？。"},{"w":"unaware","p":"adj.","d":"not knowing about something","c":"不知道的；未察覺的","s":"Ellen was unaware of the bus coming toward her because she was looking at her phone.","t":"Ellen 因為在看手機，沒注意到公車朝她開過來。"},{"w":"awareness","p":"n.","d":"knowledge or understanding of something","c":"意識；認識","s":"The campaign is meant to raise awareness of the dangers of texting while walking across busy streets.","t":"這項活動旨在提高大家對穿越繁忙街道時傳訊息之危險的意識。"},{"w":"ban","p":"v./n.","d":"to officially say that something is not allowed","c":"禁止；禁令","s":"The city put a ban on plastic straws last year.","t":"該市去年對塑膠吸管頒布禁令。"},{"w":"banned","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed by law or rule","c":"被禁止的","s":"Smoking is banned in all public buildings in Taiwan.","t":"台灣所有公共建築內都禁止吸菸。"},{"w":"bare","p":"adj.","d":"without clothes, coverage, or any decorations.","c":"赤裸的；光秃的","s":"The walls of the new apartment were completely bare, so they decided to hang some paintings to make it feel warmer.","t":"新公寓的牆壁完全空無一物，所以他們決定掛一些畫作讓空間感覺更溫馨。"},{"w":"barely","p":"adv.","d":"only just; almost not","c":"幾乎不；勉強","s":"We had barely enough time to catch the last train home.","t":"我們的時間勉強夠趕上回家的末班車。"},{"w":"barefoot","p":"adj./adv.","d":"without shoes or socks","c":"赤腳的／地","s":"The kids ran barefoot along the beach, leaving footprints in the sand.","t":"孩子們赤腳沿著沙灘奔跑，在沙上留下腳印。"},{"w":"behave","p":"v.","d":"to act in a certain way","c":"表現；守規矩","s":"Children are expected to behave well in public places.","t":"人們希望孩子們在公共場所表現得很好。"},{"w":"behavior","p":"n.","d":"the way a person or animal acts","c":"行為；舉止（英式 behaviour）","s":"The teacher praised the class for their good behavior during the field trip.","t":"老師稱讚全班在校外教學時表現良好。"},{"w":"misbehave","p":"v.","d":"to act badly","c":"行為不端；不守規矩","s":"Students who misbehave in class will have to stay after school.","t":"上課不守規矩的學生放學後必須留下來。"},{"w":"benefit","p":"n./v.","d":"to be good or helpful for someone","c":"好處；有益於","s":"The extra tutoring benefit many students who struggle to learn a foreign language.","t":"額外的輔導造福許多在學習外語方面遇到困難的學生。"},{"w":"beneficial","p":"adj.","d":"having a good or helpful effect","c":"有益的","s":"It's beneficial to take breaks when studying for long periods.","t":"長時間學習時，休息是有益的。"},{"w":"benefits","p":"n.","d":"good results or advantages","c":"好處（複數）","s":"Getting enough sleep has many benefits for students' memory.","t":"充足睡眠對學生的記憶力有很多好處。"},{"w":"bless","p":"v.","d":"(of God) to give good things to someone","c":"祝福；保佑","s":"May God bless you with happiness.","t":"願上帝賜福你幸福。"},{"w":"blessing","p":"n.","d":"something good that you are lucky to have; God's help","c":"祝福；幸事","s":"Having a warm house and enough food every day is a blessing that many people in the world do not enjoy.","t":"每天有溫暖的家和足夠的食物是一種福氣，世界上許多人並沒有享有。"},{"w":"blessed","p":"adj.","d":"lucky; having good things in your life","c":"幸運的；受祝福的","s":"Grandma blessed each of us before we left for our trip abroad.","t":"我們出國旅行前，奶奶為我們每個人祝福。"},{"w":"brave","p":"adj.","d":"not afraid to do hard or dangerous things","c":"勇敢的","s":"Q: What do you think of Ben? — A: He is brave because he often helps people in trouble.","t":"你覺得班怎麼樣？ — 他很勇敢，因為他常常幫助有麻煩的人。"},{"w":"bravely","p":"adv.","d":"in a brave way, without fear","c":"勇敢地","s":"The firefighters fought the fire bravely for six hours.","t":"消防員英勇地與火搏鬥了六小時。"},{"w":"bravery","p":"n.","d":"courageous behavior or character; the quality of being brave","c":"勇敢","s":"The soldier received a medal for his bravery.","t":"那位士兵因英勇獲頒勳章。"},{"w":"braver","p":"adj.","d":"more brave","c":"更勇敢的","s":"My little sister is braver than me; she isn't afraid of the dark.","t":"我妹妹比我更勇敢，她不怕黑。"},{"w":"breathe","p":"v.","d":"to take air into your lungs and let it out","c":"呼吸","s":"The air in the city was so polluted that it was hard to breathe.","t":"城市的空氣污染嚴重到很難呼吸。"},{"w":"breath","p":"n.","d":"the air you take into and let out of your lungs","c":"呼吸；氣息","s":"Take a deep breath and count to ten before you answer an angry customer.","t":"回應生氣的顧客前，先深吸一口氣並數到十。"},{"w":"breathless","p":"adj.","d":"having difficulty breathing, often after running","c":"上氣不接下氣的","s":"After running up ten floors of stairs, Andy was completely breathless.","t":"爬了十層樓梯後，Andy 完全上氣不接下氣。"},{"w":"breathing","p":"n.","d":"the action of taking air into and out of the lungs","c":"呼吸（作用）","s":"A: What did you learn in your first lesson at the singing studio near the train station on Saturday morning? B: The teacher did not let us sing at all, and instead we spent the whole hour practicing deep breathing from the stomach, because she said it controls everything about the voice.","t":"A：你週六早上在火車站附近的歌唱教室上第一堂課學到了什麼？ B：老師完全沒讓我們唱歌，而是整整一個小時練習從腹部深【呼吸】，因為她說這控制著聲音的一切。"},{"w":"broad","p":"adj.","d":"wide in extent from side to side; spacious","c":"寬廣的","s":"The new road through the village is twice as broad as the old one.","t":"穿過村子的新路比舊路寬兩倍。"},{"w":"broaden","p":"v.","d":"to make something wider or to include more things","c":"拓寬","s":"The city plans to broaden the narrow road near the hospital, so ambulances can reach it more quickly.","t":"市政府計畫拓寬醫院附近的狹窄道路，好讓救護車能更快抵達。"},{"w":"breadth","p":"n.","d":"the distance from one side of something to the other; width","c":"寬度；廣度","s":"The teacher was impressed by the breadth of Kelly's knowledge about world history.","t":"老師對 Kelly 世界史知識之廣感到印象深刻。"},{"w":"broadly","p":"adv.","d":"in general, without considering details","c":"大致上","s":"Broadly speaking, students in Taiwan spend more hours at school than students in Europe.","t":"大致來說，台灣學生在校時間比歐洲學生長。"},{"w":"bruise","p":"n./v.","d":"a dark mark on the skin caused by a hit or a fall","c":"瘀青；使瘀傷","s":"After the basketball game, Kevin found a large bruise on his leg.","t":"籃球比賽後，凱文發現腿上有一大塊瘀青。"},{"w":"bruised","p":"adj.","d":"having bruises","c":"瘀傷的；碰傷的","s":"The bruised apples were sold at half price at the market.","t":"市場上那些碰傷的蘋果以半價出售。"},{"w":"bruises","p":"n.","d":"dark marks on the skin after being hit","c":"瘀青（複數）","s":"His arms were covered in bruises after he fell down the stairs.","t":"他跌下樓梯後雙臂佈滿瘀青。"},{"w":"bully","p":"v./n.","d":"a person who hurts or frightens weaker people","c":"霸凌；惡霸","s":"Nobody liked the big kid in our class because he was a bully who took other kids' snacks.","t":"沒人喜歡班上那個大塊頭，因為他是會搶別人點心的惡霸。"},{"w":"bullying","p":"n.","d":"the act of hurting or frightening weaker people","c":"霸凌行為","s":"The older boys were caught bullying a first-year student behind the gym.","t":"高年級男生被抓到在體育館後面霸凌一年級學生。"},{"w":"bullied","p":"adj.","d":"hurt or frightened by someone stronger again and again","c":"被霸凌的","s":"If you are being bullied online, save the messages and tell an adult you trust.","t":"如果你在網路上被霸凌，把訊息保存下來並告訴信任的大人。"},{"w":"bustle","p":"n./v.","d":"busy, noisy movement of many people","c":"喧鬧；忙亂","s":"I love the noise and bustle of the night market on Friday evenings.","t":"我喜歡星期五晚上夜市的喧鬧熱絡。"},{"w":"bustling","p":"adj.","d":"full of busy, noisy activity","c":"熙熙攘攘的；熱鬧的","s":"Dihua Street is bustling before Lunar New Year, and shoppers squeeze past each other to buy dried fruit and candy.","t":"迪化街在農曆新年前熙熙攘攘，購物者擠來擠去購買果乾和糖果。"},{"w":"capable","p":"adj.","d":"having the ability to do something","c":"有能力的","s":"Don't worry about the project; Amy is a very capable leader.","t":"別擔心這個專案；艾咪是位很能幹的領導者。"},{"w":"capability","p":"n.","d":"the ability or power to do something","c":"能力","s":"His capability to solve complex problems quickly impressed his supervisors.","t":"他快速解決複雜問題的能力給他的主管留下了深刻的印象。"},{"w":"incapable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to do something","c":"無能力的","s":"Without his glasses, my grandfather is incapable of reading even large print.","t":"沒戴眼鏡時，我爺爺連大字都看不了。"},{"w":"captive","p":"adj./n.","d":"a person or animal that is kept somewhere and not allowed to leave","c":"被俘的；俘虜","s":"The hostages were held captive on the boat for three days.","t":"人質被扣留在船上三天。"},{"w":"captivity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being kept in a place and not allowed to leave","c":"囚禁；圈養","s":"Dolphins in captivity often show signs of boredom, because a small pool is very different from the open ocean.","t":"圈養中的海豚常常出現無聊的跡象，因為小水池和廣闊的海洋非常不同。"},{"w":"capture","p":"v.","d":"to catch an animal or person","c":"捕獲","s":"The team used soft nets to capture the birds, and they released them after putting small rings on their legs.","t":"研究團隊用柔軟的網子捕捉鳥類，並在牠們腳上套上小環後把牠們放走。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"cast – commute · 15 字族 · 38 題","cards":[{"w":"cast","p":"n./v.","d":"all the actors in a film or play; a hard cover for a broken bone","c":"演員陣容；投射（三態同形）","s":"When the teacher asked who had broken the window, everyone cast a glance at Tom.","t":"老師問誰打破窗戶時，大家都朝湯姆看了一眼。"},{"w":"casting","p":"n.","d":"choosing actors for a film or play","c":"選角","s":"The director spent months casting the leading role before choosing an unknown actress.","t":"導演花了好幾個月為主角選角，最後選了一位沒沒無聞的女演員。"},{"w":"broadcast","p":"v./n.","d":"to transmit programs on television or radio","c":"廣播；播出","s":"The national television station will broadcast the exciting international baseball championship live from Tokyo tonight.","t":"國家電視台今晚將從東京現場實況轉播激動人心的國際棒球錦標賽。"},{"w":"forecast","p":"n./v.","d":"a statement about what will probably happen, especially the weather","c":"預報","s":"The bank forecast that online payments would keep growing, so it closed several branches and opened a new app.","t":"這家銀行預測線上付款會持續成長,所以關閉了幾家分行並推出新的應用程式。"},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to show that an event or person is important","c":"慶祝","s":"The festival aims to celebrate local artists, so all the paintings on show were made by people from the village.","t":"這個藝術節旨在頌揚在地藝術家,所以所有展出的畫作都是村民創作的。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a party or special event for an important day","c":"慶祝（活動）","s":"The celebration of my grandparents' fiftieth wedding anniversary was held in a big restaurant, and over a hundred relatives came.","t":"我爺爺奶奶金婚五十週年的慶祝活動在一家大餐廳舉行，來了一百多位親戚。"},{"w":"celebrated","p":"adj.","d":"famous and praised by many people","c":"著名的","s":"Last night, the whole team celebrated their victory with hot pot.","t":"昨晚全隊吃火鍋慶祝勝利。"},{"w":"challenge","p":"n./v.","d":"to test someone's ability; to question something","c":"挑戰","s":"Learning a new language is a big challenge, but it opens many doors.","t":"學新語言是很大的挑戰，但能打開許多扇門。"},{"w":"challenging","p":"adj.","d":"tough but highly interesting; demanding hard work.","c":"有挑戰性的","s":"Climbing Jade Mountain is challenging, but the view from the top is worth it.","t":"爬玉山很有挑戰性，但山頂的景色很值得。"},{"w":"challenged","p":"adj.","d":"having a disability or difficulty","c":"有障礙的","s":"Climbing Jade Mountain is challenging, but the view from the top is worth it.","t":"爬玉山很有挑戰性，但山頂的景色很值得。"},{"w":"challenger","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that tries to win against the leader or champion","c":"挑戰者","s":"The young challenger surprised everyone by beating the world champion.","t":"那位年輕挑戰者擊敗世界冠軍，讓所有人驚訝。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"a person in a story or movie","c":"性格；角色；字","s":"Harry Potter is my favorite character in all the books I've ever read.","t":"哈利波特是我讀過所有書中最喜歡的角色。"},{"w":"characteristic","p":"n./adj.","d":"a typical quality or feature of a person or thing","c":"特徵；特有的","s":"One characteristic of Mars is its red dust, and this colour comes from rusty iron in the soil.","t":"火星的一個特徵是它的紅色塵土，而這種顏色來自土壤中生鏽的鐵。"},{"w":"characterize","p":"v.","d":"to describe the typical qualities of something; to be typical of","c":"以…為特徵","s":"Friendly people and great street food characterize life in Taiwan, according to many tourists.","t":"很多觀光客認為友善的人和美味小吃是台灣生活的特色。"},{"w":"chase","p":"v./n.","d":"to pursue in order to catch or catch up with","c":"追逐","s":"After a long chase, the police finally caught the thief near Taipei Main Station.","t":"經過一番長時間追捕，警方終於在台北車站附近抓到小偷。"},{"w":"chaser","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that runs after someone","c":"追逐者","s":"The kids chased each other around the playground until it got dark.","t":"孩子們在遊樂場互相追逐直到天黑。"},{"w":"chase after","p":"phr.","d":"to run after someone or something to catch them","c":"追趕","s":"The kids chased each other around the playground until it got dark.","t":"孩子們在遊樂場互相追逐直到天黑。"},{"w":"circulate","p":"v.","d":"to move around freely; to pass from person to person","c":"循環；流傳","s":"Ceiling fans help circulate cool air around the classroom on hot afternoons.","t":"炎熱的下午，吊扇幫助冷空氣在教室裡循環。"},{"w":"circulation","p":"n.","d":"the movement of blood around the body; the movement of air, money, or news","c":"循環；流通","s":"Walking for a few minutes every hour can improve blood circulation in your legs.","t":"每小時走動幾分鐘可以改善腿部的血液循環。"},{"w":"circulatory","p":"adj.","d":"about the movement of blood through the body","c":"循環的","s":"Walking for a few minutes every hour can improve blood circulation in your legs.","t":"每小時走動幾分鐘可以改善腿部的血液循環。"},{"w":"classic","p":"adj./n.","d":"very good and a typical example of its kind","c":"經典的；經典作品","s":"Romeo and Juliet is a classic love story that everyone knows.","t":"《羅密歐與茱麗葉》是人人皆知的經典愛情故事。"},{"w":"classical","p":"adj.","d":"traditional and long-lasting in style","c":"古典的","s":"She enjoys listening to classical music while studying.","t":"她喜歡在學習時聽經典音樂。"},{"w":"classically","p":"adv.","d":"in a traditional or classical way","c":"古典地","s":"The young singer is classically trained but now sings pop music.","t":"那位年輕歌手受過古典訓練，但現在唱流行樂。"},{"w":"code","p":"n./v.","d":"a set of rules; a system of letters, numbers, or signs that carries a message","c":"密碼；規範；編碼","s":"Each product has a unique barcode code for identification.","t":"每個產品都有一個唯一的條碼代碼用於識別。"},{"w":"decode","p":"v.","d":"to find the meaning of a code","c":"解碼","s":"It took the students an hour to decode the secret message.","t":"學生們花了一小時才解開那則密碼訊息。"},{"w":"coding","p":"n.","d":"writing instructions for a computer","c":"程式設計","s":"Our school offers a free coding class where students learn to build apps.","t":"我們學校開設免費的程式設計課，讓學生學做 App。"},{"w":"collaborate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others","c":"合作","s":"Students from Taiwan and Japan collaborated on a project using online tools, and they presented it together on video.","t":"台灣和日本的學生用線上工具合作完成一項專題,並一起用視訊發表。"},{"w":"collaboration","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together to make or do something","c":"合作","s":"The project was a collaboration between scientists from twenty countries, and they shared all their data online.","t":"這個計畫是來自二十個國家科學家之間的合作，而他們在網路上分享所有的資料。"},{"w":"collaborative","p":"adj.","d":"involving people working together","c":"合作的","s":"Our science teacher prefers a collaborative approach, so we always work in groups.","t":"我們的自然老師偏好合作式的方法，所以我們總是分組進行。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"v./n.","d":"to fall down suddenly; to fail completely","c":"倒塌；崩潰","s":"The old bridge was closed after engineers warned that it could collapse at any time.","t":"工程師警告舊橋隨時可能倒塌後，橋就被封閉了。"},{"w":"collapsed","p":"adj.","d":"having fallen down suddenly","c":"倒塌的","s":"After the long race, one runner collapsed at the finish line and was taken to the hospital.","t":"長跑結束後，一名跑者在終點線倒下並被送醫。"},{"w":"collapsible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be folded into a smaller shape","c":"可折疊的","s":"We bought a collapsible table that we can easily take camping.","t":"我們買了一張可以輕鬆帶去露營的折疊桌。"},{"w":"collect","p":"v.","d":"to bring things together from different places, often as a hobby","c":"收集","s":"Over the years, he managed to collect an impressive collection of antique coins from around the world.","t":"多年來，他成功地收集了來自世界各地的令人印象深刻的古代的錢幣收藏品。"},{"w":"collection","p":"n.","d":"a group of objects or art brought together in one place","c":"收藏品；收集","s":"Uncle Robert has built an impressive collection of rare postage stamps from around the world over thirty years.","t":"三十年來，羅伯特叔叔建立了一套令人印象深刻的全球罕見郵票收藏品。"},{"w":"collector","p":"n.","d":"a person who collects things as a hobby or as a job","c":"收藏家","s":"My uncle is a serious stamp collector who owns stamps from over a hundred countries.","t":"我舅舅是認真的集郵家，擁有一百多國的郵票。"},{"w":"collective","p":"adj.","d":"shared by or done by a group of people together","c":"集體的","s":"Climate change needs collective action, so even small efforts by millions of people can make a difference.","t":"氣候變遷需要集體行動,所以即使是數百萬人的小小努力也能帶來改變。"},{"w":"combine","p":"v.","d":"to join two or more things together.","c":"結合","s":"They decided to combine their efforts for the project.","t":"他們決定結合他們的力量來完成這個項目。"},{"w":"combination","p":"n.","d":"two or more things put together; the numbers that open a lock","c":"組合；結合","s":"The combination of flavors created a unique dish.","t":"各種風味的結合創造了一道獨特的菜肴。"},{"w":"combined","p":"adj.","d":"put together; total","c":"結合的；合計的","s":"The combined weight of the two suitcases was over 40 kilograms.","t":"兩個行李箱加起來的重量超過 40 公斤。"},{"w":"commit","p":"v.","d":"to do something wrong or illegal","c":"犯（罪）；承諾","s":"The company has commit one million dollars to save the coral reefs, and its staff will also help clean the beaches.","t":"那家公司已承諾投入一百萬美元拯救珊瑚礁，員工們也會協助清理海灘。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"a promise to do something; strong dedication","c":"承諾；投入","s":"The company made a commitment to use only green electricity, so it signed a long contract with a wind farm.","t":"這家公司承諾只使用綠電,所以它與一座風場簽訂了長期合約。"},{"w":"committed","p":"adj.","d":"willing to work very hard at something","c":"盡心盡力的","s":"Lisa is a committed volunteer who has helped at the animal shelter every weekend for five years.","t":"麗莎是位盡心的志工，五年來每週末都去動物收容所幫忙。"},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information with others","c":"溝通；傳達","s":"The telegraph helped people communicate across countries, so business decisions could be made much faster.","t":"電報幫助人們跨國溝通,所以商業決策能做得快很多。"},{"w":"communication","p":"n.","d":"the act of sharing information, ideas, or feelings with others","c":"溝通；通訊","s":"Good communication between parents and teenagers can prevent many arguments.","t":"父母與青少年之間良好的溝通可以避免許多爭吵。"},{"w":"communicator","p":"n.","d":"a person who shares ideas and information with others, especially one who does it well","c":"溝通者；表達者","s":"Our new team leader is a great communicator; she always explains things clearly.","t":"我們新的組長很會溝通，她總是把事情解釋得很清楚。"},{"w":"communicative","p":"adj.","d":"willing to talk and share information with people","c":"愛說話的；溝通的","s":"The new student was shy at first, but she became much more communicative after she joined the drama club.","t":"這位新生起初很害羞，但加入戲劇社之後，她變得健談多了。"},{"w":"commute","p":"v./n.","d":"to travel regularly between home and work or school","c":"通勤；通勤（路程）","s":"My daily commute to school takes about forty minutes.","t":"我每天上學的通勤時間約四十分鐘。"},{"w":"commuter","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels regularly to and from work","c":"通勤者","s":"My father is a daily commuter who takes the 7:15 train into the city, and he reads the news on his phone during the trip.","t":"我爸爸是每天搭7點15分火車進城的通勤者,而他在車程中用手機看新聞。"},{"w":"commuting","p":"n.","d":"the activity of traveling regularly between one's place of residence and place of work or study","c":"通勤","s":"Relying on public transit can significantly minimize the overall stress of daily commuting during the busy morning rush hour.","t":"在 busy morning rush hour 時段，依賴大眾運輸工具可以顯著減少每日通勤的整體壓力。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"company – consequence · 15 字族 · 35 題","cards":[{"w":"company","p":"n.","d":"a business","c":"陪伴；公司","s":"He works for a company that specializes in renewable energy.","t":"他在一家專門從事可再生能源的公司工作。"},{"w":"accompany","p":"v.","d":"to go somewhere with someone","c":"陪伴；伴隨","s":"He offered to accompany her to the doctor's appointment.","t":"他提議陪她去看醫生。"},{"w":"companion","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal you spend a lot of time with","c":"同伴","s":"My dog has been my faithful companion for over ten years.","t":"我的狗十多年來一直是我忠實的夥伴。"},{"w":"compare","p":"v.","d":"to look at how things are alike or different","c":"比較；比喻","s":"It's difficult to compare the two products as they serve different purposes.","t":"由於這兩種產品具有不同的用途，因此很難將它們進行比較。"},{"w":"comparison","p":"n.","d":"the act of comparing two or more things","c":"比較","s":"In comparison with last year, the weather this summer has been much hotter and drier, and the rice fields are suffering.","t":"和去年相比，今年夏天的天氣更熱更乾，稻田正受影響。"},{"w":"comparable","p":"adj.","d":"similar in size, quality, or amount, so it can be compared","c":"可比較的；比得上的","s":"The two phones are comparable in price, so choose the one with the better camera.","t":"這兩支手機價格差不多，所以選相機比較好的那支。"},{"w":"comparative","p":"adj.","d":"judged by comparing with something else; relating to comparison","c":"比較的","s":"We did a comparative study of Mars and Earth, and we found that both planets once had rivers and lakes.","t":"我們做了一項火星與地球的比較研究，而我們發現兩顆行星都曾經有河流和湖泊。"},{"w":"comparatively","p":"adv.","d":"when compared with something else","c":"相對地","s":"Housing in Tainan is comparatively cheap when you look at prices in Taipei.","t":"跟台北的房價相比，台南的房子相對便宜。"},{"w":"compassion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of sympathy for people who are suffering","c":"同情；憐憫","s":"We felt deep compassion for the families who lost their homes.","t":"我們對失去家園的家庭深感同情。"},{"w":"compassionate","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or showing sympathy for others","c":"有同情心的","s":"Patients love Dr. Lin because she is so compassionate, and she always takes time to listen.","t":"病人們很喜歡林醫師,因為她非常有同情心,總是花時間傾聽。"},{"w":"compassionately","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind and caring way","c":"同情地","s":"The nurse spoke compassionately to the frightened child.","t":"護理師溫柔體貼地對受驚的孩子說話。"},{"w":"complain","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is wrong or not satisfactory","c":"抱怨","s":"Dozens of train passengers went to the service counter to complain about the two-hour departure delay.","t":"數十名火車乘客前往服務台抱怨發車延誤兩小時。"},{"w":"complaint","p":"n.","d":"a statement that something is wrong or unfair","c":"抱怨；投訴","s":"The hotel received a complaint about noise from the bar, so the manager closed it earlier on weeknights.","t":"飯店接到關於酒吧噪音的投訴，所以經理讓它在平日提早打烊。"},{"w":"complaining","p":"n.","d":"saying that you are unhappy about something","c":"抱怨","s":"Stop complaining about the weather and enjoy the trip!","t":"別再抱怨天氣了，好好享受旅程吧！。"},{"w":"compose","p":"v.","d":"to write music, a poem, or a letter","c":"組成；作曲","s":"Water is composed of hydrogen and oxygen.","t":"水是由氫和氧組成的。"},{"w":"composition","p":"n.","d":"a piece of music or writing; the way something is made up","c":"組成；作品；作文","s":"Scientists studied the composition of the metal, and they found that a little carbon made it much stronger.","t":"科學家研究這種金屬的成分,而他們發現少量的碳讓它堅固許多。"},{"w":"composer","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes music","c":"作曲家","s":"Mozart was a great composer who began writing music at the age of five.","t":"莫札特是偉大的作曲家，五歲就開始寫曲。"},{"w":"composed","p":"adj.","d":"calm and in control of your feelings","c":"由……組成的；鎮定的","s":"Our class is composed of thirty students from four different towns.","t":"我們班由來自四個不同鄉鎮的三十位學生組成。"},{"w":"concentrate","p":"v.","d":"to give all your attention to one thing","c":"專心；集中","s":"It's hard to concentrate on my reading when my brother is playing the drums.","t":"我弟弟在打鼓時，我很難專心讀書。"},{"w":"concentration","p":"n.","d":"the ability to give all your attention to something","c":"專注力；集中","s":"His concentration on the task was so intense that he didn't notice the time passing.","t":"他對任務的專注程度非常高，以至於他沒有注意到時間過去了。"},{"w":"concentrated","p":"adj.","d":"gathered closely in one place","c":"濃縮的；集中的","s":"Mix one spoon of the concentrated orange juice with a full glass of water.","t":"把一湯匙濃縮柳橙汁加入一整杯水中調勻。"},{"w":"concern","p":"n./v.","d":"a feeling of worry; to cause worry to someone","c":"關心；擔憂；涉及","s":"Parents expressed deep concern regarding the safety of school pedestrian crossings near busy morning intersections.","t":"家長們對繁忙晨間十字路口附近的學校行人穿越道安全表達了深切的擔憂。"},{"w":"concerned","p":"adj.","d":"worried; involved in something","c":"擔心的","s":"Mom was concerned when I didn't answer my phone all evening.","t":"我整晚沒接電話，媽媽很擔心。"},{"w":"concerning","p":"prep.","d":"about; on the subject of","c":"關於","s":"The principal sent a letter to all parents concerning the new rules for using phones during school hours.","t":"校長寄了一封信給所有家長，關於上課時間使用手機的新規定。"},{"w":"conclude","p":"v.","d":"to end something; to decide after thinking","c":"下結論；結束","s":"After a lengthy discussion, they conclude the meeting.","t":"經過長時間的討論，他們結束了會議。"},{"w":"conclusion","p":"n.","d":"a decision you reach after thinking","c":"結論；結尾","s":"In conclusion, reading every day can really improve your English.","t":"總之，每天閱讀確實能提升英文。"},{"w":"conclusive","p":"adj.","d":"proving something without doubt","c":"確鑿的","s":"The evidence for human-caused warming is conclusive, and almost every climate scientist agrees with it.","t":"人為造成暖化的證據是確鑿的,幾乎每位氣候科學家都同意。"},{"w":"confess","p":"v.","d":"to admit that you have done something wrong or embarrassing","c":"坦白；承認","s":"I have to confess that I've never actually read the book I recommended to you.","t":"我必須承認，我從沒真正讀過我推薦給你的那本書。"},{"w":"confession","p":"n.","d":"a statement admitting that you did something wrong","c":"坦白；告白","s":"The thief made a full confession to the police and told them where he had hidden the stolen jewelry.","t":"小偷向警方完整認罪，並告訴他們他把偷來的珠寶藏在哪裡。"},{"w":"confessed","p":"adj.","d":"having admitted openly that you are something","c":"公開承認的","s":"Ben finally confessed to his mom that he had eaten all the cookies.","t":"Ben 終於向媽媽坦白他吃光了所有餅乾。"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"feeling sure about yourself or something","c":"有自信的","s":"I'm confident that our class will win the chorus contest.","t":"我有信心我們班會贏得合唱比賽。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you can do something well; trust in someone","c":"自信；信心","s":"Practicing in front of a mirror helped me gain confidence before my speech.","t":"對著鏡子練習幫我在演講前建立了自信。"},{"w":"confidently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you are sure","c":"自信地","s":"Jenny walked onto the stage confidently and started to sing.","t":"珍妮自信地走上舞台開始唱歌。"},{"w":"self-confidence","p":"n.","d":"belief in your own abilities","c":"自信心","s":"Joining the drama club gave Tina more self-confidence, and now she is not afraid to share her ideas in class.","t":"加入戲劇社讓蒂娜更有自信心,現在她不再害怕在課堂上分享想法。"},{"w":"conflict","p":"n./v.","d":"to be different and not able to exist together","c":"衝突；抵觸","s":"The two neighbors have been in conflict over the noisy dog for months.","t":"兩位鄰居為了那隻吵鬧的狗已經爭執好幾個月。"},{"w":"conflicting","p":"adj.","d":"opposite and not able to agree","c":"相互矛盾的","s":"I received conflicting information about the meeting time, so I didn't know when to show up.","t":"我收到關於開會時間互相矛盾的訊息，所以不知道何時該到。"},{"w":"conflicts","p":"n.","d":"serious disagreements or fights","c":"衝突（複數）","s":"Countries should solve their conflicts peacefully instead of going to war.","t":"各國應以和平方式解決衝突，而不是開戰。"},{"w":"confront","p":"v.","d":"to face a problem or a person directly","c":"面對；對抗","s":"Instead of running away from her fears, Lily decided to confront them.","t":"莉莉決定正視自己的恐懼，而不是逃避。"},{"w":"confrontation","p":"n.","d":"an angry argument or fight between people or groups","c":"對峙；衝突","s":"The teacher stepped in quickly to stop a confrontation between two boys who were shouting at each other in the hallway.","t":"老師迅速介入，制止了兩個在走廊上互相大吼的男孩之間的衝突。"},{"w":"confrontational","p":"adj.","d":"likely to argue or fight with people","c":"對抗性的","s":"His confrontational way of speaking at meetings makes other people feel attacked, so few of them want to work with him.","t":"他在會議上挑釁的說話方式讓其他人覺得受到攻擊，所以很少人想和他共事。"},{"w":"connect","p":"v.","d":"to join two things together","c":"連接；連結","s":"The new MRT line will connect Taoyuan Airport with downtown Taipei.","t":"新的捷運線將連接桃園機場與台北市中心。"},{"w":"connection","p":"n.","d":"a link between two things; a phone or Internet line","c":"關聯；連結","s":"The Internet connection in the mountains was so slow that it took ten minutes to send one photo.","t":"山上的網路連線慢到傳一張照片要十分鐘。"},{"w":"connected","p":"adj.","d":"joined or linked together.","c":"連接的；有關聯的","s":"Before you start the online class, make sure your laptop is connected to the Wi-Fi.","t":"上線上課程前，先確定你的筆電有連上 Wi-Fi。"},{"w":"disconnect","p":"v.","d":"to separate something from a power supply or another thing","c":"切斷；斷線","s":"Please disconnect the printer from the computer before you move it, or you might damage the cable.","t":"移動印表機之前請先把它與電腦斷開，否則你可能會弄壞連接線。"},{"w":"conscious","p":"adj.","d":"awake; aware of something","c":"有意識的；察覺的","s":"Many young people are becoming more conscious of the need to protect the environment.","t":"許多年輕人越來越意識到保護環境的必要。"},{"w":"consciousness","p":"n.","d":"being awake and aware of yourself","c":"意識","s":"Scientists still argue about animal consciousness, but most agree that dogs and apes have feelings.","t":"科學家仍在爭論動物的意識，但大多數人同意狗和猿類有情感。"},{"w":"unconscious","p":"adj.","d":"not awake or aware of surroundings due to a severe injury, illness, or shock","c":"失去知覺的","s":"The patient remained unconscious for two days after the operation.","t":"病人手術後昏迷了兩天。"},{"w":"consciously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is planned and deliberate","c":"有意識地","s":"The designer consciously chose recycled materials, because she wanted her shop to cause less pollution.","t":"這位設計師刻意地選擇回收材料,因為她希望她的店能減少污染。"},{"w":"consequence","p":"n.","d":"a result of an action, often a bad one","c":"後果","s":"Actions have consequence.","t":"行動有後果。"},{"w":"consequent","p":"adj.","d":"happening as a result of something","c":"隨之發生的","s":"The drought and the consequent fall in river levels meant that the hydroelectric dams produced much less power.","t":"乾旱和隨之而來的河川水位下降，意味著水力發電水壩的發電量少了很多。"},{"w":"consequently","p":"adv.","d":"used to show the result of an action","c":"因此","s":"Tim didn't study at all. Consequently, he failed the test.","t":"提姆完全沒讀書，因此考試不及格。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"consider – create · 15 字族 · 34 題","cards":[{"w":"consider","p":"v.","d":"to think carefully about something","c":"考慮","s":"Did you consider the implications of your decision?","t":"你考慮過你的決定的含義嗎？"},{"w":"consideration","p":"n.","d":"careful thought","c":"考慮；體貼","s":"After careful consideration, we decided to go to Kenting instead of Taitung.","t":"仔細考慮後，我們決定去墾丁而不是台東。"},{"w":"considerate","p":"adj.","d":"kind and careful about other people's feelings","c":"體貼的","s":"It was very considerate of you to save me a seat on the bus.","t":"你在公車上幫我留位子，真是太體貼了。"},{"w":"considerable","p":"adj.","d":"large in amount or size","c":"相當大的","s":"The damage caused a considerable amount of financial loss.","t":"損害造成了相當大的財務損失。"},{"w":"considerably","p":"adv.","d":"by a large amount","c":"相當地","s":"The costs have risen considerably since last year.","t":"費用自去年以來已經大幅上升。"},{"w":"consistent","p":"adj.","d":"always behaving or happening in the same way; not changing","c":"一致的；始終如一的","s":"Her performance has been consistent throughout the year.","t":"她的表現在整個年度都是一致的。"},{"w":"consistently","p":"adv.","d":"always in the same way","c":"一貫地","s":"Anna has consistently gotten top grades in math since junior high.","t":"Anna 從國中起數學成績一直名列前茅。"},{"w":"consistency","p":"n.","d":"the quality of always being the same","c":"一致性","s":"A good coach knows that consistency in training matters more than talent.","t":"好教練知道訓練的持之以恆比天分更重要。"},{"w":"inconsistent","p":"adj.","d":"not staying the same; changing in a confusing way","c":"不一致的","s":"The chatbot gave inconsistent answers to the same question, so I stopped trusting it for my science homework.","t":"聊天機器人對同一個問題給出前後不一致的答案,所以我寫自然作業時不再相信它。"},{"w":"constant","p":"adj.","d":"happening all the time","c":"不斷的；固定的","s":"Living near the airport means hearing the constant noise of planes all day.","t":"住在機場附近代表整天聽到飛機不斷的噪音。"},{"w":"constantly","p":"adv.","d":"all the time","c":"不斷地","s":"My little brother constantly asks \"Why?\" about everything he sees.","t":"我弟弟對看到的每件事都不停地問「為什麼？」。"},{"w":"constancy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of staying the same or loyal","c":"恆定；忠誠","s":"Living near the airport means hearing the constant noise of planes all day.","t":"住在機場附近代表整天聽到飛機不斷的噪音。"},{"w":"construct","p":"v.","d":"to build something large such as a building, bridge, or road","c":"建造","s":"They plan to construct a bridge over the river.","t":"他們計畫在河上建造一座橋樑。"},{"w":"construction","p":"n.","d":"the work of building something; the way something is built","c":"建設；施工","s":"The construction of the new mall will be completed next year.","t":"新購物中心的建設將于明年完成。"},{"w":"constructive","p":"adj.","d":"helpful and useful, especially when giving opinions","c":"建設性的","s":"The coach gave the players constructive comments after the game, so they knew exactly what to practise next week.","t":"教練在比賽後給球員們有建設性的意見,所以他們確切知道下週要練習什麼。"},{"w":"constructively","p":"adv.","d":"in a helpful and useful way","c":"建設性地","s":"Our teacher showed us how to comment on each other's work constructively.","t":"老師教我們如何以建設性的方式評論彼此的作品。"},{"w":"consume","p":"v.","d":"to eat, drink, or use something, especially in large amounts","c":"消耗；消費；吃喝","s":"Air conditioners consume a lot of electricity in the summer.","t":"冷氣在夏天會消耗大量電力。"},{"w":"consumer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys goods or uses services","c":"消費者","s":"Online shopping has changed the way a typical consumer makes decisions.","t":"網購改變了一般消費者做決定的方式。"},{"w":"consumption","p":"n.","d":"the act of using, eating, or drinking something","c":"消耗（量）；消費","s":"Taiwan's consumption of bubble tea is huge; millions of cups are sold every day.","t":"台灣的珍奶消費量非常大，每天賣出數百萬杯。"},{"w":"contact","p":"n./v.","d":"to call or write to someone","c":"聯絡；接觸","s":"We lost contact after she moved to Canada, but we found each other again on Instagram.","t":"她搬到加拿大後我們就失聯了，但後來在 IG 上又聯繫上。"},{"w":"contactless","p":"adj.","d":"done without touching another person or a machine","c":"非接觸式的","s":"A: During the busy holiday season, how can the delivery drivers bring packages to so many homes without waiting for people to sign? B: The company offers contactless delivery, so drivers simply leave the package at the door, take a photo of it, and send the picture to the customer's phone.","t":"A：在忙碌的假期期間，送貨司機要怎麼不必等人簽收，就把包裹送到這麼多戶人家？ B：那家公司提供【免接觸】配送，所以司機只要把包裹放在門口、拍張照片，再把照片傳到顧客的手機就好。"},{"w":"contacts","p":"n.","d":"people you know and can call or write to","c":"聯絡人（複數）","s":"We lost contact after she moved to Canada, but we found each other again on Instagram.","t":"她搬到加拿大後我們就失聯了，但後來在 IG 上又聯繫上。"},{"w":"contain","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from spreading","c":"包含；容納","s":"Health workers moved quickly to contain the outbreak, so it stayed in one small town.","t":"衛生人員迅速行動以遏制疫情,所以它只停留在一個小鎮。"},{"w":"container","p":"n.","d":"a box, bottle, or other object used for holding things","c":"容器","s":"The food was stored in a plastic container for transport.","t":"食物存放在一個塑料容器中進行運輸。"},{"w":"containment","p":"n.","d":"keeping something harmful under control","c":"控制；遏止","s":"Quick containment of the fire saved most of the forest, but several hectares near the road were destroyed.","t":"迅速控制火勢挽救了大部分森林,但靠近道路的幾公頃仍被燒毀。"},{"w":"continue","p":"v.","d":"to keep happening or existing without stopping","c":"繼續","s":"Although heavy snow fell across the highway, the rescue team decided to continue their search for the missing hikers.","t":"儘管大雪降在公路上，搜救隊仍決定繼續搜尋失蹤的登山客。"},{"w":"continuous","p":"adj.","d":"happening or existing without stopping","c":"連續不斷的","s":"The machine makes a continuous noise all day.","t":"這台機器整天發出不間斷的噪音。"},{"w":"continuously","p":"adv.","d":"happening without any pauses or interruptions.","c":"連續不斷地","s":"It rained continuously for three days, so the baseball game was cancelled.","t":"連續下了三天雨，所以棒球賽取消了。"},{"w":"continuation","p":"n.","d":"the act of carrying on with something","c":"延續","s":"The continuation of the free school lunch programme depends on next year's budget, so parents are worried.","t":"免費營養午餐計畫能否延續取決於明年的預算,所以家長們很擔心。"},{"w":"contrast","p":"n./v.","d":"a clear difference between two things when they are compared","c":"對比；差異；形成對比","s":"The contrast between the two paintings is quite evident.","t":"這兩幅畫之間的對比是非常明顯的。"},{"w":"contrasting","p":"adj.","d":"very different from each other","c":"截然不同的；對比的","s":"The twins have contrasting personalities: one is outgoing, and the other is quiet.","t":"這對雙胞胎個性截然不同：一個外向，一個安靜。"},{"w":"in contrast","p":"phr.","d":"showing a difference with something just said","c":"相較之下","s":"in contrast, the southern region has a much warmer climate.","t":"相對於，南方地區的氣候要暖和得多。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give money, help, or ideas to something together with other people","c":"貢獻；捐助；促成","s":"Many local businesses agreed to contribute money to the new community centre so that everyone could benefit from it.","t":"許多本地企業同意捐款資助新的社區中心，讓所有人都能從中受益。"},{"w":"contribution","p":"n.","d":"something you give or do to help make something successful","c":"貢獻","s":"Her contribution to earthquake research was huge, and many of today's safety rules are based on her work.","t":"她對地震研究的貢獻非常大，而今天許多安全規定都是根據她的研究制定的。"},{"w":"contributor","p":"n.","d":"someone or something that helps cause something","c":"貢獻者","s":"Farm fertiliser is a major contributor to the green algae in the lake, so farmers are being asked to use less.","t":"農用肥料是湖中綠藻的主要促成因素,所以農民被要求減少使用。"},{"w":"control","p":"n./v.","d":"the power to direct or manage something; to regulate","c":"控制","s":"During heavy weekend traffic, automated electronic systems help control vehicle speeds on the highway.","t":"在週末繁忙的車流中，自動化電子系統協助控制高速公路上的車速。"},{"w":"controlled","p":"adj.","d":"kept within set limits; highly organized.","c":"受控制的","s":"The fire was finally controlled after firefighters worked through the night.","t":"消防員徹夜搶救後，火勢終於被控制住。"},{"w":"controller","p":"n.","d":"a person who directs or regulates something; a handheld device used to operate games or machines","c":"控制器；管理者","s":"Ken pressed the buttons on the game controller so hard that one of them broke.","t":"Ken 按遊戲手把按鍵太用力，弄壞了一個。"},{"w":"uncontrollable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to control","c":"無法控制的","s":"When the clown fell off his bike, the kids burst into uncontrollable laughter.","t":"小丑從腳踏車上摔下來時，孩子們爆出止不住的笑聲。"},{"w":"cooperate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others to achieve something","c":"合作","s":"The two rival shops decided to cooperate during the festival, and they shared one large stall to save money.","t":"兩家競爭的商店決定在節慶期間合作，而且他們共用一個大攤位來省錢。"},{"w":"cooperation","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together for a shared purpose","c":"合作","s":"cooperation between various stakeholders is crucial for the success of the initiative.","t":"各利益相關者之間的合作對於該倡議的成功至關重要。"},{"w":"cooperative","p":"adj.","d":"willing to help and work with others","c":"合作的；樂於配合的","s":"The patient was very cooperative and followed all of the nurse's instructions.","t":"這位病人很配合，遵照護理師的所有指示。"},{"w":"corporation","p":"n.","d":"a large company or group of companies","c":"公司；企業","s":"My uncle works for a large international corporation that makes computer chips.","t":"我叔叔在一家生產電腦晶片的大型跨國企業工作。"},{"w":"corporate","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a large company","c":"公司的；企業的","s":"The new manager wants to change the corporate culture so that workers feel more relaxed.","t":"新經理想改變公司文化，讓員工感覺更輕鬆。"},{"w":"corporations","p":"n.","d":"large companies","c":"企業（複數）","s":"Some big corporations have been criticized for polluting rivers.","t":"一些大企業因污染河川而受到批評。"},{"w":"courage","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something that frightens one; bravery","c":"勇氣","s":"It took a lot of courage for Amy to sing alone on stage.","t":"艾咪要鼓起很大勇氣才敢獨自上台唱歌。"},{"w":"courageous","p":"adj.","d":"brave; not afraid to do something difficult or dangerous","c":"勇敢的","s":"Telling the truth after making a mistake is a courageous thing to do.","t":"犯錯後說實話是勇敢的行為。"},{"w":"courageously","p":"adv.","d":"in a brave way","c":"勇敢地","s":"The girl courageously stood up to the bully and protected her friend.","t":"那女孩勇敢地對抗霸凌者，保護了她的朋友。"},{"w":"create","p":"v.","d":"to make something new","c":"創造","s":"Artists create works that reflect their emotions and ideas.","t":"藝術家創建反映他們的情感和想法的作品。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new ideas","c":"有創意的","s":"She's a very creative designer with innovative concepts.","t":"她是一個非常有創造力的設計師，有很創新的概念。"},{"w":"creativity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to think of new ideas and make new things","c":"創造力","s":"Innovation requires creativity.","t":"創新需要創造力。"},{"w":"creator","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes something new","c":"創造者；創作者","s":"Hayao Miyazaki is the creator of many famous animated films, such as Spirited Away.","t":"宮崎駿是許多知名動畫電影（如《神隱少女》）的創作者。"},{"w":"creation","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something new; something that has been made","c":"創造；創作物","s":"The night market stand is famous for its latest creation: bubble tea ice cream.","t":"這個夜市攤位以最新創作——珍珠奶茶冰淇淋聞名。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"credit – definite · 15 字族 · 40 題","cards":[{"w":"credit","p":"n./v.","d":"trust that you will pay money back later","c":"功勞；信用；歸功於","s":"She deserves the credit for our team's success; she organized everything.","t":"團隊的成功應歸功於她；一切都是她安排的。"},{"w":"credible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be believed or trusted","c":"可信的","s":"The news story was not credible because it gave no sources.","t":"這則新聞不可信，因為它沒有提供任何消息來源。"},{"w":"incredible","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good, large, or surprising; amazing","c":"難以置信的；極好的","s":"The view from the top of Yushan was incredible!","t":"從玉山頂上看到的景色真是美得難以置信！。"},{"w":"crime","p":"n.","d":"an illegal action or activity for which a person can be punished","c":"罪；犯罪","s":"Stealing other people's personal information online is a serious crime.","t":"在網路上竊取他人個資是嚴重的犯罪。"},{"w":"criminal","p":"n./adj.","d":"a person who committed a major breaking of law.","c":"罪犯；犯罪的；可恥的","s":"The police finally caught the criminal who had stolen several scooters in the neighborhood.","t":"警方終於抓到偷了附近好幾台機車的犯人。"},{"w":"critic","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to give opinions about books, films, or art; a person who says something is bad","c":"評論家","s":"The famous food critic gave our little restaurant five stars, and since then the place has been full every night.","t":"那位知名的美食評論家給我們的小餐廳五顆星，從那時起這裡每晚都客滿。"},{"w":"critical","p":"adj.","d":"saying that something is bad or wrong; very important or serious","c":"批評的；關鍵的","s":"The next two days are critical for the patient's recovery.","t":"接下來兩天是病人康復的關鍵期。"},{"w":"criticism","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying what is bad or wrong about something or someone","c":"批評","s":"The new exam system received a lot of criticism, so the education department agreed to review it next year.","t":"新的考試制度受到許多批評,所以教育部門同意明年重新檢討。"},{"w":"criticize","p":"v.","d":"to say that something or someone is bad or wrong","c":"批評","s":"Teachers should never criticize students in front of the whole class.","t":"老師不應在全班面前批評學生。"},{"w":"critically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that judges carefully","c":"批判地；危急地","s":"Learning to think critically is an important skill in the age of fake news.","t":"學習批判性思考是假新聞時代的重要能力。"},{"w":"crowd","p":"n./v.","d":"a large number of people gathered together; to pack into","c":"人群；聚集；擠滿","s":"A large crowd gathered outside the stadium to welcome the baseball team home.","t":"一大群人聚集在球場外迎接棒球隊回家。"},{"w":"crowded","p":"adj.","d":"full of people, leaving little or no room for movement","c":"擁擠的","s":"The MRT is always crowded during rush hour, so I often have to stand.","t":"捷運在尖峰時段總是很擠，所以我常常得站著。"},{"w":"overcrowded","p":"adj.","d":"having too many people in a space","c":"過度擁擠的","s":"The trains are overcrowded during rush hour, so I usually leave home early to get a seat.","t":"尖峰時段火車過度擁擠,所以我通常提早出門好找到座位。"},{"w":"cruel","p":"adj.","d":"causing pain or suffering on purpose","c":"殘忍的","s":"It is cruel to leave a dog tied up outside all day in the hot sun.","t":"把狗整天綁在外面曬大太陽是很殘忍的。"},{"w":"cruelty","p":"n.","d":"behavior that causes pain or suffering to people or animals","c":"殘忍","s":"The animal shelter takes care of cats and dogs that have suffered cruelty from their owners.","t":"動物收容所照顧遭主人虐待的貓狗。"},{"w":"cruelly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that causes pain or suffering","c":"殘忍地","s":"The villain in the movie cruelly locked the princess in a dark tower.","t":"電影中的反派殘忍地把公主關在黑暗的塔裡。"},{"w":"culture","p":"n.","d":"the customs and way of life of a group","c":"文化","s":"Taiwan's night market culture attracts tourists from all over the world.","t":"台灣的夜市文化吸引了世界各地的觀光客。"},{"w":"cultural","p":"adj.","d":"about culture","c":"文化的","s":"The city is known for its cultural festivals.","t":"該城市以其文化節日而著稱。"},{"w":"culturally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to culture","c":"在文化上","s":"It is culturally important to bring a small gift when visiting someone's home in Japan.","t":"在日本拜訪別人家時帶個小禮物，在文化上是很重要的。"},{"w":"multicultural","p":"adj.","d":"including people of many different cultures","c":"多元文化的","s":"Our neighbourhood is very multicultural, and the summer festival includes food and music from Vietnam, Indonesia and the Philippines.","t":"我們的社區非常多元文化，而夏季節慶包含來自越南、印尼和菲律賓的美食和音樂。"},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"eager to know or learn something new","c":"好奇的","s":"Babies are naturally curious and want to touch everything they see.","t":"嬰兒天生好奇，看到什麼都想摸。"},{"w":"curiosity","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to know or learn about something","c":"好奇心","s":"Out of curiosity, I opened the old letter I found in the drawer.","t":"出於好奇，我打開了在抽屜裡找到的舊信。"},{"w":"curiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you want to know more; strangely","c":"好奇地","s":"The cat looked curiously at the new box before jumping inside.","t":"貓好奇地看著新箱子然後跳了進去。"},{"w":"day","p":"n.","d":"twenty-four hours; the time when it is light","c":"天；白天","s":"This convenience store is open twenty-four hours a day, seven days a week.","t":"這家便利商店一天24小時、一週七天都營業。"},{"w":"daily","p":"adj./adv.","d":"done, produced, or occurring every day or every weekday","c":"每日的；每天地","s":"Reading the news is part of my father's daily routine.","t":"看新聞是我爸爸每天例行公事的一部分。"},{"w":"daytime","p":"n.","d":"the time of day when it is light","c":"白天","s":"Bats rest in caves during the day and come out after dark.","t":"蝙蝠白天在洞穴裡休息，天黑後才出來。"},{"w":"decide","p":"v.","d":"to choose what to do after thinking","c":"決定","s":"Q: Will you buy the red bag or the blue bag? — A: I don't know. I will decide later.","t":"你會買紅色還是藍色的包包？ — 我不知道，我等一下再決定。"},{"w":"decision","p":"n.","d":"a choice that you make after thinking","c":"決定","s":"Choosing a university department is a big decision for high school students.","t":"選大學科系對高中生來說是個重大的決定。"},{"w":"decisive","p":"adj.","d":"able to make decisions quickly and with confidence","c":"決定性的；果斷的","s":"Quick action by the coastguard played a decisive role, because the oil was stopped before it reached the beach.","t":"海巡的迅速行動發揮了決定性的作用,因為油污在抵達海灘前就被攔住了。"},{"w":"indecisive","p":"adj.","d":"unable to make decisions quickly","c":"優柔寡斷的","s":"My best friend is so indecisive that it takes her twenty minutes to order a drink.","t":"我最好的朋友非常優柔寡斷，點一杯飲料要花二十分鐘。"},{"w":"decisively","p":"adv.","d":"in a firm way that settles something","c":"果斷地；決定性地","s":"Our team won decisively, beating the other school 10 to 1.","t":"我們隊以十比一大勝對手學校。"},{"w":"decline","p":"v./n.","d":"to become smaller, fewer, or weaker","c":"下降；婉拒；衰退","s":"She had to decline the invitation due to prior commitments.","t":"由於先前的承諾，她不得不拒絕了邀請。"},{"w":"declining","p":"adj.","d":"becoming less or smaller","c":"衰退中的","s":"Many villages in the mountains face a declining population as young people move away.","t":"年輕人外移，許多山村面臨人口減少。"},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something more attractive by adding pretty things","c":"裝飾","s":"Before the festive holiday dinner begins on Christmas Eve, the children always gather in the living room to decorate the tall tree.","t":"在平安夜節日晚餐開始之前，孩子們總是聚集在客廳裝飾那棵高大的樹。"},{"w":"decoration","p":"n.","d":"something that is added to make a place or thing look more beautiful","c":"裝飾（品）","s":"The students made paper decorations to hang around the classroom before the school's end-of-year celebration party.","t":"學生們製作了紙質裝飾品，在學校年終慶祝派對前掛在教室周圍。"},{"w":"decorative","p":"adj.","d":"made to look pretty","c":"裝飾性的","s":"The plates on the wall are only decorative; nobody actually eats from them.","t":"牆上的盤子只是裝飾用的，沒有人真的用來盛食物。"},{"w":"dedicate","p":"v.","d":"to give your time and energy to something important","c":"奉獻；致力於","s":"She dedicated her life to helping homeless children.","t":"她一生致力幫助無家可歸的孩子。"},{"w":"dedication","p":"n.","d":"hard work and effort that you give to something you care about","c":"奉獻","s":"The coach thanked his players for their hard work and dedication all season.","t":"教練感謝球員們整季的努力和投入。"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"used only for one particular purpose","c":"專注的；盡心盡力的","s":"The writer dedicated her first novel to her late grandfather.","t":"作家把她的第一本小說獻給已故的祖父。"},{"w":"defend","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone or something from attack or harm; to speak in support of","c":"防禦；為…辯護","s":"He is determined to defend his family from harm.","t":"他下定決心保護家人免受傷害。"},{"w":"defense","p":"n.","d":"the act of protecting someone or something from attack; the players who try to stop the other team from scoring","c":"防禦；辯護","s":"The fortress was a stronghold of defense against invaders.","t":"這座堡壘是對抗入侵者的堅強防禦。"},{"w":"defensive","p":"adj.","d":"used or meant to protect; behaving as if someone is attacking you","c":"防禦的；防衛心強的","s":"When people criticize her writing, Lisa tends to get defensive instead of listening.","t":"別人批評 Lisa 的文章時，她常會防衛心很強而不是傾聽。"},{"w":"defender","p":"n.","d":"a person who protects something; a player whose job is to stop the other team from scoring","c":"防守者；捍衛者","s":"Our team's best defender stopped three goals in the second half of the match.","t":"我們隊最好的後衛在下半場擋下三顆球。"},{"w":"define","p":"v.","d":"to explain exactly what something means","c":"下定義；界定","s":"Can you define the word \"teamwork\" in simple English for the class?","t":"你能用簡單的英文向全班解釋 teamwork 這個字的意思嗎？。"},{"w":"definition","p":"n.","d":"a sentence that explains what a word means","c":"定義","s":"The dictionary provides a clear definition of each word.","t":"字典為每個詞提供了清晰的定義。"},{"w":"defined","p":"adj.","d":"clearly shown or explained","c":"明確的；界定的","s":"My little brother has defined \"weekend\" as \"two days with no alarm clock.\"","t":"我弟弟把「週末」定義為「兩天不用鬧鐘的日子」。"},{"w":"definite","p":"adj.","d":"clear and certain; not likely to change","c":"明確的","s":"We still haven't got a definite answer from the coach about the game.","t":"我們還沒得到教練對比賽的明確答覆。"},{"w":"definitely","p":"adv.","d":"certainly; without any doubt","c":"肯定地；確實","s":"I will definitely come to your birthday party on Saturday.","t":"我星期六一定會去你的生日派對。"},{"w":"indefinite","p":"adj.","d":"with no fixed end","c":"不確定的","s":"The project has been put on an indefinite hold due to lack of funding.","t":"由於缺乏資金，該項目已被無限期擱置。"},{"w":"indefinitely","p":"adv.","d":"for a period with no fixed end","c":"無限期地","s":"The school library will be closed indefinitely because of the earthquake damage.","t":"因地震受損，學校圖書館將無限期關閉。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"deliberate – determine · 15 字族 · 36 題","cards":[{"w":"deliberate","p":"adj./v.","d":"done on purpose, not by accident","c":"故意的；仔細考慮","s":"It was not a deliberate mistake; I simply forgot to bring the book.","t":"那不是故意犯的錯；我只是忘了帶書。"},{"w":"deliberately","p":"adv.","d":"on purpose","c":"故意地","s":"I'm sure he broke the vase deliberately; he was angry with his sister.","t":"我確定他是故意打破花瓶的；他在生姊姊的氣。"},{"w":"deliberation","p":"n.","d":"careful thought or discussion before a decision","c":"深思熟慮","s":"After much deliberation, the judges finally announced the winner.","t":"經過一番深思熟慮，評審終於宣布了優勝者。"},{"w":"delicate","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged; needing careful treatment; fine and beautiful","c":"精緻的；易碎的；細膩的","s":"Picking strawberries is a delicate job, so the robot uses soft fingers that will not crush the fruit.","t":"採草莓是一項精細的工作,所以機器人使用不會把果實壓爛的柔軟手指。"},{"w":"delicacy","p":"n.","d":"a rare or expensive food that is special to eat","c":"佳餚；精緻；脆弱","s":"Mullet roe is a delicacy in Taiwan, so families often give it as a gift during Lunar New Year.","t":"烏魚子在台灣是一種珍饈，所以家家戶戶常在農曆新年時把它當作禮物送人。"},{"w":"delicately","p":"adv.","d":"in a gentle and careful way","c":"細緻地；小心地","s":"The nurse delicately removed the bandage from the child's arm.","t":"護理師小心翼翼地拆下孩子手臂上的繃帶。"},{"w":"delight","p":"n./v.","d":"a feeling of great pleasure; something that gives great pleasure","c":"欣喜；使高興","s":"The magician's tricks delight the children at the party, and they begged him to perform again.","t":"魔術師的把戲讓派對上的孩子們很開心,他們央求他再表演一次。"},{"w":"delighted","p":"adj.","d":"feeling incredibly glad or pleased about an event.","c":"高興的","s":"We were delighted to hear that our teacher had won a national award.","t":"聽到老師獲得全國性獎項，我們都很高興。"},{"w":"delightful","p":"adj.","d":"very pleasant and enjoyable","c":"令人愉快的","s":"We spent a delightful afternoon drinking tea and chatting in Jiufen.","t":"我們在九份喝茶聊天，度過一個愉快的下午。"},{"w":"delightfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a very pleasant way","c":"令人愉快地","s":"We were delighted to hear that our teacher had won a national award.","t":"聽到老師獲得全國性獎項，我們都很高興。"},{"w":"deliver","p":"v.","d":"to bring and hand over a letter, parcel, or goods to the proper recipient","c":"運送；發表","s":"The online store promised to deliver my order within 24 hours.","t":"網路商店承諾 24 小時內送達我的訂單。"},{"w":"delivery","p":"n.","d":"the act of providing a service","c":"運送；投遞","s":"The delivery of health services in mountain areas is difficult, so doctors sometimes travel by helicopter.","t":"在山區提供醫療服務很困難,所以醫生有時要搭直升機前往。"},{"w":"deliverer","p":"n.","d":"a person who brings things to people","c":"送貨員","s":"The online store promised to deliver my order within 24 hours.","t":"網路商店承諾 24 小時內送達我的訂單。"},{"w":"demand","p":"n./v.","d":"a strong request; the wish of people to buy something","c":"需求；要求","s":"There is a growing demand for electric scooters in Taiwan.","t":"台灣對電動機車的需求日益增加。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time, effort or skill","c":"要求高的；費力的","s":"Being a nurse is a very demanding job that requires long hours.","t":"當護理師是一份工時很長、非常辛苦的工作。"},{"w":"demands","p":"n.","d":"strong requests","c":"要求（複數）","s":"The workers went on strike, and their demands included higher pay and shorter hours.","t":"工人罷工，他們的訴求包括加薪和縮短工時。"},{"w":"democracy","p":"n.","d":"a system of government by the whole population, usually through elected representatives","c":"民主（政治）","s":"Taiwan became a full democracy in the 1990s.","t":"台灣在1990年代成為完全的民主國家。"},{"w":"democratic","p":"adj.","d":"based on the idea that everyone has an equal right to vote and decide","c":"民主的","s":"The class made a democratic decision about the trip; everyone voted, and the beach won by just two votes.","t":"全班對旅行做出了民主的決定；每個人都投票，海邊以兩票之差勝出。"},{"w":"democratically","p":"adv.","d":"by a fair vote of all the people","c":"民主地","s":"Our class leader was chosen democratically by a vote.","t":"我們的班長是經由投票民主選出的。"},{"w":"democrat","p":"n.","d":"a person who believes that people should choose their leaders by voting","c":"民主主義者","s":"As a true democrat, my grandfather believes that every adult should have the right to vote, no matter how poor they are.","t":"身為一位真正的民主主義者，我爺爺相信每個成年人無論多窮都應該有投票權。"},{"w":"demonstrate","p":"v.","d":"to show how to do something; to prove that something is true","c":"示範；證明；示威","s":"The engineer demonstrated how the robot could sort rubbish, and the audience was impressed by its speed.","t":"工程師示範了機器人如何分類垃圾,觀眾對它的速度印象深刻。"},{"w":"demonstration","p":"n.","d":"an act of showing how something works; a march or meeting to protest or support something","c":"示範；示威","s":"Our science teacher gave a demonstration of how a volcano erupts using baking soda.","t":"自然老師用小蘇打示範火山如何爆發。"},{"w":"demonstrator","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a public protest","c":"示威者","s":"The demonstrators marched through the streets to protest peacefully.","t":"示威者在街上遊行以和平抗議。"},{"w":"dense","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of things or people close together; thick and hard to see through","c":"濃密的；稠密的","s":"The Earth's core is very dense, so it sank to the centre of the planet when the Earth was young.","t":"地核的密度非常高，所以在地球還年輕時它就沉到了地球中心。"},{"w":"densely","p":"adv.","d":"with many people or things close together","c":"稠密地","s":"The mountains in central Taiwan are densely covered with forests.","t":"台灣中部的山區覆蓋著茂密的森林。"},{"w":"density","p":"n.","d":"how many people or things there are in a space","c":"密度","s":"Scientists measure the density of the ice to learn how much weight the frozen lake can hold before it breaks.","t":"科學家測量冰的密度，以了解結冰的湖面在破裂前能承受多少重量。"},{"w":"deny","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is not true","c":"否認；拒絕給予","s":"The politician had to deny the allegations made against him.","t":"政治人士不得不否認對他提出的指控。"},{"w":"denial","p":"n.","d":"a statement that something is not true","c":"否認","s":"The singer's quick denial of the rumors only made fans more curious.","t":"那位歌手很快否認傳聞，反而讓粉絲更好奇。"},{"w":"undeniable","p":"adj.","d":"clearly true and impossible to doubt","c":"不可否認的","s":"It is undeniable that smartphones have changed the way teenagers make friends.","t":"不可否認，智慧型手機改變了青少年交朋友的方式。"},{"w":"undeniably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that cannot be doubted","c":"不可否認地","s":"Jeremy Lin is undeniably one of the most famous basketball players with Taiwanese roots.","t":"林書豪無疑是最有名的台裔籃球員之一。"},{"w":"depart","p":"v.","d":"to leave a place, especially to start a journey","c":"出發；離開","s":"Flight CI-100 to Tokyo will depart from Gate 5 at 8:30 a.m.","t":"往東京的 CI-100 班機將於早上 8:30 從 5 號登機門出發。"},{"w":"departure","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving a place; a plane or train that leaves","c":"出發；離開","s":"Please check the departure board for any changes to your train time.","t":"請查看出發時刻看板，確認火車時間是否有更動。"},{"w":"departed","p":"adj.","d":"dead (a polite word)","c":"已故的","s":"Flight CI-100 to Tokyo will depart from Gate 5 at 8:30 a.m.","t":"往東京的 CI-100 班機將於早上 8:30 從 5 號登機門出發。"},{"w":"depress","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel very sad and without hope","c":"使沮喪","s":"The bad news began to depress her.","t":"壞消息開始使她感到沮喪。"},{"w":"depressed","p":"adj.","d":"very sad and without hope","c":"（人）沮喪的","s":"He felt depressed after hearing about the accident.","t":"聽到事故的消息後，他感到很沮喪。"},{"w":"depressing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel sad","c":"令人沮喪的","s":"Rainy days always make the city look gray and depressing.","t":"下雨天總讓城市看起來灰暗又令人沮喪。"},{"w":"depression","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great sadness that lasts a long time; a long period when the economy is very bad","c":"沮喪；憂鬱症；蕭條","s":"Doctors say that regular exercise can help people suffering from depression.","t":"醫生說規律運動能幫助憂鬱症患者。"},{"w":"describe","p":"v.","d":"to say what someone or something is like","c":"描述","s":"Can you describe the man who took your bag?","t":"你能描述一下拿走你包包的男子嗎？"},{"w":"description","p":"n.","d":"words that tell what something looks or feels like.","c":"描述","s":"The witness gave a detailed description of the suspect to the police, including his height, hair colour, and clothing.","t":"目擊者向警方提供了嫌疑人的詳細描述，包括他的身高、髮色和衣著。"},{"w":"descriptive","p":"adj.","d":"giving a clear picture of something in words","c":"描述性的","s":"Use more descriptive adjectives in your essay to help readers picture the scene.","t":"作文裡多用描述性的形容詞，幫助讀者想像畫面。"},{"w":"indescribable","p":"adj.","d":"too great or strange to describe in words","c":"難以形容的","s":"The beauty of the sea of clouds at Alishan was indescribable; no words could explain it.","t":"阿里山雲海的美難以形容，任何言語都無法說明。"},{"w":"desperate","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that you have no hope and will do anything to change the situation; needing something very much","c":"絕望的；極度渴望的","s":"After days without food, the lost hikers were desperate for help.","t":"幾天沒吃東西後，迷路的登山客急切地需要救援。"},{"w":"desperately","p":"adv.","d":"in an extreme, intense, or dangerous manner.","c":"拚命地；極度地","s":"The lost puppy was desperately looking for its owner in the rain.","t":"走失的小狗在雨中拚命找主人。"},{"w":"desperation","p":"n.","d":"a baseline state of panic driven by zero options.","c":"絕望","s":"In desperation, the trapped hiker used his phone light to signal for help.","t":"受困的登山客在絕望中用手機燈光求救。"},{"w":"destroy","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it cannot be used","c":"摧毀","s":"The forest fire destroy thousands of trees last summer, and many koalas lost their homes and food.","t":"去年夏天的森林大火摧毀了數千棵樹，許多無尾熊因此失去了家園和食物。"},{"w":"destruction","p":"n.","d":"the act of damaging something so badly that it no longer exists or cannot be used","c":"破壞；毀滅","s":"The destruction of wetlands for new factories has left many birds with nowhere to rest during their long journey.","t":"為了蓋新工廠而破壞濕地，讓許多鳥類在漫長的旅程中無處歇息。"},{"w":"destructive","p":"adj.","d":"causing a lot of damage","c":"破壞性的","s":"The destructive power of the tsunami shocked the whole world.","t":"海嘯的破壞力震驚了全世界。"},{"w":"determine","p":"v.","d":"to decide or find out exactly","c":"決定；查明","s":"In some turtles, the sand temperature can determine whether a baby is male or female.","t":"在某些海龜中，沙子的溫度能決定寶寶是雄性還是雌性。"},{"w":"determination","p":"n.","d":"the strong wish to keep trying until you succeed","c":"決心","s":"With great determination, the swimmer kept training even after she hurt her shoulder.","t":"那位游泳選手以極大的決心，即使肩膀受傷仍繼續訓練。"},{"w":"determined","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to do something so much that you will not let anything stop you","c":"下定決心的","s":"Tom is determined to pass the GEPT this year, so he studies every night.","t":"Tom 決心今年要通過全民英檢，所以他每晚都在念書。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"differ – economy · 15 字族 · 34 題","cards":[{"w":"differ","p":"v.","d":"to be not the same as something else","c":"不同","s":"Twins may look alike, but their personalities can differ a lot.","t":"雙胞胎也許長得很像，但個性可能差很多。"},{"w":"different","p":"adj.","d":"not the same","c":"不同的","s":"Q: Are the two pictures the same or different? — A: They are different. One cat is black, and the other is white.","t":"這兩張圖一樣還是不一樣？ — 不一樣，一隻貓是黑的，另一隻是白的。"},{"w":"difference","p":"n.","d":"the way in which two or more things are not like each other","c":"差異","s":"Can you tell the difference between oolong tea and green tea just by tasting them?","t":"光用嚐的，你分得出烏龍茶和綠茶的差別嗎？。"},{"w":"differentiate","p":"v.","d":"to see or show how two things are different","c":"區分","s":"It's important to differentiate between facts and opinions.","t":"區分事實和意見非常重要。"},{"w":"digest","p":"v.","d":"to change food in your stomach so the body can use it","c":"消化","s":"Babies can't digest some kinds of food yet.","t":"嬰兒還無法消化某些食物。"},{"w":"digestion","p":"n.","d":"the process by which your body breaks down food","c":"消化","s":"Eating slowly and chewing well helps your digestion, and it also stops you from eating more than your body needs.","t":"慢慢吃、好好咀嚼有助於消化，也能防止你吃得比身體需要的多。"},{"w":"digestive","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the body's track for breaking food.","c":"消化的","s":"The stomach is an important part of the digestive system.","t":"胃是消化系統的重要部分。"},{"w":"indigestion","p":"n.","d":"pain in the stomach because food is hard to break down","c":"消化不良","s":"Eating too fast can give you indigestion.","t":"吃太快會讓你消化不良。"},{"w":"digital","p":"adj.","d":"using computer technology; showing numbers instead of hands","c":"數位的","s":"Many young people now prefer digital books because they can read them on their phones.","t":"很多年輕人現在比較喜歡電子書，因為可以用手機看。"},{"w":"digitally","p":"adv.","d":"by using computer technology","c":"數位地","s":"The old family photos were scanned and saved digitally, so now every relative can see them on their phones.","t":"這些老家庭照片被掃描並以數位方式儲存，現在每個親戚都能在手機上看到。"},{"w":"digitize","p":"v.","d":"to change something into digital form","c":"數位化","s":"The library plans to digitize its old newspapers so people can read them online.","t":"圖書館計畫把舊報紙數位化，讓大家可以線上閱讀。"},{"w":"disappoint","p":"v.","d":"to make someone sad because something is not as good as hoped","c":"使失望","s":"I did not want to disappoint my parents, so I studied hard and finally got into the school they hoped for.","t":"我不想讓父母失望，所以努力讀書，終於考上他們期望的學校。"},{"w":"disappointed","p":"adj.","d":"sad because something was not as good as hoped","c":"（人）失望的","s":"Lily was disappointed that her best friend forgot her birthday.","t":"Lily 對好朋友忘記她生日感到很失望。"},{"w":"disappointing","p":"adj.","d":"not as good as hoped","c":"令人失望的","s":"The ending of the movie was so disappointing that many viewers left bad reviews online.","t":"那部電影的結局令人非常失望，很多觀眾在網路上留下負評。"},{"w":"disappointment","p":"n.","d":"the sad feeling when something is not as good as hoped","c":"失望","s":"Much to our disappointment, the outdoor concert was cancelled because of heavy rain.","t":"令我們很失望的是，戶外演唱會因大雨取消了。"},{"w":"discriminate","p":"v.","d":"to see the difference between two things","c":"歧視；區別","s":"Banks must make sure their AI does not discriminate against older people, because everyone deserves a fair chance at a loan.","t":"銀行必須確保它們的人工智慧不會歧視年長者,因為每個人都應該有公平申請貸款的機會。"},{"w":"discrimination","p":"n.","d":"treating a person or group unfairly because of their race, sex, age, etc.","c":"歧視","s":"Racial discrimination is still a problem in many countries.","t":"種族歧視在許多國家仍是個問題。"},{"w":"discriminatory","p":"adj.","d":"treating some people unfairly","c":"歧視性的","s":"The company changed its discriminatory rules after many complaints.","t":"在許多投訴之後，公司修改了帶有歧視性的規定。"},{"w":"discuss","p":"v.","d":"to talk about something with another person or in a group","c":"討論","s":"Let's discuss the plan for the school fair after lunch.","t":"午餐後我們來討論園遊會的計畫吧。"},{"w":"discussion","p":"n.","d":"the action or process of talking about something to reach a decision","c":"討論","s":"After two hours of lively class discussion, students finally reached a consensus on the topic of their science project.","t":"經過兩小時熱烈的課堂______後，學生們終於就他們的科學專案主題達成了共識。"},{"w":"discussable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be talked about","c":"可討論的","s":"Our group discussed the project for two hours but still couldn't agree on a topic.","t":"我們組討論專題兩小時，還是無法決定主題。"},{"w":"display","p":"v./n.","d":"to show something for people to see","c":"展示；陳列；表演","s":"The fireworks display at Taipei 101 on New Year's Eve lasted about five minutes.","t":"跨年夜台北101的煙火秀持續了大約五分鐘。"},{"w":"on display","p":"phr.","d":"put out for people to see","c":"展出中","s":"The students' paintings about Taiwan's beautiful mountains are _____ _____ in the school hall, and parents can visit them this week.","t":""},{"w":"distant","p":"adj.","d":"far away","c":"遙遠的；遠親的","s":"Light from distant galaxies takes billions of years to reach us, so we see them as they were long ago.","t":"來自遙遠星系的光需要數十億年才能到達我們這裡，所以我們看到的是它們很久以前的樣子。"},{"w":"distance","p":"n.","d":"the amount of space between two points or places","c":"距離；遠處","s":"The distance between Taipei and Kaohsiung is about 350 kilometers.","t":"台北到高雄的距離大約350公里。"},{"w":"distantly","p":"adv.","d":"from far away; not closely related","c":"遠遠地；（親戚）遠房地","s":"Ken and I are distantly related; his grandmother was my grandfather's cousin.","t":"Ken 和我是遠房親戚，他的奶奶是我爺爺的表姊妹。"},{"w":"distract","p":"v.","d":"to take someone's attention away from what they are doing","c":"使分心","s":"The noise from the street distracted me while I was studying.","t":"街上的噪音讓我讀書時分心。"},{"w":"distraction","p":"n.","d":"something that takes your attention away from what you are doing","c":"使人分心的事物","s":"My phone is my biggest distraction, so I leave it in another room when I need to finish my homework.","t":"手機是最讓我分心的東西，所以需要寫完作業時我會把它放在另一個房間。"},{"w":"distracted","p":"adj.","d":"not able to pay attention because you are thinking of other things","c":"分心的","s":"Amy looked distracted during the meeting and kept checking her phone.","t":"Amy 開會時看起來心不在焉，一直看手機。"},{"w":"distracting","p":"adj.","d":"taking your attention away from what you are doing","c":"令人分心的","s":"The loud music from next door kept distracting me while I was trying to study for the test.","t":"我努力準備考試時，隔壁的大聲音樂一直讓我分心。"},{"w":"distribute","p":"v.","d":"to give things out to a number of people","c":"分發；分配","s":"The organization will distribute food to those in need.","t":"該組織將向有需要的人分發食物。"},{"w":"distribution","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving things out; the way things are spread","c":"分發；分布","s":"The Red Cross is in charge of the distribution of food and water after the typhoon.","t":"颱風過後，紅十字會負責分發食物和飲水。"},{"w":"distributor","p":"n.","d":"a company that delivers goods from producers to shops","c":"經銷商","s":"The milk distributor delivers to over two hundred stores every morning, so his trucks leave the factory before dawn.","t":"這家牛奶經銷商每天早上配送到兩百多家商店，所以他的貨車天亮前就離開工廠。"},{"w":"disturb","p":"v.","d":"to interrupt someone or stop them from being calm","c":"打擾","s":"Please don't disturb me; I'm studying for the exam.","t":"請別打擾我，我在準備考試。"},{"w":"disturbance","p":"n.","d":"something that interrupts or upsets people; noisy or violent behavior","c":"干擾；騷動","s":"The solar storm caused a disturbance to phone signals, so some people could not make calls for a few hours.","t":"太陽風暴對手機訊號造成了干擾，所以有些人好幾個小時無法打電話。"},{"w":"disturbing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel worried or upset","c":"令人不安的","s":"The news report showed some disturbing pictures of the war.","t":"新聞報導播出一些令人不安的戰爭畫面。"},{"w":"disturbed","p":"adj.","d":"worried or upset","c":"心煩的","s":"She was deeply disturbed by the strange phone calls she kept receiving late at night from an unknown number.","t":"她對深夜不斷接到來自不明號碼的奇怪電話感到非常不安。"},{"w":"dominate","p":"v.","d":"to control or be the most important thing in something","c":"支配；主宰","s":"The company continues to dominate in the tech industry.","t":"該公司繼續在科技行業佔據主導地位。"},{"w":"dominant","p":"adj.","d":"more powerful or important than others","c":"佔優勢的","s":"The dominant theme of the conference was sustainability.","t":"會議的主要主題是可持續性。"},{"w":"dominance","p":"n.","d":"the state of being the most powerful","c":"優勢；支配","s":"The team's dominance of the league finally ended last season.","t":"這支球隊在聯盟的霸主地位在上個賽季終於結束。"},{"w":"drama","p":"n.","d":"a play or show","c":"戲劇；劇情","s":"The drama tells a story of love and betrayal.","t":"戲劇講述了一個關於愛與背叛的故事。"},{"w":"dramatic","p":"adj.","d":"exciting or sudden","c":"戲劇性的；巨大的","s":"The dramatic change in weather conditions affected their plans.","t":"戲劇性的天氣變化影響了他們的計劃。"},{"w":"dramatically","p":"adv.","d":"in a very large or sudden way","c":"大幅地","s":"Sales have increased dramatically since the new marketing campaign was launched.","t":"自新的營銷活動推出以來，銷售額戲劇性地增加了。"},{"w":"dramatize","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem more exciting than it is; to turn into a play","c":"戲劇化","s":"Don't dramatize the situation; it's just a small mistake.","t":"別把情況誇大，那只是個小錯誤。"},{"w":"eager","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to do something very much","c":"渴望的；熱切的","s":"Max is an eager learner who always asks questions in class.","t":"Max 是個熱衷學習的學生，上課總是發問。"},{"w":"eagerly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you really want to do or have something","c":"熱切地","s":"The children waited eagerly for Santa Claus to appear at the school party.","t":"孩子們熱切地等待聖誕老公公出現在學校派對上。"},{"w":"eagerness","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to do something","c":"渴望；熱切","s":"Her eagerness to learn impressed all of the teachers at the summer camp.","t":"她的求知欲讓夏令營的所有老師印象深刻。"},{"w":"economy","p":"n.","d":"the system of money, trade, and industry in a country","c":"經濟","s":"The global economy has been affected by the pandemic.","t":"全球經濟受到了大流行的影響。"},{"w":"economic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with trade, industry, and money","c":"經濟（上）的","s":"The economic situation in the country is improving.","t":"該國的經濟形勢正在改善。"},{"w":"economical","p":"adj.","d":"not using a lot of money, fuel, or time; cheap to use","c":"節省的；划算的","s":"It's more economical to buy groceries in bulk.","t":"批量購買雜貨更為省錢。"},{"w":"economist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies or writes about economics","c":"經濟學家","s":"My cousin studied finance and now works as an economist at a bank.","t":"我表哥念財金，現在在銀行擔任經濟學家。"},{"w":"economically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way related to the economy","c":"經濟上","s":"Taiwan has become economically strong thanks to its chip industry.","t":"多虧晶片產業，台灣在經濟上變得強大。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"edit – engage · 15 字族 · 34 題","cards":[{"w":"edit","p":"v.","d":"to correct and improve writing","c":"編輯","s":"Before publishing, it's essential to edit the manuscript carefully to ensure accuracy and clarity.","t":"在出版之前，必須仔細編輯稿件以確保準確性和清晰度。"},{"w":"edition","p":"n.","d":"one printing of a book","c":"版本","s":"The latest edition of the software has several new features that enhance user experience.","t":"軟件的最新版本具有多個增強用戶體驗的新功能。"},{"w":"editor","p":"n.","d":"a person who checks and decides what is published","c":"編輯（人）","s":"Lucy wants to be the editor of the school newspaper next year.","t":"Lucy 明年想當校刊的編輯。"},{"w":"editorial","p":"n./adj.","d":"an article in a newspaper that gives the editor's opinion","c":"社論；編輯的","s":"Today's editorial criticises the government's new housing plan, and many readers have written letters to agree with it.","t":"今天的社論批評政府的新住宅計畫，而許多讀者寫信表示贊同。"},{"w":"educate","p":"v.","d":"to teach or train someone.","c":"教育","s":"The government aims to educate children on environmental issues.","t":"政府旨在教育兒童有關環境問題。"},{"w":"education","p":"n.","d":"the process of receiving or giving systematic instruction, especially at school","c":"教育","s":"The government invested millions of tax dollars into public education, ensuring that every rural school has modern computers.","t":"政府在公共______方面投入了數百萬稅收，確保每所偏鄉學校都能擁有現代化的電腦。"},{"w":"educational","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the provision of education; intended or serving to educate or enlighten.","c":"有教育意義的","s":"The long historical movie was certainly highly educational, but unfortunately, absolutely all the young energetic students thought it was incredibly boring.","t":"這部長篇歷史電影確實高度有教育意義的，但不幸的是，絕對所有年輕充滿活力的學生都認為它極其無聊。"},{"w":"educated","p":"adj.","d":"having received a good education","c":"受過教育的","s":"Both of my parents are highly educated; my mom has a PhD in chemistry.","t":"我父母都受過高等教育；我媽媽有化學博士學位。"},{"w":"educator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is teaching or education","c":"教育家","s":"Ms. Lin is an experienced educator who has taught English for twenty years.","t":"林老師是一位有經驗的教育者，教英文已二十年。"},{"w":"effect","p":"n.","d":"a change or result caused by something","c":"影響；效果","s":"Too much screen time can have a negative effect on your eyes.","t":"太長的螢幕時間會對你的眼睛造成負面影響。"},{"w":"effective","p":"adj.","d":"producing the result you want","c":"有效的","s":"This medicine is very effective against headaches.","t":"這藥對頭痛非常有效。"},{"w":"effectively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that works well","c":"有效地","s":"Studying with a friend can help you learn more effectively.","t":"和朋友一起讀書可以幫助你更有效地學習。"},{"w":"ineffective","p":"adj.","d":"not producing the result you want","c":"無效的","s":"The first medicine was ineffective, so the doctor gave her a stronger one.","t":"第一種藥沒有效，所以醫生給她更強的藥。"},{"w":"efficient","p":"adj.","d":"working well without wasting time or energy","c":"有效率的","s":"The new train system is fast and efficient.","t":"新的火車系統快速又有效率。"},{"w":"efficiency","p":"n.","d":"the quality of doing something well without wasting time or energy","c":"效率","s":"The delivery company uses AI to plan routes, and this efficiency saves fuel and gets parcels to customers sooner.","t":"這家物流公司用人工智慧規劃路線,這樣的效率能節省燃料,並讓包裹更快送到顧客手上。"},{"w":"efficiently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that does not waste time or money","c":"有效率地","s":"If you plan your time efficiently, you'll have more time to relax.","t":"如果你有效率地安排時間，就會有更多時間放鬆。"},{"w":"inefficient","p":"adj.","d":"wasting time, energy or money","c":"沒效率的","s":"Old air conditioners are inefficient and use too much electricity.","t":"舊冷氣效率差又太耗電。"},{"w":"elder","p":"adj./n.","d":"born earlier; senior; older person in a family or tribe","c":"年長的；長者","s":"My elder sister is studying medicine at a university in Kaohsiung.","t":"我姊姊在高雄一所大學念醫學系。"},{"w":"elderly","p":"adj.","d":"old","c":"年長的","s":"Please give your seat to elderly passengers on the MRT.","t":"搭捷運時請讓座給年長的乘客。"},{"w":"the elderly","p":"n.","d":"elderly · A 抽象/延伸義","c":"老年人","s":"My elder sister is studying medicine at a university in Kaohsiung.","t":"我姊姊在高雄一所大學念醫學系。"},{"w":"eldest","p":"adj.","d":"oldest of three or more people","c":"最年長的","s":"As the eldest of five children, Grace often helped her mother cook dinner.","t":"身為五個孩子中的老大，Grace 常幫媽媽煮晚餐。"},{"w":"elegant","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and graceful in style","c":"優雅的","s":"Grandma's old qipao is simple but elegant, with fine silk and neat buttons.","t":"奶奶的舊旗袍簡單卻優雅，絲質細緻、釦子整齊。"},{"w":"elegance","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being graceful and stylish","c":"優雅","s":"The dancer moved with great elegance, so the audience hardly noticed how difficult the steps were.","t":"這位舞者的動作極為優雅,所以觀眾幾乎沒察覺舞步有多困難。"},{"w":"elegantly","p":"adv.","d":"in a graceful and attractive way","c":"優雅地","s":"The bride walked elegantly down the aisle in a long white dress.","t":"新娘穿著白色長禮服優雅地走過紅毯。"},{"w":"elevate","p":"v.","d":"to lift something up; to make something higher or better","c":"提升；舉起","s":"Many families elevate their houses on concrete posts, so floodwater can pass underneath without entering the rooms.","t":"許多家庭把房子架高在混凝土柱上,讓洪水可以從下方流過而不會進到房間。"},{"w":"elevated","p":"adj.","d":"raised above the ground; higher than usual","c":"高架的；提高的","s":"The new MRT line runs on an elevated track above the road.","t":"新的捷運線行駛在道路上方的高架軌道上。"},{"w":"elevation","p":"n.","d":"the height of a place above the sea","c":"海拔；升遷","s":"This oolong tea is grown at an elevation of 2,000 meters in the mountains.","t":"這種烏龍茶種植在海拔兩千公尺的山區。"},{"w":"elevator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that carries people up and down in a building","c":"電梯","s":"The elevator made tall buildings possible, because nobody wanted to climb twenty floors every day.","t":"電梯讓高樓成為可能,因為沒有人想每天爬二十層樓。"},{"w":"eloquent","p":"adj.","d":"able to speak or write well and persuade people","c":"有說服力的；口才好的","s":"The class president gave an eloquent speech at the graduation ceremony.","t":"班長在畢業典禮上發表了一場動人的演說。"},{"w":"eloquently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is clear, strong, and persuasive","c":"雄辯地；流利動人地","s":"Ting-yu spoke eloquently about the importance of protecting sea turtles.","t":"庭宇流暢動人地談論保護海龜的重要性。"},{"w":"eloquence","p":"n.","d":"the ability to speak or write well and persuade people","c":"口才；雄辯","s":"Even shy students can develop eloquence by practicing speaking a little every day.","t":"即使是害羞的學生，只要每天練習說一點，也能培養口才。"},{"w":"embarrass","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel shy, ashamed, or uncomfortable","c":"使尷尬","s":"Please don't embarrass me by showing my baby photos to my friends.","t":"拜託別拿我的嬰兒照給朋友看讓我丟臉。"},{"w":"embarrassed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling shy, ashamed, or uncomfortable","c":"（人）尷尬的","s":"My dad embarrassed me by dancing in front of my classmates at the school fair.","t":"我爸爸在園遊會上當著同學的面跳舞，讓我很尷尬。"},{"w":"embarrassing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel embarrassed","c":"令人尷尬的","s":"It was really embarrassing to forget my lines on stage, but the audience was kind and clapped anyway.","t":"在台上忘詞真的很令人尷尬，但觀眾很友善，還是給了掌聲。"},{"w":"embarrassment","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being shy or uncomfortable in front of others","c":"尷尬","s":"Her face turned red with embarrassment when she called her teacher \"Mum\" by mistake, but everyone laughed kindly.","t":"她不小心把老師叫成「媽媽」時,臉因為尷尬而漲紅,但大家都善意地笑了。"},{"w":"emotion","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling such as joy, sorrow, love, or anger","c":"情感；情緒","s":"When the Olympic champion stood on the medal podium, she was overwhelmed with strong emotion and wept tears of joy.","t":"當這位奧運冠軍站在獎牌頒獎台上時，她內心湧現出強烈澎湃的情緒，流下了喜悅的淚水。"},{"w":"emotional","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a person's inner feelings and heart.","c":"情緒的；易動感情的","s":"Grandpa got very emotional when he saw his old classmates after fifty years.","t":"爺爺五十年後見到老同學時非常激動。"},{"w":"emotionally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to feelings","c":"情緒上","s":"Moving to a new city can be emotionally difficult for young children.","t":"搬到新城市對年幼孩子來說可能在情緒上很辛苦。"},{"w":"employ","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a job and pay them","c":"雇用","s":"The new factory will employ more than 300 local workers.","t":"新工廠將雇用三百多名在地員工。"},{"w":"employment","p":"n.","d":"having paid work","c":"就業；雇用","s":"AI may reduce employment in some office jobs, but it is also creating new jobs that did not exist ten years ago.","t":"人工智慧可能會減少某些辦公室工作的就業機會,但它也創造了十年前不存在的新工作。"},{"w":"employee","p":"n.","d":"a person employed for wages or salary, especially at non-executive level","c":"員工","s":"The generous manufacturing firm offered every hardworking employee a generous year-end bonus and three weeks of paid leave.","t":"這家慷慨的製造業公司為每位辛勤工作的員工提供了優厚的年終獎金和三週的有薪假。"},{"w":"employer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that pays people to work","c":"雇主","s":"Many employers now ask whether job seekers can use AI tools, so students should learn these skills before graduating.","t":"許多雇主現在會詢問求職者是否會使用人工智慧工具,所以學生應該在畢業前學會這些技能。"},{"w":"unemployment","p":"n.","d":"the state of not having a job; the number of people without jobs","c":"失業","s":"Some experts fear that unemployment will rise as machines take over simple tasks, while others expect new kinds of work to appear.","t":"有些專家擔心隨著機器接手簡單的工作,失業率會上升,而其他人則預期會出現新型態的工作。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone hope and support","c":"鼓勵","s":"They encourage each other to keep pursuing their dreams.","t":"他們互相鼓勵，繼續追求自己的夢想。"},{"w":"encouragement","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that give hope","c":"鼓勵","s":"With a little encouragement, he felt ready to try again.","t":"在一些鼓勵的支持下，他覺得準備好再次嘗試。"},{"w":"encouraging","p":"adj.","d":"giving hope and support","c":"鼓舞人心的","s":"The coach's encouraging words helped the team keep fighting until the end.","t":"教練鼓舞人心的話幫助球隊奮戰到最後。"},{"w":"discourage","p":"v.","d":"to make someone lose hope or confidence","c":"使氣餒；勸阻","s":"Don't let one bad score discourage you, because every learner has difficult days and you can still improve.","t":"不要讓一次糟糕的分數使你灰心,因為每個學習者都有不順的日子,而你仍然可以進步。"},{"w":"endure","p":"v.","d":"to suffer something painful or difficult for a long time","c":"忍受；持久","s":"Athletes must endure hours of hard training, but the joy of winning makes the pain worthwhile for many of them.","t":"運動員必須忍受好幾個小時的艱苦訓練,但對許多人來說,勝利的喜悅讓這些痛苦都值得。"},{"w":"endurance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to keep doing something difficult for a long time","c":"耐力","s":"Cycling to school every day built up my endurance, so I finished the five-kilometre fun run without stopping once.","t":"每天騎腳踏車上學增強了我的耐力，所以我一次都沒停就跑完了五公里的趣味路跑。"},{"w":"enduring","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time","c":"持久的","s":"Their enduring friendship began in elementary school.","t":"他們持久的友誼始於小學。"},{"w":"unendurable","p":"adj.","d":"too painful or bad to bear","c":"無法忍受的","s":"The heat in the classroom was almost unendurable without air conditioning.","t":"沒有冷氣，教室的悶熱幾乎讓人無法忍受。"},{"w":"energy","p":"n.","d":"power used to make machines work","c":"能量；精力","s":"After a long day at school, I have no energy left to do my homework.","t":"在學校待了一整天，我已經沒力氣寫作業了。"},{"w":"energetic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy","c":"精力充沛的","s":"Even after a long day, she remains energetic and enthusiastic.","t":"即使經過漫長的一天，她仍然保持充滿活力和熱情。"},{"w":"energetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows a lot of energy","c":"精力充沛地","s":"The kids danced energetically to the music at the school festival.","t":"孩子們在校慶上隨著音樂賣力跳舞。"},{"w":"energize","p":"v.","d":"to give energy to someone or something","c":"使充滿活力","s":"The motivational speech seemed to energize the entire team.","t":"激勵性的演講似乎為整個團隊注入了能量。"},{"w":"engage","p":"v.","d":"to take part in; to attract and keep interest","c":"參與；吸引","s":"Students learn more when they actively engage in class activities.","t":"學生主動參與課堂活動時學得更多。"},{"w":"engaged","p":"adj.","d":"having agreed to marry someone","c":"訂婚的；忙於","s":"My cousin and her boyfriend got engaged last month and will marry next spring.","t":"我表姊和男友上個月訂婚，明年春天結婚。"},{"w":"engagement","p":"n.","d":"an agreement to marry; the time before the wedding","c":"訂婚；參與","s":"They announced their engagement at the family dinner, and Grandma cried with happiness when she saw the ring.","t":"他們在家庭聚餐上宣布訂婚，奶奶看到戒指時高興得哭了。"},{"w":"engaging","p":"adj.","d":"charming and attractive; capturing attention.","c":"吸引人的","s":"Ms. Wang is an engaging speaker who keeps everyone listening until the end.","t":"王老師是位很吸引人的講者，讓大家聽到最後。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"entertain – except · 15 字族 · 34 題","cards":[{"w":"entertain","p":"v.","d":"to amuse people; to have guests at your home","c":"使娛樂；招待","s":"The company refused to entertain any suggestions from new workers.","t":"公司拒絕考慮新進員工的任何建議。"},{"w":"entertainment","p":"n.","d":"activities, shows, or performances that people enjoy.","c":"娛樂","s":"The theme park offers various forms of entertainment.","t":"這個主題公園提供各種形式的娛樂。"},{"w":"entertaining","p":"adj.","d":"enjoyable and fun to watch, hear, or do.","c":"有趣的；令人愉快的","s":"Mr. Huang's history class is so entertaining that nobody ever falls asleep in it.","t":"黃老師的歷史課很有趣，從來沒人打瞌睡。"},{"w":"entertainer","p":"n.","d":"a person who performs to amuse an audience.","c":"表演者；藝人","s":"The entertainer captivated the audience with his performance.","t":"這位藝人以他的表演吸引了觀眾。"},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of interest and excitement","c":"熱忱","s":"The students showed great enthusiasm for the science fair, so they stayed after school to build their projects.","t":"學生們對科展展現極大的熱忱,所以他們放學後留下來製作作品。"},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lot of excitement and interest about something","c":"熱衷的","s":"The students were enthusiastic about the school trip to Green Island.","t":"學生們對去綠島的校外教學充滿熱情。"},{"w":"enthusiastically","p":"adv.","d":"with a lot of interest and excitement","c":"熱情地","s":"The whole class clapped enthusiastically on Friday when Amy finished her speech about protecting sea turtles.","t":"星期五當艾咪結束關於保護海龜的演講時，全班熱情地鼓掌。"},{"w":"enthusiast","p":"n.","d":"a person who is very interested in an activity","c":"愛好者","s":"My father is a jazz enthusiast who owns over a thousand records.","t":"我爸爸是爵士樂迷，擁有一千多張唱片。"},{"w":"environment","p":"n.","d":"the air, water and land around us","c":"環境","s":"Plastic bags are bad for the environment because they take hundreds of years to break down.","t":"塑膠袋對環境有害，因為它們要好幾百年才會分解。"},{"w":"environmental","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the natural world and surroundings","c":"環境的","s":"Some illnesses come from genes, but others are caused by environmental factors like dirty air.","t":"有些疾病來自基因，但其他疾病是由像髒空氣這樣的環境的因素所造成的。"},{"w":"environmentally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to nature and the environment","c":"在環境方面","s":"More and more shops in Taiwan are offering environmentally friendly straws made of glass or bamboo.","t":"台灣越來越多店家提供玻璃或竹子做的環保吸管。"},{"w":"environmentalist","p":"n.","d":"a person who works to protect nature","c":"環保人士","s":"Plastic bags are bad for the environment because they take hundreds of years to break down.","t":"塑膠袋對環境有害，因為它們要好幾百年才會分解。"},{"w":"equal","p":"adj./v.","d":"the same in quantity, size, or value; to be the same as","c":"平等的；等於","s":"Both teams scored equal points, so the game went into overtime.","t":"兩隊分數相同，所以比賽進入延長賽。"},{"w":"equality","p":"n.","d":"the state of having the same rights and chances as others","c":"平等","s":"The charity works for equality in health care, so that poor families receive the same treatment as rich ones.","t":"這個慈善團體致力於醫療平等,讓貧困家庭獲得和富裕家庭相同的治療。"},{"w":"equally","p":"adv.","d":"to the same degree","c":"平等地；同樣地","s":"A good teacher treats all students equally, no matter how well they do in class.","t":"好老師不論成績好壞都平等對待所有學生。"},{"w":"unequal","p":"adj.","d":"not fair or the same for everyone","c":"不平等的","s":"In some countries, the pay between men and women is still very unequal.","t":"在某些國家，男女薪資仍非常不平等。"},{"w":"equip","p":"v.","d":"to provide someone or something with what is needed","c":"裝備；使具備","s":"The program aims to equip young people with the skills they need for future jobs.","t":"這個計畫旨在讓年輕人具備未來工作所需的技能。"},{"w":"equipment","p":"n.","d":"tools or machines used for a job","c":"設備（不可數）","s":"Proper maintenance of equipment is essential for ensuring long-term functionality.","t":"正確維護設備對於確保長期功能至關重要。"},{"w":"equipped","p":"adj.","d":"having the tools or things that are needed","c":"配備…的","s":"The new hospital is equipped with the latest medical machines.","t":"新醫院配備了最新的醫療儀器。"},{"w":"escape","p":"v./n.","d":"a way of forgetting about daily problems or a stressful situation for a short time","c":"逃脫；逃避","s":"The prisoner made a daring escape through a hole in the wall.","t":"那名囚犯從牆上的洞大膽逃脫。"},{"w":"escaped","p":"adj.","d":"having got away from a place","c":"逃脫的","s":"The prisoner made a daring escape through a hole in the wall.","t":"那名囚犯從牆上的洞大膽逃脫。"},{"w":"escaping","p":"v.","d":"getting away from a dangerous place","c":"逃離（V-ing）","s":"Reading novels is my favorite way of escaping from stress.","t":"看小說是我最喜歡的抒壓方式。"},{"w":"establish","p":"v.","d":"to start or create an organization, system, or relationship","c":"建立；設立","s":"The city government plans to establish more bike lanes along the river.","t":"市政府計畫沿河設立更多自行車道。"},{"w":"establishment","p":"n.","d":"the act of starting something; an organization","c":"建立；機構","s":"The establishment of new parks benefits the community.","t":"新公園的建立對社區有益。"},{"w":"established","p":"adj.","d":"well known and accepted for a long time","c":"已確立的；知名的","s":"Our school was established in 1965.","t":"我們學校創立於 1965 年。"},{"w":"estimate","p":"v./n.","d":"to guess the size, amount, or cost of something","c":"估計","s":"According to one estimate, about 2,000 people joined the beach cleanup.","t":"據一項估計，約有兩千人參加了淨灘活動。"},{"w":"estimated","p":"adj.","d":"guessed, not exact","c":"估計的","s":"The estimated arrival time is 5 pm.","t":"估計的到達時間是下午5點。"},{"w":"underestimate","p":"v.","d":"to think that something or someone is smaller, weaker, or less important than they really are","c":"低估","s":"Never underestimate the power of a good night's sleep, because tired students make many more careless mistakes on tests.","t":"絕不要低估一夜好眠的力量，因為疲倦的學生在考試中會犯更多粗心的錯誤。"},{"w":"overestimate","p":"v.","d":"to think something is bigger or better than it is","c":"高估","s":"Students often overestimate how much they can study in one night, and then they feel disappointed when they cannot finish.","t":"學生常常高估自己一個晚上能讀多少,結果讀不完時就感到失望。"},{"w":"ethics","p":"n.","d":"moral rules about what is right and wrong","c":"倫理；道德規範","s":"Our class discussed the ethics of using AI in hospitals, because a wrong decision by a machine could hurt a patient.","t":"我們班討論了在醫院使用人工智慧的倫理問題,因為機器做出錯誤決定可能會傷害病人。"},{"w":"ethical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with right and wrong; morally right","c":"合乎道德的；倫理的","s":"It's important to make ethical decisions in business to maintain a good reputation.","t":"在商業中做出倫理決策以維護良好的聲譽非常重要。"},{"w":"unethical","p":"adj.","d":"morally wrong; not following the rules of right behavior","c":"不道德的","s":"Copying a classmate's report and handing it in as your own is unethical.","t":"抄同學的報告當成自己的交出去是不道德的。"},{"w":"ethically","p":"adv.","d":"in a morally right way","c":"合乎道德地","s":"This café promises that all of its coffee beans are ethically produced.","t":"這家咖啡店保證所有咖啡豆都是以合乎道德的方式生產的。"},{"w":"evaluate","p":"v.","d":"to judge how good, useful, or successful something is","c":"評估；評量","s":"It is not easy for teachers to evaluate students' speaking skills fairly.","t":"老師要公平地評量學生的口說能力並不容易。"},{"w":"evaluation","p":"n.","d":"a judgment about how good or useful something is","c":"評估；評量","s":"The teacher gave an evaluation of each student's performance.","t":"老師評價了每個學生的表現。"},{"w":"eventual","p":"adj.","d":"happening at the end of a process","c":"最終的","s":"Nobody expected the shy girl to be the eventual winner of the singing contest.","t":"沒有人料到那個害羞的女孩會是歌唱比賽最後的贏家。"},{"w":"eventually","p":"adv.","d":"in the end","c":"最後；終於","s":"After hours of searching, we eventually found my cat sleeping under the neighbor's car.","t":"找了好幾個小時後，我們終於發現我的貓睡在鄰居的車底下。"},{"w":"evidence","p":"n.","d":"facts or signs that show something is true","c":"證據","s":"The police found no evidence that the man had been at the scene.","t":"警方找不到那名男子曾在現場的證據。"},{"w":"evident","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see or understand; clear","c":"明顯的","s":"His love for cooking is evident in every dish he makes.","t":"他對烹飪的熱愛在他做的每道菜裡都顯而易見。"},{"w":"evidently","p":"adv.","d":"clearly; it is easy to see that","c":"顯然地","s":"Evidently, nobody had cleaned the kitchen for weeks; there were dirty dishes everywhere.","t":"顯然好幾週沒人打掃廚房了；到處都是髒碗盤。"},{"w":"exaggerate","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem bigger or better than it really is","c":"誇大","s":"People under stress often exaggerate their problems, so talking to a friend can help them see things more clearly.","t":"處於壓力下的人常常誇大自己的問題,所以和朋友聊聊可以幫助他們看得更清楚。"},{"w":"exaggeration","p":"n.","d":"a statement that makes something seem bigger, better, or worse than it really is","c":"誇大","s":"It is no exaggeration to say that the night market is the most popular place in town on a Saturday evening.","t":"說夜市是週六晚上鎮上最受歡迎的地方，一點也不誇張。"},{"w":"exaggerated","p":"adj.","d":"made to seem bigger or more important than it is","c":"誇張的","s":"The fisherman exaggerated the size of the fish he caught; it was actually quite small.","t":"漁夫誇大了他釣到的魚的大小；其實那條魚很小。"},{"w":"excel","p":"v.","d":"to be extremely good at something","c":"擅長；勝過","s":"Some students excel in exams, while others perform better in projects, so teachers should use different kinds of tests.","t":"有些學生在考試中表現優異,而有些人在專題中表現更好,所以老師應該使用不同類型的評量。"},{"w":"excellent","p":"adj.","d":"very, very good","c":"優秀的","s":"Q: Amy got 100 on the math test. — A: What an excellent student she is!","t":"艾美數學考了一百分。 — 她真是個優秀的學生！"},{"w":"excellence","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being extremely good","c":"卓越","s":"The school won an award for excellence in science teaching.","t":"這所學校因科學教學卓越而獲獎。"},{"w":"excellently","p":"adv.","d":"in a very good way","c":"極好地","s":"Wendy excels at languages; she speaks English, Japanese and Korean.","t":"溫蒂擅長語言，會說英、日、韓語。"},{"w":"except","p":"prep.","d":"but not; not including","c":"除了","s":"Everyone in our group went to the beach except Amy, who had a cold.","t":"除了感冒的艾咪，我們這組每個人都去了海邊。"},{"w":"exception","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that is not included in a rule","c":"例外","s":"Most mammals do not lay eggs, but the platypus is an exception, and that surprised early scientists.","t":"大多數哺乳類動物不會下蛋，但鴨嘴獸是例外，而這讓早期的科學家很驚訝。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"unusually good; much better than usual","c":"傑出的；例外的","s":"She showed exceptional calm during the emergency, and her quick thinking helped everyone leave the building safely.","t":"她在緊急狀況中展現了非凡的冷靜,她的機智幫助大家安全離開大樓。"},{"w":"exceptionally","p":"adv.","d":"unusually; to a very great degree","c":"格外地","s":"The weather was exceptionally hot for late October, so we went swimming.","t":"以十月底來說天氣格外炎熱，所以我們去游泳。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"excess – faith · 15 字族 · 33 題","cards":[{"w":"excess","p":"n./adj.","d":"an amount that is more than needed","c":"過量；過量的","s":"Eating sugar in excess can lead to health problems.","t":"攝取過量的糖可能導致健康問題。"},{"w":"excessive","p":"adj.","d":"more than is necessary, normal, or reasonable","c":"過度的","s":"Excessive use of smartphones can harm your eyes.","t":"過度使用智慧型手機會傷害眼睛。"},{"w":"excessively","p":"adv.","d":"too much","c":"過度地","s":"He was fined for driving excessively fast near the school.","t":"他因在學校附近開車過快而被罰款。"},{"w":"exceed","p":"v.","d":"to be greater than a number or amount; to go beyond a limit","c":"超過","s":"Your bag must not exceed 7 kilograms on this flight.","t":"這班飛機上你的包包不能超過七公斤。"},{"w":"exchange","p":"v./n.","d":"to give something to someone and receive something from them","c":"交換","s":"We need to exchange ideas to improve our strategy.","t":"我們需要交換意見來改進我們的策略。"},{"w":"exchangeable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be traded for something else","c":"可交換的","s":"Sorry, this gift card is not exchangeable for cash; you can only use it in our stores.","t":"抱歉，這張禮物卡不能兌換現金，只能在本店使用。"},{"w":"exchange student","p":"n.","d":"a student who studies in another country for a short time","c":"交換學生","s":"An exchange student from Germany joined our class, and we taught her how to use chopsticks.","t":"一位來自德國的交換學生加入我們班，而我們教她怎麼用筷子。"},{"w":"execute","p":"v.","d":"to do or carry out a plan, order, or piece of work","c":"處決；執行","s":"In the past, criminals were executed in public.","t":"過去罪犯會被公開處決。"},{"w":"execution","p":"n.","d":"the carrying out of a plan; the killing of someone as a punishment","c":"處決；執行","s":"The idea for the school festival was wonderful, but its execution was poor because nobody checked the weather or booked the equipment.","t":"校慶的構想很棒，但執行得很差，因為沒有人查天氣，也沒有人預訂設備。"},{"w":"executive","p":"n.","d":"a senior manager in a company or organization","c":"主管；高階經理","s":"She works as a marketing executive for a big phone company.","t":"她在一家大型手機公司擔任行銷主管。"},{"w":"exhaust","p":"v./n.","d":"to make someone very tired; to use something up completely","c":"耗盡；廢氣","s":"If we keep using water like this, we will soon exhaust our supply.","t":"如果我們繼續這樣用水，很快就會把存水用完。"},{"w":"exhaustion","p":"n.","d":"the state of being extremely tired","c":"筋疲力盡","s":"After three nights of little sleep, Tom was suffering from exhaustion, and his doctor told him to rest for a few days.","t":"連續三晚睡得很少之後,湯姆陷入筋疲力盡的狀態,醫生要他休息幾天。"},{"w":"exhausted","p":"adj.","d":"extremely tired","c":"筋疲力盡的","s":"After climbing Hehuanshan, we were completely exhausted.","t":"爬完合歡山後，我們累壞了。"},{"w":"exhausting","p":"adj.","d":"making you extremely tired","c":"令人疲憊的","s":"Taking care of three kids all day is really exhausting.","t":"整天照顧三個小孩真的很累人。"},{"w":"exhibit","p":"v./n.","d":"to show something in a public place","c":"展出；展品","s":"The museum will exhibit new artifacts next month.","t":"博物館將在下個月展示新的文物。"},{"w":"exhibition","p":"n.","d":"a public show of art or objects","c":"展覽","s":"The annual art exhibition showcases works from local artists.","t":"年度藝術展覽展示了當地藝術家的作品。"},{"w":"exhibitor","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that shows things at a show","c":"參展者","s":"Over fifty artists are exhibiting their works at the Taipei art fair this week.","t":"本週有五十多位藝術家在台北藝博會展出作品。"},{"w":"exist","p":"v.","d":"to be real; to be in the world","c":"存在","s":"Some people believe that life may exist on other planets.","t":"有些人相信其他星球上可能有生命存在。"},{"w":"existence","p":"n.","d":"the state of being real or alive","c":"存在","s":"Scientists doubted the existence of the giant squid for years, until someone finally filmed one in 2004.","t":"科學家多年來一直懷疑大王魷的存在，直到2004年終於有人拍到了一隻。"},{"w":"existing","p":"adj.","d":"that is already there now","c":"現有的","s":"Some people believe that life may exist on other planets.","t":"有些人相信其他星球上可能有生命存在。"},{"w":"existent","p":"adj.","d":"currently real or existing right now.","c":"存在的","s":"The committee reviewed all existent policies before deciding which ones needed to be updated or removed entirely.","t":"委員會審查了所有現存的政策，然後決定哪些需要更新或完全廢除。"},{"w":"expand","p":"v.","d":"to become larger or make something larger","c":"擴大；擴張","s":"Reading widely can help you expand your vocabulary.","t":"廣泛閱讀能幫你擴充字彙。"},{"w":"expansion","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming larger","c":"擴張","s":"The city is experiencing rapid expansion due to the influx of businesses.","t":"由於業務湧入，該市正在經歷迅速的擴張。"},{"w":"expansive","p":"adj.","d":"covering a large area","c":"廣闊的","s":"The estate offers an expansive view of the mountains.","t":"該莊園提供了山脈的廣闊景觀。"},{"w":"expect","p":"v.","d":"to think that something will happen","c":"期待；預期","s":"Q: Do you think you can do well on the test? — A: Yes, I do. I expect to get a good grade.","t":"你覺得你考試會考好嗎？ — 會，我期待拿到好成績。"},{"w":"expectation","p":"n.","d":"a belief about what someone should achieve","c":"期望","s":"Her parents had high expectation for her, but they never stopped her from choosing art as her major.","t":"她父母對她有很高的期望，但他們從未阻止她選擇藝術當主修。"},{"w":"expected","p":"adj.","d":"thought likely to happen","c":"預期的","s":"The final exam was easier than I had expected.","t":"期末考比我預期的簡單。"},{"w":"unexpected","p":"adj.","d":"surprising and not planned","c":"意外的","s":"The results were unexpected, because the \"lazy\" ants actually acted as a back-up team when others were lost.","t":"結果是出乎意料的，因為那些「懶惰」的螞蟻在其他螞蟻消失時其實擔任了後備隊伍。"},{"w":"unexpectedly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that surprises you because you did not think it would happen","c":"出乎意料地","s":"It started to rain unexpectedly in the middle of the outdoor concert, and everyone ran for cover.","t":"戶外演唱會進行到一半突然下起雨，大家紛紛找地方躲。"},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone about something so they can understand it","c":"解釋","s":"Can you explain why the sky turns red at sunset?","t":"你能解釋為什麼日落時天空會變紅嗎？。"},{"w":"explanation","p":"n.","d":"a reason or description that makes something clear","c":"解釋","s":"The teacher's clear explanation of the math problem helped everyone understand it, even the students who had failed the quiz.","t":"老師對這道數學題清楚的解釋幫助每個人都理解了，連小考不及格的學生也懂了。"},{"w":"explanatory","p":"adj.","d":"giving an explanation","c":"解釋的；說明的","s":"The museum added explanatory videos next to each rock, so visitors can understand how it was formed.","t":"博物館在每塊岩石旁加上了解說影片，讓參觀者能了解它是如何形成的。"},{"w":"unexplained","p":"adj.","d":"without a known reason","c":"無法解釋的","s":"For some unexplained reason, the lights in the classroom kept turning on and off.","t":"不知什麼原因，教室的燈一直忽明忽暗。"},{"w":"explode","p":"v.","d":"to burst with a loud noise; to suddenly increase","c":"爆炸","s":"A gas tank exploded in the restaurant kitchen, but luckily no one was hurt.","t":"餐廳廚房的瓦斯桶爆炸了，幸好無人受傷。"},{"w":"explosion","p":"n.","d":"a sudden loud burst when something like a bomb blows up","c":"爆炸","s":"Gas in the mine caused a terrible explosion, and the whole town gathered at the gate for news.","t":"礦坑裡的瓦斯引發了一場可怕的爆炸,而全鎮的人都聚集在大門口等消息。"},{"w":"explosive","p":"adj./n.","d":"able to explode; likely to blow up","c":"易爆的；炸藥","s":"Firefighters warned that the gas tank was explosive and could blow up at any moment.","t":"消防員警告瓦斯桶可能會爆炸，隨時都會炸開。"},{"w":"explore","p":"v.","d":"to travel around a place to learn about it","c":"探索","s":"We spent the whole afternoon exploring the old streets and small shops of Tainan.","t":"我們整個下午都在探索台南的老街和小店。"},{"w":"exploration","p":"n.","d":"the act of traveling through a place to learn about it; careful study of a subject","c":"探索","s":"The exploration of deep-sea environments has revealed hundreds of new species that science had never documented before.","t":"對深海環境的探索揭示了數百個科學從未記錄過的新物種。"},{"w":"explorer","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels to unknown places to learn about them","c":"探險家","s":"The famous ocean explorer spent his life studying the sea, and his films made millions of people love marine life.","t":"這位著名的海洋探險家一生都在研究海洋,而他的影片讓數百萬人愛上海洋生物。"},{"w":"expose","p":"v.","d":"to show something that was hidden; to make the truth known","c":"使暴露；揭發","s":"Reporters tried to expose the company's illegal dumping of waste into the river.","t":"記者試圖揭發那家公司非法將廢棄物倒入河中。"},{"w":"exposure","p":"n.","d":"the state of being in a place where something can affect you","c":"暴露；接觸","s":"Long-term exposure to strong sunlight without protection can cause serious skin damage and increase the risk of cancer.","t":"長期在沒有保護的情況下暴露在強烈陽光下可能會導致嚴重的皮膚損傷並增加癌症風險。"},{"w":"exposed","p":"adj.","d":"not covered or protected","c":"暴露的","s":"Living abroad exposed Mia to many different foods and cultures.","t":"住在國外讓 Mia 接觸到許多不同的食物和文化。"},{"w":"express","p":"v.","d":"to convey a thought or feeling in words or gestures; rapid","c":"表達","s":"It is sometimes hard for teenagers to express their feelings to their parents.","t":"青少年有時很難向父母表達自己的感受。"},{"w":"expression","p":"n.","d":"showing feelings or ideas through words or art","c":"表達；表情；措辭","s":"Poetry was her main form of expression, because she found it difficult to talk about her feelings with others.","t":"詩是她主要的表達方式,因為她發現很難和別人談論自己的感受。"},{"w":"expressive","p":"adj.","d":"showing feelings clearly","c":"富有表情的；善於表達的","s":"The dancer's expressive face showed both joy and sadness at the same time.","t":"舞者富有表情的臉同時流露出喜悅與悲傷。"},{"w":"extend","p":"v.","d":"to make something longer or larger; to last longer","c":"延長；延伸","s":"We decided to extend our stay by two more days.","t":"我們決定再延長兩天的停留。"},{"w":"extension","p":"n.","d":"extra time given to finish something; a part added to make something longer or bigger","c":"延長；延伸","s":"She requested an extension for her project deadline.","t":"她要求延長她的項目截止日期。"},{"w":"extensive","p":"adj.","d":"covering a large area or a lot of things; very great in amount","c":"廣泛的；大量的","s":"Our school library has an extensive collection of comics and graphic novels.","t":"我們學校圖書館收藏了大量漫畫與圖像小說。"},{"w":"extent","p":"n.","d":"how large, important, or serious something is","c":"程度；範圍","s":"Satellites showed the extent of the ice loss, and the photos made the news around the world.","t":"衛星顯示了冰層流失的範圍,這些照片登上了全世界的新聞。"},{"w":"faith","p":"n.","d":"strong belief or trust in someone or something","c":"信任；信念","s":"My dad has great faith in me; he believes I can do anything I set my mind to.","t":"我爸爸非常信任我，他相信我下定決心就能做到任何事。"},{"w":"faithful","p":"adj.","d":"always loyal and supporting someone or something","c":"忠實的；忠誠的","s":"Her translation is faithful to the original novel, but it also reads naturally, which is why it won an award.","t":"她的譯文忠於原著小說，但讀起來也很自然，這就是它得獎的原因。"},{"w":"faithfully","p":"adv.","d":"exactly and accurately","c":"忠實地","s":"The old guard dog faithfully waited at the door every day for its owner to come home.","t":"那隻老看門狗每天都忠實地在門口等主人回家。"},{"w":"unfaithful","p":"adj.","d":"not loyal to a partner or friend","c":"不忠的","s":"She ended the relationship because her boyfriend had been unfaithful to her, and she could no longer trust him at all.","t":"她結束了這段關係，因為男友對她不忠，她再也無法信任他。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"fake – frequent · 15 字族 · 40 題","cards":[{"w":"fake","p":"adj./n./v.","d":"not real, but made to look real","c":"假的；仿冒品；偽造；假裝","s":"Be careful — some online shops sell fake brand-name bags.","t":"小心——有些網路商店賣假的名牌包。"},{"w":"faking","p":"n.","d":"pretending that something is true or real","c":"假裝","s":"The player was faking an injury to get a free kick.","t":"那名球員假裝受傷想騙一個自由球。"},{"w":"fascinate","p":"v.","d":"to attract and hold someone's interest very strongly","c":"使著迷","s":"Old maps have always fascinate my brother, and he spends hours studying the strange sea monsters drawn on them.","t":"古地圖一向讓我哥哥著迷,他會花好幾個小時研究上面畫的奇怪海怪。"},{"w":"fascinated","p":"adj.","d":"very interested in something","c":"著迷的","s":"The children were so fascinated by the magic show that they forgot about the ice cream melting in their hands.","t":"孩子們被魔術表演迷住了，忘了手上的冰淇淋正在融化。"},{"w":"fascinating","p":"adj.","d":"extremely interesting","c":"迷人的","s":"The documentary about deep-sea fish was so fascinating that I watched it twice.","t":"那部深海魚的紀錄片太有趣了，我看了兩遍。"},{"w":"fascination","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest in something","c":"著迷；魅力","s":"Ever since he was a child, Ray has had a fascination with old trains.","t":"Ray 從小就對老火車很著迷。"},{"w":"feature","p":"n./v.","d":"an important or typical part","c":"特色；以…為特色","s":"The main feature of this product is its durability and compatibility with various electronic devices.","t":"該產品的主要特點是其耐用性以及與各式各樣電子裝置的相容性。"},{"w":"featured","p":"adj.","d":"shown as a special part of something","c":"被特別介紹的","s":"The film featured several famous Taiwanese actors in small roles.","t":"那部電影由幾位知名台灣演員客串小角色。"},{"w":"features","p":"n.","d":"parts of the face; special qualities","c":"五官；特徵","s":"One of the best features of this phone is its long battery life.","t":"這支手機最棒的特色之一是電池續航力長。"},{"w":"fertile","p":"adj.","d":"(of land) good for growing plants","c":"肥沃的；能生育的","s":"The river flooded every year and left fertile soil behind, so farmers could grow plenty of wheat.","t":"河流每年氾濫並留下肥沃的土壤,所以農民能種出大量的小麥。"},{"w":"fertility","p":"n.","d":"the ability of land to grow good crops; the ability to have babies","c":"肥沃；生育力","s":"Volcanic soil is famous for its high fertility.","t":"火山土以高肥沃度聞名。"},{"w":"fertilizer","p":"n.","d":"a substance put on soil to help plants grow","c":"肥料","s":"The farmer adds natural fertilizer to the soil to help his rice grow.","t":"農夫在土壤中加入天然肥料幫助稻子生長。"},{"w":"fertilize","p":"v.","d":"to add substances to soil to help plants grow","c":"施肥","s":"You should fertilize your plants once a month during spring.","t":"春天時你應該每月幫植物施肥一次。"},{"w":"finance","p":"n.","d":"the management of money, especially by governments or companies","c":"財務；金融","s":"He works in the field of finance.","t":"他在財務領域工作。"},{"w":"financial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with money","c":"財務的","s":"The company faced financial difficulties.","t":"該公司面臨財務困難。"},{"w":"financially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way related to money","c":"財務上","s":"After getting a job, Sam became financially independent from his parents.","t":"找到工作後，山姆在經濟上脫離了父母獨立。"},{"w":"finances","p":"n. pl.","d":"the money a person or organization has","c":"財源","s":"After losing his job, he had to look carefully at his finances and stop eating out at restaurants every weekend.","t":"失業後，他必須仔細檢視自己的財務狀況，不再每個週末上餐廳吃飯。"},{"w":"firm","p":"adj./n.","d":"a company, especially a small or professional one","c":"堅定的；結實的；公司；事務所","s":"Mom gave a firm \"No!\" when I asked to stay out after midnight.","t":"我問能不能過了午夜再回家時，媽媽堅決地說「不行！」。"},{"w":"firmly","p":"adv.","d":"in a strong, clear way that shows you will not change your mind","c":"堅定地；牢固地","s":"A: Did the supplier agree to lower the price of the steel after our long meeting with them yesterday? B: No, their sales manager firmly said that the price could not change because of higher shipping costs, so we will have to look for another company that can offer a better deal.","t":"A：昨天和供應商開了很久的會之後，他們同意降低鋼材價格了嗎？ B：沒有，他們的業務經理【堅定地】表示，因為運費提高，價格無法調整，所以我們必須找另一家能提供更好條件的公司。"},{"w":"flavor","p":"n./v.","d":"the distinctive taste of a food or drink; to impart flavor to","c":"口味；調味","s":"The experienced Italian chef likes to flavor his tomato pasta sauce with fresh basil and garlic.","t":"那位經驗豐富的義大利主廚喜歡用新鮮羅勒和大蒜為他的番茄義大利麵醬調味。"},{"w":"flavorful","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong, pleasant taste","c":"美味的","s":"This beef noodle soup is rich and flavorful thanks to the spices simmered for hours.","t":"這碗牛肉麵湯頭濃郁美味，多虧香料燉了好幾個小時。"},{"w":"flavoring","p":"n.","d":"something added to food to give it taste","c":"調味料","s":"The soup was flavorless because the cook forgot to add salt.","t":"湯淡而無味，因為廚師忘了加鹽。"},{"w":"flavorless","p":"adj.","d":"having no taste","c":"無味的","s":"The soup was flavorless because the cook forgot to add salt.","t":"湯淡而無味，因為廚師忘了加鹽。"},{"w":"flaw","p":"n.","d":"a mistake or weak point that makes something not perfect","c":"缺點；瑕疵","s":"There was a flaw in the experiment, because the scientists forgot to give one group of mice the same food.","t":"這個實驗有一個缺陷，因為科學家忘了給其中一組老鼠吃同樣的食物。"},{"w":"flawed","p":"adj.","d":"having mistakes or weaknesses","c":"有缺陷的","s":"The plan was flawed from the start because no one checked the budget.","t":"這個計畫一開始就有缺陷，因為沒人核對預算。"},{"w":"flawless","p":"adj.","d":"perfect, with no mistakes","c":"完美無瑕的","s":"Her English is flawless; she never makes any mistakes.","t":"她的英文完美無瑕，從不犯錯。"},{"w":"flawlessly","p":"adv.","d":"perfectly, without any mistakes","c":"完美地","s":"The pianist played the difficult piece flawlessly.","t":"鋼琴家完美無瑕地彈奏了那首難曲。"},{"w":"flexible","p":"adj.","d":"able to change easily to suit new situations","c":"有彈性的；柔軟的","s":"My company offers flexible working hours, so I can pick up my kids after school.","t":"我的公司提供彈性工時，所以我可以放學接小孩。"},{"w":"flexibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to bend easily; the ability to change plans or ideas when needed","c":"彈性；柔軟度","s":"Yoga can improve your flexibility and balance.","t":"瑜伽能改善你的柔軟度和平衡感。"},{"w":"inflexible","p":"adj.","d":"unable to change easily","c":"死板的","s":"The rules at our cram school are quite inflexible; nothing can be changed.","t":"我們補習班的規定相當死板，什麼都不能改。"},{"w":"flock","p":"n./v.","d":"a group of birds or sheep","c":"（鳥、羊）群；群集；蜂擁","s":"Tourists always flock to Jiufen on weekends.","t":"遊客總是在週末湧向九份。"},{"w":"flocks","p":"n. pl.","d":"groups of birds or sheep","c":"群","s":"Every winter, huge flocks of black-faced spoonbills arrive in Tainan.","t":"每年冬天，大群黑面琵鷺飛抵台南。"},{"w":"flood","p":"n./v.","d":"to cover an area with water","c":"洪水；淹沒；湧入","s":"Heavy rain flood the underground car park, and dozens of cars were stuck under the water until the next day.","t":"大雨淹沒了地下停車場,數十輛汽車被困在水下直到隔天。"},{"w":"flooded","p":"adj.","d":"covered or submerged with water.","c":"淹水的","s":"After the singer posted the news, messages flooded into her account.","t":"歌手發布消息後，留言大量湧進她的帳號。"},{"w":"flooding","p":"n.","d":"a situation when water covers land that is usually dry","c":"水災","s":"Southern Taiwan suffered three serious floods this summer.","t":"南台灣今年夏天發生了三次嚴重水災。"},{"w":"focus","p":"v./n.","d":"to adapt to see clearly; the center of interest or activity","c":"專注；集中；焦點；重點","s":"It's hard for me to focus on my homework when my phone keeps buzzing.","t":"手機一直震動時，我很難專心寫作業。"},{"w":"focused","p":"adj.","d":"paying full attention to one aim or task","c":"專注的","s":"Stay focused during the exam and don't let the noise outside distract you.","t":"考試時保持專注，別讓外面的噪音讓你分心。"},{"w":"fortune","p":"n.","d":"a very large amount of money","c":"財富；運氣","s":"The businessman made a fortune by selling smartphones.","t":"那位商人靠賣智慧型手機發了大財。"},{"w":"fortunate","p":"adj.","d":"lucky","c":"幸運的","s":"We were very fortunate that the rain stopped just in time for the outdoor graduation ceremony to begin on schedule.","t":"我們非常幸運，雨恰好在戶外畢業典禮準時開始前停了下來。"},{"w":"fortunately","p":"adv.","d":"by a stroke of good luck; luckily.","c":"幸運地","s":"Fortunately, nobody was hurt when the old tree fell onto the road.","t":"幸好老樹倒在路上時沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"unfortunate","p":"adj.","d":"unlucky; experiencing bad events or conditions.","c":"不幸的","s":"It was unfortunate that the shop was already closed when we finally got there after a long walk.","t":"我們走了好久終於到了，店卻已經關門，真不走運。"},{"w":"unfortunately","p":"adv.","d":"it is a pity that; unluckily.","c":"不幸地；可惜","s":"Unfortunately, it rained all day on the day of our class picnic.","t":"很可惜，我們班野餐那天下了一整天的雨。"},{"w":"found","p":"v.","d":"to start a company or organization","c":"創立","s":"They plan to found a non-profit organization to support education in underprivileged areas.","t":"他們計劃創立一個非盈利組織以支持貧困地區的教育。"},{"w":"foundation","p":"n.","d":"the strong base under a building","c":"基礎；基金會","s":"Learning basic grammar gives you a strong foundation for reading English novels later.","t":"學好基礎文法能為日後讀英文小說打下穩固基礎。"},{"w":"founder","p":"n.","d":"a person who starts a company, school, or organization","c":"創辦人","s":"The founder of the company is known for his innovative ideas and charismatic leadership.","t":"公司的創始人以其創新思想和富有感召力的領導而著稱。"},{"w":"founding","p":"adj.","d":"starting an organization or country","c":"創立的","s":"The school was founded in 1920 and is one of the oldest in the city.","t":"這所學校創立於 1920 年，是市內最古老的學校之一。"},{"w":"frequent","p":"adj.","d":"happening or done very often across brief intervals.","c":"頻繁的","s":"Earthquakes are frequent in Taiwan, so every school holds safety drills.","t":"台灣地震頻繁，所以每間學校都會舉行安全演習。"},{"w":"frequently","p":"adv.","d":"often","c":"頻繁地","s":"Jessie frequently visits her grandparents in Yilan on weekends.","t":"Jessie 週末常去宜蘭探望祖父母。"},{"w":"frequency","p":"n.","d":"how often something happens","c":"頻率；次數","s":"The frequency of strong typhoons has increased in recent years, and insurance companies have raised their prices.","t":"近年來強烈颱風的頻率增加了,保險公司也提高了保費。"},{"w":"infrequent","p":"adj.","d":"not happening often","c":"不常發生的","s":"Trains to the small mountain village are infrequent, with only two in the morning and one in the late afternoon.","t":"到那個山區小村的火車班次很少，早上只有兩班，傍晚一班。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"frighten – graduate · 15 字族 · 33 題","cards":[{"w":"frighten","p":"v.","d":"to make someone afraid","c":"使驚嚇","s":"The loud noise frightened the children.","t":"巨大的聲音嚇到了孩子們。"},{"w":"fright","p":"n.","d":"a sudden feeling of fear","c":"驚嚇","s":"The loud bang gave the old woman such a fright that she dropped her cup.","t":"那聲巨響把老太太嚇得手中的杯子都掉了。"},{"w":"frightened","p":"adj.","d":"afraid or anxious, often suddenly","c":"害怕的","s":"The sudden bang of the fireworks frightened the baby, and she started crying.","t":"突然的煙火爆炸聲嚇到小嬰兒，她哭了起來。"},{"w":"frightening","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel afraid","c":"令人害怕的","s":"Walking alone through the dark forest was a frightening experience.","t":"獨自走過漆黑的森林是很可怕的經驗。"},{"w":"frustrate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel annoyed because they cannot do what they want","c":"使挫折","s":"The constant technical problems began to frustrate the entire team, as they were unable to meet the project deadline.","t":"不斷出現的技術問題開始讓整個團隊感到沮喪，因為他們無法在專案截止日期前完成。"},{"w":"frustration","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being upset because you cannot do or get something","c":"挫折","s":"She threw her pencil down in frustration after failing the math problem again.","t":"她又解錯數學題後，沮喪地把鉛筆丟下。"},{"w":"frustrated","p":"adj.","d":"feeling annoyed or discouraged due to failure.","c":"感到挫折的","s":"He felt very frustrated after failing the driving test for the second time, but his instructor encouraged him to try again.","t":"第二次駕駛考試不及格後，他感到非常沮喪，但教練鼓勵他再試一次。"},{"w":"frustrating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed, stuck, or disappointed.","c":"令人挫折的","s":"Waiting in line for two hours only to find the tickets sold out was really frustrating.","t":"排隊兩小時才發現票賣完了，真令人沮喪。"},{"w":"fulfill","p":"v.","d":"to do what you promised or what is needed; to make a dream come true","c":"實現；履行","s":"Grandpa worked for forty years to fulfill his dream of owning a small farm, and he finally bought one last spring.","t":"爺爺工作了四十年來實現擁有一座小農場的夢想，去年春天他終於買了一座。"},{"w":"fulfillment","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being happy because you achieved something","c":"實現；滿足感","s":"Teaching in a small village school gave her a deep sense of fulfillment that a higher salary in the city never could.","t":"在小村莊的學校教書帶給她一種深深的成就感，那是城市裡更高的薪水永遠無法給予的。"},{"w":"fulfilling","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel happy and satisfied","c":"令人有成就感的","s":"Many volunteers say that teaching kids in rural areas is a truly fulfilling experience.","t":"許多志工說在偏鄉教孩子是很有成就感的經驗。"},{"w":"fulfilled","p":"adj.","d":"happy and satisfied with what you do","c":"感到滿足的","s":"After years of hard work, Grandpa finally fulfilled his dream of opening a small noodle shop.","t":"多年努力後，爺爺終於實現了開一家小麵店的夢想。"},{"w":"function","p":"n./v.","d":"the job or purpose something has","c":"功能；運作","s":"The function of the heart is to pump blood.","t":"心臟的功能是泵血。"},{"w":"functional","p":"adj.","d":"working properly; made to be useful rather than beautiful","c":"實用的；運作中的","s":"After the earthquake, only one of the three elevators in the building was still functional.","t":"地震後，大樓三部電梯只剩一部還能運作。"},{"w":"functioning","p":"adj.","d":"working in the right way","c":"正常運作的","s":"After the earthquake, only one of the three elevators in the building was still functional.","t":"地震後，大樓三部電梯只剩一部還能運作。"},{"w":"malfunction","p":"n./v.","d":"to fail to work in the correct way","c":"故障","s":"The self-checkout machine began to malfunction during the busy lunch hour, so a staff member had to help every customer.","t":"自助結帳機在忙碌的午餐時間開始故障,所以一位店員必須幫每位顧客結帳。"},{"w":"fury","p":"n.","d":"very strong anger","c":"狂怒","s":"In a fit of fury, he threw his phone across the room.","t":"他一怒之下把手機扔到房間另一頭。"},{"w":"furious","p":"adj.","d":"extremely angry","c":"狂怒的","s":"Mom was furious when she saw the mess in the kitchen.","t":"媽媽看到廚房一團亂時氣炸了。"},{"w":"furiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a very angry way; very fast and with a lot of energy","c":"狂怒地；猛烈地","s":"The dog barked furiously at the delivery man.","t":"狗對著外送員狂吠。"},{"w":"gene","p":"n.","d":"a part of a cell that controls what you get from your parents","c":"基因","s":"Scientists found a gene that affects how tall people grow, but food and sleep also play an important role.","t":"科學家發現了一個會影響人們長多高的基因，但食物和睡眠也扮演重要的角色。"},{"w":"genetic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with genes, which parents pass to their children","c":"基因的；遺傳的","s":"Some diseases are genetic, which means they can be passed from parents to their children through the family line.","t":"有些疾病是遺傳的，意思是它們可以透過家族血脈從父母傳給子女。"},{"w":"genetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to genes","c":"基因上","s":"Some farmers refuse to grow genetically modified crops.","t":"有些農夫拒絕種植基因改造作物。"},{"w":"generous","p":"adj.","d":"happy to give money, time, or help","c":"慷慨的","s":"Thank you for your generous donation to our school library.","t":"感謝您對本校圖書館的慷慨捐贈。"},{"w":"generosity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of giving money, time, or help freely","c":"慷慨","s":"Thanks to the generosity of local shop owners, every child at the orphanage received a new coat and a gift this winter.","t":"多虧了當地店家的慷慨，孤兒院的每個孩子今年冬天都收到一件新外套和一份禮物。"},{"w":"generously","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind way that gives a lot","c":"慷慨地","s":"Many people gave generously to help the victims of the earthquake.","t":"許多人慷慨解囊幫助地震災民。"},{"w":"genuine","p":"adj.","d":"real, not fake","c":"真正的；真誠的","s":"The way Mia listens to everyone shows her genuine interest in other people.","t":"Mia 傾聽每個人的方式顯示她對別人真正的關心。"},{"w":"genuinely","p":"adv.","d":"really; in a sincere way","c":"真誠地；真正地","s":"My grandmother was genuinely surprised when the whole family showed up for her eightieth birthday.","t":"全家人出現在奶奶八十大壽時，她真的很驚訝。"},{"w":"genuineness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being real or honest","c":"真實；真誠","s":"My grandmother was genuinely surprised when the whole family showed up for her eightieth birthday.","t":"全家人出現在奶奶八十大壽時，她真的很驚訝。"},{"w":"geography","p":"n.","d":"the study of the physical features of the earth and its atmosphere","c":"地理（學）","s":"In geography class, we learned about the mountains and rivers of Taiwan.","t":"在地理課上，我們學了台灣的山脈與河流。"},{"w":"geographical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with geography or the position of places","c":"地理的","s":"The city's geographical position between two seas made it rich, because every trader had to pass through it.","t":"這座城市位於兩海之間的地理位置讓它變得富裕,因為每個商人都必須經過那裡。"},{"w":"geographer","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies the earth and its places","c":"地理學家","s":"The geographer spent years studying how rivers change the land.","t":"那位地理學家花了數年研究河流如何改變地貌。"},{"w":"geographically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with where places are","c":"地理上","s":"Geographically, Taiwan lies between Japan and the Philippines.","t":"從地理上看，台灣位於日本和菲律賓之間。"},{"w":"globe","p":"n.","d":"the world; a round model of the Earth","c":"地球儀；地球","s":"The teacher spun the globe and asked us to find Brazil.","t":"老師轉動地球儀，要我們找出巴西。"},{"w":"global","p":"adj.","d":"about the whole world","c":"全球的","s":"The pandemic has had a global impact on economies worldwide.","t":"大流行病對全球經濟產生了全球性影響。"},{"w":"globally","p":"adv.","d":"around the whole world","c":"全球地","s":"Bubble tea has become popular globally, not just in Asia.","t":"珍珠奶茶已在全球流行，不只是在亞洲。"},{"w":"globalization","p":"n.","d":"the process by which the world's businesses and cultures become connected","c":"全球化","s":"Because of globalization, you can buy the same brand of shoes in Taipei, Paris, and New York at almost the same price.","t":"由於全球化，你可以在台北、巴黎和紐約以幾乎相同的價格買到同一品牌的鞋子。"},{"w":"glory","p":"n.","d":"great honor and praise that you win by doing something important","c":"榮耀","s":"The team returned home in glory after winning the national championship for the first time in thirty years.","t":"球隊在三十年來首次贏得全國冠軍後，帶著榮耀回到家鄉。"},{"w":"glorious","p":"adj.","d":"very beautiful or wonderful; deserving great praise","c":"輝煌的；壯麗的","s":"After a week of rain, we finally woke up to a glorious sunny morning and decided to go to the beach.","t":"下了一週的雨後，我們終於在一個燦爛的晴朗早晨醒來，決定去海邊。"},{"w":"glorify","p":"v.","d":"to praise someone and make them seem better than they are","c":"美化；頌揚","s":"Some video games glorify violence, which worries parents.","t":"有些電玩美化暴力，令家長擔心。"},{"w":"gloriously","p":"adv.","d":"in a very beautiful or wonderful way","c":"輝煌地","s":"The sun shone gloriously on the first morning of the new year.","t":"新年第一個早晨陽光燦爛。"},{"w":"gossip","p":"n./v.","d":"talk about other people's private lives","c":"八卦；閒聊","s":"Don't believe everything you hear; it's probably just gossip.","t":"別相信你聽到的每件事，那可能只是八卦。"},{"w":"gossipy","p":"adj.","d":"liking to talk about other people's private lives","c":"愛說閒話的","s":"Our gossipy neighbor always knows what is happening in every family on the street.","t":"我們那個愛說閒話的鄰居總是知道整條街每戶人家的事。"},{"w":"gossiper","p":"n.","d":"a person who often talks about other people","c":"愛說閒話的人","s":"Don't believe everything you hear; it's probably just gossip.","t":"別相信你聽到的每件事，那可能只是八卦。"},{"w":"grace","p":"n.","d":"a smooth, beautiful way of moving; polite and kind behavior","c":"優雅","s":"The ballet dancer performed with such grace that the audience held their breath.","t":"芭蕾舞者表演得如此優雅，觀眾都屏住了呼吸。"},{"w":"graceful","p":"adj.","d":"moving in a smooth and beautiful way","c":"優雅的","s":"The skater's jumps were so graceful that the judges gave her the highest score of the whole competition.","t":"那位滑冰選手的跳躍如此優美，評審給了她整場比賽的最高分。"},{"w":"gracefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a smooth and beautiful way; politely","c":"優雅地","s":"The swan moved gracefully across the lake in the morning light.","t":"天鵝在晨光中優雅地滑過湖面。"},{"w":"gracious","p":"adj.","d":"polite, kind, and generous, especially to people of lower position","c":"親切的；有禮的","s":"Although the famous writer was very busy, she was gracious enough to sign every book and chat with each young fan.","t":"雖然那位名作家非常忙碌，但她親切有禮地為每本書簽名，並和每位年輕粉絲聊天。"},{"w":"gradual","p":"adj.","d":"happening slowly over a long time","c":"逐漸的","s":"Doctors suggest a gradual increase in exercise rather than a sudden change.","t":"醫生建議逐步增加運動量，而不是突然改變。"},{"w":"gradually","p":"adv.","d":"slowly over time","c":"逐漸地","s":"After moving to Canada, Jason gradually got used to the cold winters.","t":"搬到加拿大後，Jason 漸漸習慣了寒冷的冬天。"},{"w":"gradualness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of happening slowly","c":"漸進","s":"After moving to Canada, Jason gradually got used to the cold winters.","t":"搬到加拿大後，Jason 漸漸習慣了寒冷的冬天。"},{"w":"graduate","p":"v./n.","d":"a person who has finished a degree","c":"畢業；畢業生","s":"Many new graduates find that companies now expect AI skills, so they take extra courses after leaving university.","t":"許多應屆畢業生發現公司現在要求人工智慧技能,所以他們離開大學後會額外修課。"},{"w":"graduation","p":"n.","d":"the act of finishing your studies at a school or university; the ceremony for this","c":"畢業","s":"Her whole family attended the graduation ceremony and cheered loudly when her name was called on the stage.","t":"她的全家都出席了畢業典禮，當她的名字在台上被念到時，大家大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"graduated","p":"v.","d":"finished school or university","c":"畢業（過去式）","s":"Over 400 graduates of our school will go on to study at universities this year.","t":"本校今年有四百多名畢業生將升上大學。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"grateful – hostile · 15 字族 · 37 題","cards":[{"w":"grateful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that you want to thank someone","c":"感激的","s":"I'm really grateful to my teammates for helping me after I hurt my ankle.","t":"我腳踝受傷後隊友幫助我，我真的很感激。"},{"w":"gratefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you are thankful","c":"感激地","s":"The tired hikers gratefully accepted the hot tea that the old farmer offered them at the foot of the mountain.","t":"疲憊的登山客感激地接受了老農夫在山腳下請他們喝的熱茶。"},{"w":"gratitude","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being thankful","c":"感激","s":"Writing down three things you feel gratitude for each night can make you happier, and it only takes two minutes.","t":"每天晚上寫下三件讓你心懷感恩的事可以讓你更快樂,而且只需要兩分鐘。"},{"w":"ungrateful","p":"adj.","d":"not showing thanks for what others do for you","c":"忘恩負義的","s":"The ungrateful boy never thanked his grandma for the gifts she gave him.","t":"那個不知感恩的男孩從沒為奶奶送的禮物道謝。"},{"w":"greet","p":"v.","d":"to welcome or say hello to someone with words or actions","c":"問候；迎接","s":"Every weekday morning, the friendly hotel manager stands near the front entrance to greet all the international guests with a warm smile.","t":"每個工作日早晨，這位友善的飯店經理都會站在正門附近，帶著溫暖的微笑【問候】所有國際賓客。"},{"w":"greeting","p":"n.","d":"something you say or do when you meet someone","c":"問候；招呼","s":"A greeting card from my pen pal in Canada arrived just before Christmas.","t":"聖誕節前夕，加拿大筆友寄來的賀卡到了。"},{"w":"greeting card","p":"n.","d":"a card with a message for a birthday, holiday, or special event","c":"賀卡","s":"The bookstore sells a greeting card for almost every occasion, from birthdays and weddings to passing an exam.","t":"這家書店幾乎每種場合的賀卡都有賣，從生日、婚禮到通過考試。"},{"w":"guarantee","p":"v./n.","d":"to promise that something will certainly happen or be done","c":"保證；保證（書）","s":"We guarantee satisfaction or your money back.","t":"我們保證滿意，否則退款。"},{"w":"guaranteed","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen","c":"有保證的","s":"Hard work doesn't always mean guaranteed success, but it helps.","t":"努力不一定保證成功，但很有幫助。"},{"w":"guard","p":"n./v.","d":"to watch over in order to protect or control; a protector","c":"警衛；守衛；保護","s":"Two dogs guard the farm every night while the farmer sleeps.","t":"農夫睡覺時，兩隻狗每晚看守農場。"},{"w":"guardian","p":"n.","d":"a person who is legally responsible for a child; someone who protects something","c":"監護人；守護者","s":"Students under 18 need a parent or guardian to sign the form.","t":"未滿十八歲的學生需由父母或監護人簽表。"},{"w":"guarded","p":"adj.","d":"careful not to show feelings or give information","c":"有戒心的","s":"A: Did the CEO say anything about the possible merger when the reporters asked him questions after the shareholders' meeting this morning? B: He gave only a guarded answer, saying that talks were continuing, because the details are still secret and nothing has been signed yet.","t":"A：今天早上股東會後記者發問時，執行長有提到可能的合併案嗎？ B：他只給了一個【有所保留的】回答，說談判仍在持續，因為細節還是祕密，而且還沒有簽任何文件。"},{"w":"guilt","p":"n.","d":"the bad feeling you have when you know you have done something wrong; the fact of having broken a law","c":"罪惡感；有罪","s":"After lying to his best friend, Jack was filled with guilt.","t":"傑克對好友撒謊後滿心罪惡感。"},{"w":"guilty","p":"adj.","d":"having broken a law; feeling bad because you have done something wrong","c":"內疚的；有罪的","s":"The court found the driver guilty of causing the accident.","t":"法院判定那名駕駛須為事故負責、有罪。"},{"w":"guiltless","p":"adj.","d":"not guilty of doing anything wrong","c":"無罪的","s":"After lying to his best friend, Jack was filled with guilt.","t":"傑克對好友撒謊後滿心罪惡感。"},{"w":"harm","p":"n./v.","d":"damage or injury caused to a person or thing","c":"傷害；危害","s":"Smoking does a lot of harm to both smokers and the people around them.","t":"抽菸對吸菸者和周遭的人都有很大的傷害。"},{"w":"harmful","p":"adj.","d":"causing damage or injury","c":"有害的","s":"Smoke from the factories was harmful to people's health, but many families could not afford to move away.","t":"工廠排出的煙對人們的健康有害,但許多家庭沒有能力搬走。"},{"w":"harmless","p":"adj.","d":"not able to cause harm","c":"無害的","s":"Don't be afraid of that snake; it's completely harmless to people.","t":"別怕那條蛇，牠對人完全無害。"},{"w":"harvest","p":"n./v.","d":"the time when crops are collected","c":"收成；收穫期；收割","s":"This year's rice harvest was smaller because of the long dry season.","t":"因為長期乾旱，今年稻米收成較少。"},{"w":"harvester","p":"n.","d":"a machine or person that gathers crops","c":"收割機；收割者","s":"The farmer bought a new harvester to cut his wheat faster.","t":"農夫買了一台新收割機，好更快收割小麥。"},{"w":"harvesting","p":"n.","d":"gathering crops from the fields","c":"收割","s":"This year's rice harvest was smaller because of the long dry season.","t":"因為長期乾旱，今年稻米收成較少。"},{"w":"hesitate","p":"v.","d":"to pause before doing something because you are unsure","c":"猶豫","s":"Please don't hesitate to ask if you have any questions.","t":"有任何問題請不要猶豫，儘管提問。"},{"w":"hesitation","p":"n.","d":"a pause before you do or say something because you are not sure","c":"猶豫","s":"After a moment of hesitation, the boy jumped into the cold pool, and his friends cheered loudly from the side.","t":"猶豫了一會兒之後，男孩跳進冰冷的泳池，他的朋友們在池邊大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"hesitant","p":"adj.","d":"slow to act or speak because you are not sure","c":"猶豫的","s":"Amy was hesitant about joining the dance club at first, but now she practices with the team three times a week.","t":"艾咪起初對加入舞蹈社感到猶豫，但現在她每週和隊員一起練習三次。"},{"w":"highlight","p":"n./v.","d":"to make people notice something important","c":"最精彩的部分；強調","s":"The fireworks show was the highlight of our trip to Taipei.","t":"煙火秀是我們台北之旅的最精彩部分。"},{"w":"highlighter","p":"n.","d":"a bright pen used to mark important words","c":"螢光筆","s":"He used a yellow highlighter on almost every line, so the colour no longer showed what was really important.","t":"他幾乎每一行都用黃色螢光筆畫，所以顏色已經無法顯示真正重要的內容。"},{"w":"highlighted","p":"v.","d":"marked to show importance","c":"強調（過去式）","s":"Last week's news report highlighted the problem of plastic waste in our oceans.","t":"上週的新聞報導強調了海洋塑膠垃圾的問題。"},{"w":"history","p":"n.","d":"the study of things that happened in the past","c":"歷史","s":"Q: What class does your brother have this afternoon? — A: He has history class. He learns about the past.","t":"你哥哥今天下午有什麼課？ — 他有歷史課，他學習過去的事。"},{"w":"historian","p":"n.","d":"an expert who studies and writes about past events and civilizations","c":"歷史學家","s":"The knowledgeable university historian spent twenty long years investigating the political causes of the ancient civil war.","t":"那位博學的大學歷史學家花了整整二十年調查那場古代內戰的政治成因。"},{"w":"historic","p":"adj.","d":"important in history","c":"有歷史意義的","s":"Tainan is full of historic sites such as temples and old forts.","t":"台南到處都是寺廟、古堡等歷史古蹟。"},{"w":"historical","p":"adj.","d":"related to the past or history","c":"歷史的","s":"Tainan is full of historic sites such as temples and old forts.","t":"台南到處都是寺廟、古堡等歷史古蹟。"},{"w":"honest","p":"adj.","d":"always telling the truth","c":"誠實的","s":"To be honest, I didn't enjoy the movie very much.","t":"老實說，我不太喜歡這部電影。"},{"w":"honestly","p":"adv.","d":"in a truthful way, without hiding anything","c":"誠實地；老實說","s":"Please answer all the questions on the survey honestly.","t":"請誠實回答問卷上的所有問題。"},{"w":"honesty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being truthful, trustworthy, and fair","c":"誠實","s":"My grandfather taught me that honesty is the best policy in life, and you will always earn respect by telling the truth.","t":"我的祖父教導我誠實是人生上策，而你說實話總能贏得別人的尊重。"},{"w":"dishonest","p":"adj.","d":"not honest; intending to trick or lie to people","c":"不誠實的","s":"It is dishonest to copy someone's homework and say it is your own.","t":"抄別人的作業還說是自己寫的，是不誠實的。"},{"w":"dishonesty","p":"n.","d":"the habit of not telling the truth","c":"不誠實","s":"To be honest, I didn't enjoy the movie very much.","t":"老實說，我不太喜歡這部電影。"},{"w":"honor","p":"n./v.","d":"to show immense public respect or reward an expert.","c":"榮譽；使增光","s":"It is a great honor to represent our school at the national science fair.","t":"代表學校參加全國科展是極大的榮耀。"},{"w":"honorable","p":"adj.","d":"deserving respect because of good and fair behavior","c":"可敬的；光榮的","s":"The soldier was praised for his honorable conduct during the mission and was awarded a medal for exceptional bravery.","t":"這位士兵因在任務中的高尚行為而受到表彰，並獲得了一枚英勇勛章。"},{"w":"honored","p":"adj.","d":"feeling proud and pleased because people respect you","c":"感到榮幸的","s":"I'm honored to be invited to speak at this year's graduation ceremony.","t":"我很榮幸受邀在今年畢業典禮上致詞。"},{"w":"dishonor","p":"n.","d":"loss of respect; shame","c":"恥辱","s":"It is a great honor to represent our school at the national science fair.","t":"代表學校參加全國科展是極大的榮耀。"},{"w":"horror","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great shock and fear","c":"恐怖；驚恐","s":"To our horror, we found a cockroach in the soup.","t":"令我們驚恐的是，我們在湯裡發現一隻蟑螂。"},{"w":"horrible","p":"adj.","d":"causing horror; dreadful or very shocking","c":"可怕的；糟糕的","s":"The smell coming from the abandoned trash container was truly horrible, so everyone held their noses while walking past.","t":"廢棄垃圾子車散發出來的氣味實在太令人作嘔可怕了，以至於每個人走過時都捏住了鼻子。"},{"w":"horrify","p":"v.","d":"to shock someone very much; to make someone feel great fear","c":"使驚恐","s":"The news of the plane crash will horrify the whole country, because more than two hundred people were on board.","t":"飛機失事的消息將會震驚全國，因為機上有兩百多人。"},{"w":"horrified","p":"adj.","d":"feeling great shock and fear","c":"（人）感到驚恐的","s":"We were horrified to see a dog left alone in a hot car.","t":"看到一隻狗被獨自留在悶熱的車裡，我們嚇壞了。"},{"w":"horrifying","p":"adj.","d":"very shocking and frightening","c":"令人驚恐的","s":"The film shows horrifying pictures of the war, so the teacher warned us that some scenes would be hard to watch.","t":"這部影片呈現了令人驚駭的戰爭畫面，所以老師警告我們有些場景會很難看下去。"},{"w":"hospitable","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and generous to visitors","c":"好客的","s":"The people in Penghu were very hospitable and invited us into their homes.","t":"澎湖人非常好客，邀請我們到家裡坐坐。"},{"w":"hospitality","p":"n.","d":"friendly and generous behavior toward visitors","c":"好客；款待","s":"We were impressed by the warm hospitality of the hotel staff.","t":"飯店員工的熱情款待讓我們印象深刻。"},{"w":"inhospitable","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to live in because of harsh conditions","c":"不適居住的；冷淡的","s":"The desert is an inhospitable place where few plants or animals can survive.","t":"沙漠是個不適居住的地方，很少動植物能存活。"},{"w":"hostile","p":"adj.","d":"unfriendly and showing that you are against someone","c":"有敵意的","s":"The new student felt the class was hostile, but it was only because they were shy.","t":"新同學覺得班上對他不友善，其實只是大家害羞。"},{"w":"hostility","p":"n.","d":"unfriendly or angry feelings or behavior","c":"敵意","s":"Online comments can be full of hostility, so think twice before you post.","t":"網路留言可能充滿敵意，所以發文前要三思。"},{"w":"hostilities","p":"n.","d":"fighting in a war","c":"（複數）戰爭；交戰","s":"After months of fighting, the two countries finally agreed to end hostilities.","t":"經過數月的戰鬥，兩國終於同意停戰。"}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"hug – infect · 15 字族 · 36 題","cards":[{"w":"hug","p":"v./n.","d":"holding someone in your arms to show love","c":"擁抱","s":"Mom gave me a big hug when I got home from summer camp.","t":"我從夏令營回到家時，媽媽給了我一個大大的擁抱。"},{"w":"hugged","p":"v.","d":"held someone closely in your arms","c":"擁抱（過去式）","s":"Mom gave me a big hug when I got home from summer camp.","t":"我從夏令營回到家時，媽媽給了我一個大大的擁抱。"},{"w":"hugging","p":"v.","d":"holding someone closely in your arms","c":"擁抱（V-ing）","s":"The two friends were hugging and crying at the airport.","t":"兩個朋友在機場相擁而泣。"},{"w":"idea","p":"n.","d":"a thought or a plan in your mind","c":"主意；想法","s":"Going to the night market after the concert sounds like a great idea!","t":"演唱會後去逛夜市聽起來是個好主意！。"},{"w":"ideal","p":"adj./n.","d":"perfect; the best possible","c":"理想的；理想","s":"The weather was ideal for a picnic.","t":"這天氣很適合野餐。"},{"w":"ideally","p":"adv.","d":"in the best possible situation","c":"理想上；最好是","s":"Ideally, you should get at least eight hours of sleep every night.","t":"理想上，你每晚應至少睡八小時。"},{"w":"identify","p":"v.","d":"to recognize someone or something and say who or what they are","c":"辨認；確認","s":"Can you identify the bird in this picture?","t":"你能認出這張照片裡的鳥嗎？。"},{"w":"identity","p":"n.","d":"who or what a person is","c":"身分","s":"He struggles with his cultural identity.","t":"他為自己的文化身份感到困惑。"},{"w":"identification","p":"n.","d":"proof of who you are, such as a passport; the act of recognizing someone or something","c":"身分證明；辨認","s":"You need to show some identification, such as a student card, to enter.","t":"入場須出示學生證等身分證明。"},{"w":"identical","p":"adj.","d":"exactly the same","c":"完全相同的","s":"The two fish look almost identical, but one lives only in fresh water while the other lives in the sea.","t":"這兩種魚看起來幾乎一模一樣,但一種只生活在淡水中,而另一種生活在海裡。"},{"w":"ignore","p":"v.","d":"to pay no attention to something","c":"忽視；不理會","s":"Don't ignore the warning signs on the hiking trail.","t":"不要忽視登山步道上的警告標誌。"},{"w":"ignorance","p":"n.","d":"lack of knowledge or information about something","c":"無知；不知道","s":"ignorance of the historical context may lead to a misinterpretation of the event.","t":"對歷史背景的無知可能會導致對事件的誤解。"},{"w":"ignorant","p":"adj.","d":"not knowing about something; not educated","c":"無知的；不知道的","s":"Many people are ignorant of the dangers of using a phone while crossing the street.","t":"很多人不知道邊過馬路邊用手機的危險。"},{"w":"ill","p":"adj./adv.","d":"not feeling well; suffering from a disease or sickness","c":"生病的；惡劣地（speak ill of 說壞話）","s":"Grandpa has been ill since last winter, so we visit him often.","t":"爺爺從去年冬天就一直生病，所以我們常去看他。"},{"w":"illness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being sick","c":"疾病","s":"Because of his illness, Mr. Wang had to stay in hospital for a month.","t":"王先生因病必須住院一個月。"},{"w":"illnesses","p":"n.","d":"diseases or health problems","c":"疾病（複數）","s":"Smoking can lead to serious illnesses such as lung cancer and heart disease.","t":"吸菸可能導致肺癌、心臟病等嚴重疾病。"},{"w":"illustrate","p":"v.","d":"to explain something by giving examples; to draw pictures for a book","c":"畫插圖；舉例說明","s":"The book is illustrate by a famous artist.","t":"這本書是由一位著名藝術家插畫的。"},{"w":"illustration","p":"n.","d":"a picture in a book; an example that explains something","c":"插圖；例證","s":"The illustration in the book brought the story to life.","t":"書中的插畫使故事栩栩如生。"},{"w":"illustrator","p":"n.","d":"an artist who draws pictures for books or magazines","c":"插畫家","s":"Mia hopes to become an illustrator and draw pictures for children's books.","t":"米亞希望成為插畫家，替兒童書畫圖。"},{"w":"imagine","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture in your mind","c":"想像","s":"Can you imagine living without a phone for a month?","t":"你能想像一個月不用手機嗎？"},{"w":"imagination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to form pictures and ideas in your mind","c":"想像力","s":"Children have a wonderful imagination, and a simple cardboard box can become a spaceship or a castle in their games.","t":"孩子們擁有奇妙的想像力,一個簡單的紙箱在他們的遊戲中就能變成太空船或城堡。"},{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing new and interesting ideas","c":"富有想像力的","s":"Wen is the most imaginative student in our art class; her drawings are full of strange creatures.","t":"雯是美術班上最有想像力的學生；她的畫充滿奇怪的生物。"},{"w":"imaginary","p":"adj.","d":"existing only in your mind, not real","c":"想像中的；虛構的","s":"When she was little, my sister had an imaginary friend called Lulu who lived under her bed.","t":"我妹妹小時候有個叫 Lulu 的假想朋友住在她床底下。"},{"w":"immediate","p":"adj.","d":"occurring or done at once; direct and without delay","c":"立即的；直接的","s":"The new bus lane had an immediate effect on traffic; cars started moving faster the very first day.","t":"新公車專用道帶來立即的效果，第一天車流就變快了。"},{"w":"immediately","p":"adv.","d":"used to say something happens right away","c":"立刻","s":"When the bell rang, the students immediately packed their bags and rushed out of the classroom.","t":"鐘聲一響，學生們立刻收拾書包衝出教室。"},{"w":"immediacy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being urgent and happening now","c":"即時性","s":"The immediacy of the energy crisis forced leaders to act quickly, but some of their decisions were not well planned.","t":"能源危機的迫切性迫使領導人迅速行動，但他們有些決定並未經過周詳規劃。"},{"w":"impress","p":"v.","d":"to make someone admire or notice your top talents.","c":"使印象深刻","s":"Jason practiced the song for weeks because he wanted to impress his girlfriend.","t":"Jason 練這首歌好幾週，因為他想讓女友刮目相看。"},{"w":"impressed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling admiration for someone or something","c":"印象深刻的","s":"The judges were deeply impressed by the young pianist's performance.","t":"評審們對那位年輕鋼琴家的演奏印象深刻。"},{"w":"impression","p":"n.","d":"an idea or feeling you have about someone or something","c":"印象","s":"My first impression of the gallery was not good, but the guide's stories changed my mind completely.","t":"我對這家畫廊的第一印象不太好,但導覽員的故事完全改變了我的想法。"},{"w":"impressive","p":"adj.","d":"causing admiration","c":"令人印象深刻的","s":"His drawing skills are impressive for a twelve-year-old, so the art teacher entered his work in a national competition.","t":"以十二歲來說,他的繪畫技巧令人印象深刻,所以美術老師把他的作品送去參加全國比賽。"},{"w":"improve","p":"v.","d":"to make or become better in quality or performance","c":"改善；進步","s":"If you want to improve your listening, try watching English videos with subtitles.","t":"如果你想提升聽力，試著看有字幕的英文影片。"},{"w":"improvement","p":"n.","d":"a change that makes something better","c":"改善；進步","s":"Watt's improvement to the steam engine saved coal, so factory owners were eager to buy his machines.","t":"瓦特對蒸汽機的改進節省了煤,所以工廠老闆們都急著買他的機器。"},{"w":"improved","p":"adj.","d":"made better","c":"改良的","s":"Reading English novels every day has greatly improved my vocabulary.","t":"每天讀英文小說大大提升了我的字彙量。"},{"w":"increase","p":"v./n.","d":"to become larger in amount, number, or degree; a rise","c":"增加","s":"There has been a sharp increase in the number of tourists visiting Tainan this year.","t":"今年造訪台南的觀光客人數大幅增加。"},{"w":"increasingly","p":"adv.","d":"more and more","c":"越來越","s":"Robots are increasingly common in restaurants, and some young children have never ordered food from a person.","t":"機器人在餐廳裡越來越常見,有些小孩甚至從來沒有向真人點過餐。"},{"w":"increased","p":"adj.","d":"larger in number or amount","c":"增加的","s":"There has been a sharp increase in the number of tourists visiting Tainan this year.","t":"今年造訪台南的觀光客人數大幅增加。"},{"w":"increasing","p":"adj.","d":"becoming greater in amount or number","c":"漸增的","s":"An increasing number of teenagers are learning to code in their free time.","t":"越來越多青少年利用空閒時間學寫程式。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"free from outside control; not depending on another's authority","c":"獨立的","s":"Living alone in a foreign city taught Rachel how to cook, manage finances, and become truly independent.","t":"獨自生活在異國城市教會了瑞秋如何烹飪、打理財務，並成為一個真正獨立自主的人。"},{"w":"independence","p":"n.","d":"freedom from control or help by others","c":"獨立","s":"The United States celebrates its Independence Day on July 4th.","t":"美國在七月四日慶祝獨立紀念日。"},{"w":"independently","p":"adv.","d":"without help from others","c":"獨立地","s":"Moving into a college dorm helped Amy learn to live independently.","t":"搬進大學宿舍幫助 Amy 學會獨立生活。"},{"w":"dependent","p":"adj.","d":"needing someone or something in order to live or succeed","c":"依賴的","s":"Young children are dependent on their parents for almost everything.","t":"年幼的孩子幾乎凡事都依賴父母。"},{"w":"indicate","p":"v.","d":"to show or point to something","c":"指出；顯示","s":"Please indicate which club you want to join by ticking a box on the form.","t":"請在表格上勾選，標明你想加入哪個社團。"},{"w":"indication","p":"n.","d":"a sign that shows something is true or is happening","c":"跡象；指示","s":"The forecast gives an indication of rain tomorrow.","t":"天氣預報顯示明天有雨的跡象。"},{"w":"indicator","p":"n.","d":"a sign that shows the state of something","c":"指標","s":"The fuel indicator on my dad's car shows that the tank is almost empty.","t":"我爸車上的油表顯示油箱快空了。"},{"w":"individual","p":"n./adj.","d":"a single person","c":"個人；個別的","s":"Each individual student has a locker in the classroom.","t":"每位學生在教室都有一個置物櫃。"},{"w":"individually","p":"adv.","d":"separately, one by one","c":"個別地","s":"The teacher talked to each student individually about their test results.","t":"老師個別和每位學生討論考試結果。"},{"w":"individuality","p":"n.","d":"the qualities that make a person different from others","c":"個性","s":"The teacher talked to each student individually about their test results.","t":"老師個別和每位學生討論考試結果。"},{"w":"infect","p":"v.","d":"to pass a disease to a person, animal, or plant","c":"感染；傳染","s":"If you don't clean the cut, bacteria may infect it.","t":"如果你不清理傷口，細菌可能會感染它。"},{"w":"infection","p":"n.","d":"an illness caused by germs getting into the body","c":"感染","s":"The cut on my knee became red and hot, so the doctor said I had an infection and gave me some cream.","t":"我膝蓋上的傷口變得又紅又熱,所以醫生說我被感染了,並給了我一些藥膏。"},{"w":"infected","p":"adj.","d":"containing germs that cause disease","c":"受感染的","s":"Doctors quickly separated the patients who had been infected with the virus.","t":"醫生迅速隔離了感染病毒的病人。"},{"w":"infectious","p":"adj.","d":"(of a disease) able to spread from one person to another","c":"傳染性的","s":"Wash your hands often; the flu is highly infectious and spreads quickly in classrooms.","t":"常洗手；流感傳染力很強，在教室裡傳得很快。"}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"inhabit – invade · 15 字族 · 35 題","cards":[{"w":"inhabit","p":"v.","d":"to live in a place","c":"居住於","s":"Thousands of birds inhabit the wetlands along the river.","t":"數千隻鳥棲息在河邊的濕地。"},{"w":"inhabitant","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal that lives in a place","c":"居民","s":"The oldest inhabitant of the village is ninety-eight years old, and she still remembers when there was no electricity.","t":"這個村子最年長的居民九十八歲，她還記得沒有電的時代。"},{"w":"inhabited","p":"adj.","d":"having people or animals living there","c":"有人居住的","s":"Orchid Island is inhabited mainly by the Tao people.","t":"蘭嶼主要居住的是達悟族人。"},{"w":"uninhabited","p":"adj.","d":"with no people living there","c":"無人居住的","s":"Nobody lives on that small island; it is completely uninhabited.","t":"沒有人住在那座小島上，那裡完全無人居住。"},{"w":"initial","p":"adj.","d":"happening at the beginning; first","c":"最初的","s":"My initial reaction to the news was shock, but later I felt happy.","t":"我聽到消息的第一反應是震驚，但後來感到開心。"},{"w":"initially","p":"adv.","d":"initial · A 抽象/延伸義","c":"起初","s":"Initially, I didn't like coriander, but now I put it on everything.","t":"起初我不喜歡香菜，但現在什麼都加。"},{"w":"initials","p":"n.","d":"the first letters of a person's names","c":"姓名首字母","s":"She had her initials, J.L., printed on her pencil case.","t":"她把自己的姓名縮寫 J.L. 印在鉛筆盒上。"},{"w":"injure","p":"v.","d":"to hurt a person or animal, especially in an accident","c":"使受傷","s":"Be careful not to injure yourself while using these tools.","t":"使用這些工具時要小心不要受傷。"},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"harm done to the body","c":"傷害","s":"Chen missed the rest of the season because of a serious knee injury.","t":"陳因為嚴重的膝傷錯過了剩下的賽季。"},{"w":"injured","p":"adj.","d":"hurt","c":"受傷的","s":"After the bus accident, the injured were rushed to the nearest hospital.","t":"公車事故後，傷者被緊急送往最近的醫院。"},{"w":"the injured","p":"n.","d":"people who have been hurt in an accident","c":"傷者","s":"After the earthquake, doctors and nurses worked all night to take care of the injured in the small town.","t":"地震過後，醫生和護士整夜工作，照顧小鎮上的傷者。"},{"w":"innocent","p":"adj.","d":"not guilty of committing a specific crime.","c":"無辜的；天真的","s":"The war in that region has killed thousands of innocent people, including many children.","t":"那個地區的戰爭已奪走數千名無辜民眾的性命，其中包括許多孩童。"},{"w":"innocence","p":"n.","d":"the fact of not being guilty of a crime; lack of experience","c":"無罪；天真","s":"The lawyer worked for years to prove the man's innocence.","t":"律師花了好幾年證明那名男子的清白。"},{"w":"innocently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows no bad intention or experience","c":"天真地；無辜地","s":"\"Who, me?\" the little boy asked innocently, with chocolate all over his face.","t":"「誰？我嗎？」小男孩滿臉巧克力、一臉無辜地問。"},{"w":"innovate","p":"v.","d":"to make new ideas or ways of doing things","c":"創新","s":"Companies that fail to innovate risk falling behind in the competitive market.","t":"未能創新的公司有在競爭市場中落後的風險。"},{"w":"innovation","p":"n.","d":"a new idea, method, or invention","c":"創新；新發明","s":"The tech industry is driven by constant innovation and development.","t":"科技行業受到不斷創新和發展的推動。"},{"w":"innovative","p":"adj.","d":"using new ideas and methods","c":"創新的","s":"Taiwan is known for its innovative technology companies.","t":"台灣以創新的科技公司聞名。"},{"w":"innovator","p":"n.","d":"a person who introduces new ideas or methods","c":"創新者","s":"Steve Jobs is often called an innovator, although many people helped him create his famous products.","t":"史蒂夫·賈伯斯常被稱為創新者,雖然有很多人幫他打造出那些知名產品。"},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something good or creative","c":"激勵；啟發","s":"Her story inspired many young people to become volunteers.","t":"她的故事激勵許多年輕人成為志工。"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that gives you new ideas or makes you want to do something","c":"靈感；鼓舞","s":"The athlete's story was a great inspiration to the students, and many of them joined the school running team.","t":"那位運動員的故事對學生們是很大的鼓舞,許多人加入了學校的跑步隊。"},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel that you want to do something good","c":"激勵人心的","s":"The athlete's inspiring speech made many students want to work harder.","t":"那位運動員激勵人心的演講讓很多學生想更加努力。"},{"w":"inspired","p":"adj.","d":"having excellent, original qualities","c":"受啟發的；絕妙的","s":"A visit to the National Palace Museum inspired Ivy to study Chinese history in college.","t":"一次參觀故宮的經驗啟發了 Ivy 在大學主修中國歷史。"},{"w":"instinct","p":"n.","d":"a natural way of behaving or feeling that you are born with","c":"本能","s":"Birds build nests by instinct; no one teaches them how.","t":"鳥築巢靠的是本能，沒有人教牠們。"},{"w":"instinctive","p":"adj.","d":"done without thinking, from a natural feeling","c":"本能的","s":"A mother's love for her baby is instinctive.","t":"母親對嬰兒的愛是出於本能的。"},{"w":"instinctively","p":"adv.","d":"in a natural way, without thinking first","c":"本能地","s":"When the ball flew toward her face, Mia instinctively closed her eyes.","t":"球飛向她的臉時，米亞本能地閉上眼睛。"},{"w":"instruct","p":"v.","d":"to teach someone or tell them officially what to do","c":"指示；教導","s":"The teacher will instruct the students on how to complete the assignment.","t":"老師將指示學生如何完成作業。"},{"w":"instruction","p":"n.","d":"information on how to do something","c":"指示；說明","s":"Follow the instruction carefully to ensure the task is completed accurately.","t":"仔細遵循指示以確保任務準確完成。"},{"w":"instructor","p":"n.","d":"a person who teaches a skill or sport","c":"教練；講師","s":"Our swimming instructor taught us how to breathe under water.","t":"我們的游泳教練教我們如何在水中換氣。"},{"w":"instructive","p":"adj.","d":"giving useful information or lessons","c":"有教育意義的","s":"The defeat was instructive, because it showed the team exactly which skills they still had to practise.","t":"這場敗仗很有教育意義，因為它確切顯示了球隊還必須練習哪些技能。"},{"w":"intelligent","p":"adj.","d":"smart; good at learning","c":"聰明的","s":"She is an intelligent young woman with a bright future ahead of her.","t":"她是一位有前途的聰明年輕女性。"},{"w":"intelligence","p":"n.","d":"the ability to learn, understand, and think","c":"智力；智慧","s":"Artificial intelligence is changing the way students learn.","t":"人工智慧正在改變學生的學習方式。"},{"w":"intelligently","p":"adv.","d":"in a clever and thoughtful way","c":"聰明地","s":"Dolphins can solve problems intelligently and even use tools.","t":"海豚能聰明地解決問題，甚至會使用工具。"},{"w":"intend","p":"v.","d":"to plan to do something","c":"打算；意圖","s":"We intend to visit our grandparents in Tainan this weekend, but we will stay home if the typhoon comes closer.","t":"我們打算這個週末去台南看爺爺奶奶，但如果颱風更接近，我們就會待在家。"},{"w":"intention","p":"n.","d":"something you plan or want to do","c":"意圖","s":"I'm sorry I hurt your feelings; it was never my intention.","t":"很抱歉傷了你的心，我從來不是故意的。"},{"w":"intentional","p":"adj.","d":"done on purpose, not by accident","c":"故意的","s":"The referee decided that the push was intentional, so the player received a red card and had to leave the field.","t":"裁判判定那一推是故意的，所以該球員收到紅牌，必須離場。"},{"w":"unintentionally","p":"adv.","d":"without planning or meaning to","c":"無意地","s":"On the crowded MRT, I unintentionally stepped on a woman's foot, so I apologized right away.","t":"在擁擠的捷運上，我不小心踩到一位女士的腳，所以馬上道歉。"},{"w":"interact","p":"v.","d":"to talk to and do things with other people","c":"互動","s":"The moon and the oceans interact through gravity, and this is why the sea rises and falls twice a day.","t":"月球和海洋透過重力相互作用，而這就是海水一天漲落兩次的原因。"},{"w":"interaction","p":"n.","d":"the activity of talking and doing things together","c":"互動","s":"Online classes often lack face-to-face interaction between teachers and students.","t":"線上課程常缺乏師生面對面的互動。"},{"w":"interactive","p":"adj.","d":"allowing people and computers to respond to each other","c":"互動式的","s":"The museum has many interactive displays that let children touch and play.","t":"博物館有許多讓孩子動手玩的互動展品。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to explain the meaning of something; to change spoken words into another language","c":"解讀；口譯","s":"Different readers may interpret the same poem in different ways.","t":"不同讀者可能以不同方式解讀同一首詩。"},{"w":"interpretation","p":"n.","d":"an explanation of the meaning of something","c":"解讀；詮釋","s":"She did the interpretation during the meeting.","t":"她在會議中進行了口譯"},{"w":"interpreter","p":"n.","d":"a person who translates spoken words from one language into another","c":"口譯員","s":"The president spoke in English, and an interpreter translated his speech into Chinese.","t":"總統以英語發言，由口譯員將演說翻成中文。"},{"w":"intimate","p":"adj.","d":"very close and friendly; private and personal","c":"親密的；詳盡的","s":"Only a few intimate friends were invited to the small wedding.","t":"只有幾位親密好友受邀參加這場小型婚禮。"},{"w":"intimacy","p":"n.","d":"a close personal relationship","c":"親密","s":"Eating dinner together every evening without phones builds intimacy between family members, even if the meal is simple.","t":"每天晚上一起吃晚餐、不用手機，即使餐點簡單，也能建立家人之間的親密感。"},{"w":"intimately","p":"adv.","d":"in a very close or detailed way","c":"親密地；熟悉地","s":"She knows the city intimately because she has lived there all her life.","t":"她對這座城市瞭若指掌，因為她一輩子都住在那裡。"},{"w":"introduce","p":"v.","d":"to make someone known by name to another person","c":"介紹；引進","s":"Let me introduce you to my cousin, who just moved here from Kaohsiung.","t":"讓我介紹你認識我剛從高雄搬來的表妹。"},{"w":"introduction","p":"n.","d":"the starting chapter of an educational book item.","c":"介紹；引進；導論","s":"The introduction of the textbook provides a clear overview of the key topics students will study throughout the entire course.","t":"教科書的導論提供了學生在整個課程中將學習的關鍵主題的清晰概述。"},{"w":"introductory","p":"adj.","d":"giving basic information at the start","c":"入門的；介紹的","s":"Before the main course begins, students must take an introductory class on computer skills.","t":"主課程開始前，學生必須先上電腦技能的入門課。"},{"w":"invade","p":"v.","d":"to enter a country or place by force","c":"入侵；侵犯","s":"The enemy decided to invade in winter, because they knew the river would be frozen and easy to cross.","t":"敵人決定在冬天入侵,因為他們知道河流會結冰而容易渡過。"},{"w":"invasion","p":"n.","d":"the act of entering a place by force","c":"入侵","s":"The museum shows how the island's people fought bravely against the invasion of foreign soldiers four hundred years ago.","t":"博物館展示了四百年前島上的人民如何勇敢對抗外國士兵的入侵。"},{"w":"invader","p":"n.","d":"a person, army, or thing that enters a place by force","c":"入侵者","s":"The farmers built a high wall around the village to keep out invaders, and parts of it are still standing today.","t":"農民們在村莊周圍築起高牆以阻擋入侵者，其中一部分至今仍然屹立。"},{"w":"invasive","p":"adj.","d":"spreading quickly and harming the local plants or animals","c":"入侵性的","s":"Green iguanas are an invasive species that harms farms in southern Taiwan.","t":"綠鬣蜥是危害南台灣農作的外來入侵物種。"}]},{"unit":19,"theme":"investigate – manage · 15 字族 · 36 題","cards":[{"w":"investigate","p":"v.","d":"to try to find out the facts about something","c":"調查","s":"Scientists are trying to investigate why so many fish died in the river.","t":"科學家正試著調查為什麼河裡有這麼多魚死亡。"},{"w":"investigation","p":"n.","d":"an official attempt to find out the truth about something","c":"調查","s":"The results of the investigation will be published next month.","t":"調查結果將於下個月公布。"},{"w":"investigator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to find out the facts about something","c":"調查員","s":"The private investigator was hired by the insurance company to look into the suspicious circumstances of the claim.","t":"保險公司聘請了私人調查員，調查這起索賠案的可疑情況。"},{"w":"isolate","p":"v.","d":"to keep a person or thing separate from others","c":"隔離；孤立","s":"The researchers aim to isolate the cause of the problem.","t":"研究人員的目標是隔離問題的原因。"},{"w":"isolated","p":"adj.","d":"alone; far from others","c":"孤立的；偏遠的","s":"The little village is so isolated that there is only one bus a day.","t":"那個小村莊非常偏僻，一天只有一班公車。"},{"w":"isolation","p":"n.","d":"the state of being separate from other people or things","c":"孤立；隔離","s":"The isolation of the virus was a critical step in developing a vaccine.","t":"病毒的隔離是開發疫苗的關鍵步驟。"},{"w":"journal","p":"n.","d":"a magazine about a special subject","c":"期刊；日誌","s":"During our trip to Hualien, I kept a travel journal and wrote in it every night.","t":"我們去花蓮旅行時，我寫旅遊日誌，每晚都寫。"},{"w":"journalist","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes news reports for newspapers, TV, or the Internet","c":"記者","s":"Wei-ting wants to be a journalist and report news from around the world.","t":"薇婷想成為記者，報導世界各地的新聞。"},{"w":"journalism","p":"n.","d":"the job of writing news reports for newspapers, TV, or the Internet","c":"新聞業；新聞學","s":"After high school, Ann plans to major in journalism because she loves writing news stories.","t":"高中畢業後，安打算主修新聞學，因為她熱愛寫新聞報導。"},{"w":"legal","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by the law","c":"合法的；法律的","s":"It's not legal to park here. It's prohibited.","t":"在這裡停車是不合法的。這是禁止的"},{"w":"illegal","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed by the law","c":"違法的","s":"Selling counterfeit goods is illegal. People  with violation of the regulation will be sentenced to 3 years of jail","t":"出售假冒商品是非法的。觸犯該法規的人會被判三年徒刑"},{"w":"legally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that follows the law","c":"合法地","s":"In Taiwan, you can legally drive a car once you turn eighteen.","t":"在台灣，年滿十八歲就可以合法開車。"},{"w":"illegally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is against the law","c":"非法地","s":"The man was caught illegally selling fireworks to children.","t":"那名男子被抓到非法販賣鞭炮給小孩。"},{"w":"legalize","p":"v.","d":"to make something allowed by law","c":"使合法化","s":"Some countries have decided to legalize the use of certain drugs for medical purposes.","t":"有些國家已決定將某些藥物合法用於醫療用途。"},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"an old story from the past that may not be true","c":"傳說；傳奇人物","s":"According to legend, a white snake once lived by West Lake.","t":"根據傳說，曾有一條白蛇住在西湖邊。"},{"w":"legendary","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and admired, especially over a long time","c":"傳奇的；傳說中的","s":"The legendary guitarist played a free concert in the park, and fans travelled from other cities to see him.","t":"這位傳奇吉他手在公園舉辦免費音樂會,歌迷從其他城市遠道而來看他。"},{"w":"legends","p":"n. pl.","d":"old stories that may not be true","c":"傳說","s":"Grandpa loves telling us old legends about the mountain spirits.","t":"爺爺很愛講關於山靈的古老傳說給我們聽。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"free time when you are not working","c":"空閒；休閒","s":"Swimming and hiking are popular leisure activities in summer.","t":"游泳和健行是夏天受歡迎的休閒活動。"},{"w":"leisurely","p":"adj./adv.","d":"relaxed and not hurried","c":"悠閒的；從容地","s":"We took a leisurely walk along the riverside after dinner.","t":"晚餐後我們沿著河濱悠閒地散步。"},{"w":"leisure time","p":"n.","d":"leisure · C 固定搭配","c":"空閒時間","s":"We took a leisurely walk along the riverside after dinner.","t":"晚餐後我們沿著河濱悠閒地散步。"},{"w":"license","p":"n./v.","d":"an official paper that allows you to do or own something","c":"執照；許可","s":"The government will license the company to operate within its borders.","t":"政府將授權該公司在其邊界內運營。"},{"w":"licensed","p":"adj.","d":"having official permission to do something","c":"有執照的","s":"Make sure your electrician is licensed before you let him change the wires in your house, or it could be very dangerous.","t":"在讓電工更換你家電線之前，務必確認他是有執照的，否則可能非常危險。"},{"w":"unlicensed","p":"adj.","d":"without official permission","c":"無照的","s":"It is dangerous to see an unlicensed doctor.","t":"看無照醫生很危險。"},{"w":"limit","p":"n./v.","d":"the greatest amount, number, or speed allowed; to restrict","c":"限制；極限","s":"Drivers must strictly obey the posted speed limit when passing school zones, or they will be fined heavily by the traffic police.","t":"駕駛人行經學校區域時必須嚴格遵守公告的速限，否則將會受到交通警察的重罰。"},{"w":"limitation","p":"n.","d":"a rule or fact that limits something; a weakness","c":"限制；侷限","s":"One limitation of chatbots is that they sometimes make up facts, so users must always check important information.","t":"聊天機器人的一個局限是它們有時會捏造事實,所以使用者必須隨時查核重要資訊。"},{"w":"limited","p":"adj.","d":"small in amount or number","c":"有限的","s":"Only a limited number of tickets are available, so book yours early.","t":"票數有限，請及早訂購。"},{"w":"unlimited","p":"adj.","d":"without any limit","c":"無限的","s":"This phone plan gives you unlimited data, so you can watch videos all day without worrying.","t":"這個方案提供無限流量，你可以整天看影片不用擔心。"},{"w":"literal","p":"adj.","d":"following the exact, basic meaning of words","c":"字面的；逐字的","s":"The literal meaning of \"break a leg\" is very different from what it really means.","t":"「break a leg」的字面意思和它的真正意思差很多。"},{"w":"literally","p":"adv.","d":"in the exact, basic meaning of the words","c":"照字面地；真的","s":"When I said I was dying of hunger, I didn't mean it literally!","t":"我說我快餓死了，不是字面上的意思啦！。"},{"w":"literature","p":"n.","d":"written works such as novels, poems, and plays","c":"文學","s":"My brother is studying English literature at university, so he reads novels by Dickens and plays by Shakespeare every week.","t":"我哥哥在大學讀英國文學，所以他每週都讀狄更斯的小說和莎士比亞的戲劇。"},{"w":"literary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with literature or writing","c":"文學的","s":"She won a literary prize for her first novel.","t":"她的第一部小說獲得文學獎。"},{"w":"literate","p":"adj.","d":"able to read and write","c":"識字的","s":"Today, young people need to be computer literate.","t":"現在年輕人需要具備電腦能力。"},{"w":"illiterate","p":"adj.","d":"unable to read or write","c":"不識字的","s":"In the past, many farmers were illiterate because they had never gone to school.","t":"過去許多農民不識字，因為他們從沒上過學。"},{"w":"literacy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to read and write","c":"讀寫能力","s":"Reading stories to children at home helps improve their literacy.","t":"在家唸故事給孩子聽有助提升他們的讀寫能力。"},{"w":"locate","p":"v.","d":"to find the exact position of something","c":"找出…的位置","s":"Can you help me locate the nearest convenience store on this map?","t":"你能幫我在地圖上找出最近的便利商店嗎？。"},{"w":"location","p":"n.","d":"a place or position","c":"位置；地點","s":"The location of the conference will be announced later.","t":"會議的地點將在稍後宣布。"},{"w":"located","p":"adj.","d":"in a particular place","c":"位於…的","s":"The museum is located near the MRT station, so it is easy to get to.","t":"博物館位於捷運站附近，交通方便。"},{"w":"relocate","p":"v.","d":"to move animals to a new place","c":"搬遷","s":"The team had to relocate the turtle eggs to a safer beach, because the old beach was going to flood during the typhoon.","t":"團隊必須把海龜蛋移置到較安全的海灘，因為原本的海灘在颱風期間將會淹水。"},{"w":"maintain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something in good condition","c":"維持；保養","s":"It's not easy to maintain a healthy diet when there are so many night markets around.","t":"周圍有這麼多夜市，要維持健康飲食並不容易。"},{"w":"maintenance","p":"n.","d":"the work of keeping something in good condition","c":"維修；保養","s":"The machine requires regular maintenance.","t":"機器需要定期維護。"},{"w":"maintainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be kept in good condition","c":"可維持的","s":"It's not easy to maintain a healthy diet when there are so many night markets around.","t":"周圍有這麼多夜市，要維持健康飲食並不容易。"},{"w":"majesty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being very beautiful, large, and impressive","c":"雄偉；威嚴；陛下","s":"The majesty of Taroko Gorge left the tourists speechless.","t":"太魯閣峽谷的雄偉讓遊客說不出話來。"},{"w":"majestic","p":"adj.","d":"very beautiful, large, and impressive","c":"雄偉的；莊嚴的","s":"From the top of the hill, we had a majestic view of the Pacific Ocean.","t":"我們從山頂上看到太平洋的壯麗景色。"},{"w":"majestically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is grand and impressive","c":"雄偉地","s":"An eagle flew majestically over the valley.","t":"一隻老鷹雄偉地飛越山谷。"},{"w":"major","p":"adj./v./n.","d":"very important or big","c":"主要的；重大的；主修；主修科目","s":"Air pollution is a major problem in many big cities.","t":"空氣污染是許多大城市的主要問題。"},{"w":"majority","p":"n.","d":"more than half of a group","c":"大多數","s":"The majority of my classmates use AI to check grammar, but only a few use it to write whole paragraphs.","t":"我的同學中大多數都用人工智慧檢查文法,但只有少數人用它寫整段文章。"},{"w":"manage","p":"v.","d":"To be in control of a business, team, organization, or time.","c":"管理；設法做到","s":"Mr. Lin has to manage a large team of software engineers, so he always arrives at the office early to plan their daily tasks.","t":"林先生必須管理一個由軟體工程師組成的大型團隊，因此他總是提早到達辦公室來規劃他們每日的任務。"},{"w":"management","p":"n.","d":"the people who control a company","c":"管理","s":"The management decided to close the factory, so hundreds of workers protested outside the head office.","t":"管理階層決定關閉工廠，所以數百名工人在總公司外抗議。"},{"w":"manager","p":"n.","d":"a person responsible for controlling or administering an organization or staff","c":"經理","s":"The manager of the bubble tea shop asked all the workers to arrive ten minutes early.","t":"手搖飲店的經理要求所有員工提早十分鐘到。"},{"w":"manageable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to deal with or control","c":"可應付的","s":"Breaking a big project into small steps makes it more manageable.","t":"把大型專題拆成小步驟會讓它更容易應付。"}]},{"unit":20,"theme":"manipulate – motive · 15 字族 · 39 題","cards":[{"w":"manipulate","p":"v.","d":"to control or influence someone in a clever and unfair way","c":"操縱；控制","s":"Some ads try to manipulate teenagers into buying things they don't need.","t":"有些廣告試圖操縱青少年購買不需要的東西。"},{"w":"manipulation","p":"n.","d":"controlling people or things unfairly","c":"操縱","s":"The manipulation of data can lead to incorrect conclusions.","t":"數據操縱可能導致不正確的結論。"},{"w":"manipulative","p":"adj.","d":"good at controlling people unfairly","c":"善於操縱的","s":"Don't trust him; he is a manipulative person who uses others.","t":"別相信他，他是個會操縱、利用別人的人。"},{"w":"manufacture","p":"v./n.","d":"to make goods in large numbers in a factory","c":"製造","s":"The company plans to manufacture its new electric scooters in Taiwan before expanding sales to markets across Southeast Asia.","t":"這家公司計劃在台灣製造其新款電動滑板車，然後再將銷售擴展到東南亞市場。"},{"w":"manufacturer","p":"n.","d":"a company that makes goods in large numbers","c":"製造商","s":"This toy manufacturer moved its factory to another country, because the costs there were much lower.","t":"這家玩具製造商把工廠遷到另一個國家,因為那裡的成本低得多。"},{"w":"manufacturing","p":"n.","d":"making goods in large numbers in factories","c":"製造業","s":"Taiwan is famous for manufacturing computer chips.","t":"台灣以製造電腦晶片聞名。"},{"w":"marvel","p":"v./n.","d":"a wonderful and surprising thing or person","c":"驚嘆；奇蹟；奇觀","s":"Taipei 101 is a marvel of modern engineering.","t":"台北101是現代工程的奇蹟。"},{"w":"marvelous","p":"adj.","d":"very, very good; wonderful","c":"令人驚嘆的","s":"They had a marvelous time on their vacation.","t":"他們度過了一個奇妙的假期。"},{"w":"marvelously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that causes great wonder or is extraordinarily good.","c":"極好地","s":"The little girl played the violin marvelously well for her age.","t":"以她的年紀來說，小女孩小提琴拉得極好。"},{"w":"measure","p":"v./n.","d":"an action taken to deal with a problem (often plural: measures)","c":"測量；措施","s":"They measured the length of the room.","t":"他們測量了房間的長度。"},{"w":"measurement","p":"n.","d":"a size or amount found by measuring","c":"測量；尺寸","s":"Every part needed an exact measurement, or the machine would not fit together properly at the end.","t":"每個零件都需要精確的尺寸,否則機器最後就無法正確組裝。"},{"w":"measurable","p":"adj.","d":"large enough to be noticed or measured","c":"可測量的","s":"Teachers hope to see measurable progress in students' reading skills by June.","t":"老師們希望在六月前看到學生閱讀能力有可衡量的進步。"},{"w":"memory","p":"n.","d":"the power to remember things","c":"記憶；回憶","s":"My grandmother has a poor memory and often forgets where she puts her glasses.","t":"奶奶記性不好，常忘記眼鏡放在哪。"},{"w":"memorize","p":"v.","d":"to learn something so that you can remember it exactly","c":"背誦；記住","s":"She used flashcards to memorize the vocabulary list and tested herself every evening before going to sleep.","t":"她用卡片來背誦詞彙表，每天晚上睡覺前自我測試。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"worth remembering; special","c":"難忘的","s":"Our class trip to Kenting was one of the most memorable experiences of my high school life.","t":"去墾丁的班遊是我高中最難忘的經驗之一。"},{"w":"memorial","p":"n./adj.","d":"a building or statue built to remember a person or event","c":"紀念館；紀念的","s":"Thousands of visitors come to the war memorial every year to lay flowers and remember the soldiers who died.","t":"每年有成千上萬的遊客來到戰爭紀念碑獻花，緬懷陣亡的士兵。"},{"w":"mercy","p":"n.","d":"kindness shown to someone you could punish or hurt","c":"仁慈；寬恕","s":"The frightened soldiers begged for mercy.","t":"受驚的士兵們求饒。"},{"w":"merciful","p":"adj.","d":"kind and forgiving towards people","c":"仁慈的","s":"The judge was merciful and gave the young thief a second chance.","t":"法官很仁慈，給了那名年輕小偷第二次機會。"},{"w":"merciless","p":"adj.","d":"showing no kindness or pity","c":"無情的","s":"The merciless summer sun beat down on the farmers all afternoon, and several of them had to stop working and rest in the shade.","t":"無情的夏日烈陽整個下午照在農夫身上，好幾個人不得不停下工作，到樹蔭下休息。"},{"w":"mercilessly","p":"adv.","d":"in a cruel way, without kindness","c":"無情地","s":"The judge was merciful and gave the young thief a second chance.","t":"法官很仁慈，給了那名年輕小偷第二次機會。"},{"w":"mere","p":"adj.","d":"used to say that something is small or not important","c":"僅僅的","s":"He paid a mere NT$50 for that old comic book.","t":"他只花了區區五十元就買到那本舊漫畫。"},{"w":"merely","p":"adv.","d":"only; nothing more than","c":"僅僅；只不過","s":"I was merely asking a question; I didn't mean to be rude.","t":"我只是在問問題，並沒有冒犯的意思。"},{"w":"merest","p":"adj.","d":"very small; only","c":"極微小的","s":"I was merely asking a question; I didn't mean to be rude.","t":"我只是在問問題，並沒有冒犯的意思。"},{"w":"minimum","p":"n./adj.","d":"the smallest possible or allowed","c":"最低限度；最低的","s":"You need a minimum score of 60 to pass the test.","t":"你至少要考六十分才能通過考試。"},{"w":"minimal","p":"adj.","d":"very small in amount or degree; the least possible","c":"極少的","s":"The typhoon caused only minimal damage to our town.","t":"颱風只對我們鎮造成極輕微的損害。"},{"w":"minimize","p":"v.","d":"to reduce something to the smallest possible amount or degree","c":"減到最少","s":"Wearing a helmet when you ride a scooter can minimize the risk of serious head injury in an accident.","t":"騎機車時戴安全帽，可以把發生事故時頭部重傷的風險減到最低。"},{"w":"misery","p":"n.","d":"great suffering or unhappiness","c":"痛苦；悲慘","s":"The earthquake brought great misery to the village, and many families lost their homes and had to live in tents.","t":"地震為這個村莊帶來巨大的痛苦，許多家庭失去家園，必須住在帳篷裡。"},{"w":"miserable","p":"adj.","d":"very unhappy or uncomfortable","c":"痛苦的；悲慘的","s":"I felt miserable when I had the flu and couldn't go to the concert.","t":"我得了流感沒能去演唱會，覺得好慘。"},{"w":"miserably","p":"adv.","d":"in a very unhappy way; very badly","c":"悲慘地；徹底地","s":"Jack failed miserably in his first driving test.","t":"傑克第一次駕照考試慘敗。"},{"w":"mislead","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe something false","c":"誤導","s":"Don't let one bad online review mislead you; most customers love this beef noodle shop.","t":"別讓一則負評誤導你，大多數客人都很喜歡這家牛肉麵店。"},{"w":"misled","p":"v.","d":"caused someone to believe something wrong","c":"誤導（過去式／過去分詞）","s":"The confusing signs at the train station misled dozens of tourists last weekend.","t":"上週末火車站令人困惑的指標誤導了好幾十位遊客。"},{"w":"misleading","p":"adj.","d":"giving the wrong idea","c":"誤導的；騙人的","s":"The ad was misleading; the \"free\" gift actually cost NT$200.","t":"這則廣告會誤導人；那個「免費」贈品其實要兩百元。"},{"w":"mobile","p":"adj.","d":"able to move easily from place to place","c":"可移動的；行動的","s":"The hospital has a mobile robot that travels between floors, and it can even take the lift by itself.","t":"醫院有一台在樓層間移動的可移動式機器人,它甚至能自己搭電梯。"},{"w":"mobility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to move or travel easily","c":"行動力；流動性","s":"Cars gave people much more mobility, so they could take jobs in other towns without moving house.","t":"汽車給了人們更多的移動能力,所以他們不必搬家就能在其他城鎮工作。"},{"w":"immobile","p":"adj.","d":"not moving or not able to move","c":"不能動的","s":"After breaking her hip, Grandma was immobile for weeks and needed a wheelchair.","t":"奶奶髖骨骨折後好幾週無法行動，需要坐輪椅。"},{"w":"mobilize","p":"v.","d":"to bring people together and get them ready to act","c":"動員","s":"After the earthquake, the government moved quickly to mobilize soldiers and volunteers to search for people trapped under fallen buildings.","t":"地震後，政府迅速動員軍人和志工，搜救被困在倒塌建築下的人。"},{"w":"modest","p":"adj.","d":"not talking proudly about your own abilities or success","c":"謙虛的；樸素的","s":"Their family lives in a modest apartment near the night market.","t":"他們一家住在夜市附近一間樸素的公寓。"},{"w":"modestly","p":"adv.","d":"by a small amount; not very much","c":"謙虛地","s":"When she won first prize, Lily modestly said that she had just been lucky.","t":"莉莉得到第一名時，謙虛地說她只是運氣好。"},{"w":"modesty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of not talking proudly about yourself","c":"謙虛","s":"His modesty was one of the qualities people admired most about him, even after he became a world-famous scientist.","t":"即使在他成為世界著名科學家之後，他的謙遜仍是人們最欣賞他的品質之一。"},{"w":"modify","p":"v.","d":"to change something slightly, especially to improve it","c":"修改；改造","s":"If the recipe is too sweet for you, you can modify it by using less sugar.","t":"如果食譜對你來說太甜，可以減少糖量來修改。"},{"w":"modification","p":"n.","d":"a small change","c":"修改","s":"Several modifications to the original design were made to improve performance.","t":"對原始設計進行了幾次修改以提高性能。"},{"w":"modified","p":"adj.","d":"changed a little","c":"改良的；修改過的","s":"Some farmers grow modified crops that can survive with less water.","t":"有些農民種植改良過、用水較少也能存活的作物。"},{"w":"moral","p":"adj./n.","d":"about right and wrong; a lesson from a story","c":"道德的；寓意；教訓","s":"The moral of this fable is that slow and steady wins the race.","t":"這則寓言的寓意是穩紮穩打才能獲勝。"},{"w":"morality","p":"n.","d":"ideas about what is right and wrong behavior","c":"道德","s":"Some people think downloading movies for free is fine, but others say it is a question of morality, because the filmmakers get nothing.","t":"有些人認為免費下載電影沒關係，但另一些人說這是道德問題，因為電影製作者什麼都得不到。"},{"w":"immoral","p":"adj.","d":"not following accepted standards of right and wrong","c":"不道德的","s":"Many people think it is immoral to cheat on an exam.","t":"很多人認為考試作弊是不道德的。"},{"w":"morally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to standards of good and bad behavior","c":"道德上","s":"Stealing from a poor person is morally wrong.","t":"偷窮人的東西在道德上是錯的。"},{"w":"motive","p":"n.","d":"the reason why a person does something, especially something bad","c":"動機","s":"Money is the main motive for most poachers, so helping villagers find other jobs can reduce hunting.","t":"金錢是大多數盜獵者的主要動機，所以幫助村民找到其他工作可以減少獵捕。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something or work hard","c":"激勵","s":"A good teacher knows how to motivate students to keep learning.","t":"好老師知道如何激勵學生持續學習。"},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the reason or desire that makes you want to do something","c":"動力；動機","s":"Lack of motivation is a common problem among students during summer vacation.","t":"缺乏動力是學生暑假常見的問題。"},{"w":"motivated","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong reason or desire to do something.","c":"有動力的","s":"Students who are highly motivated usually do their homework without being told.","t":"動機強的學生通常不用人提醒就會寫作業。"}]},{"unit":21,"theme":"mourn – offer · 15 字族 · 36 題","cards":[{"w":"mourn","p":"v.","d":"to feel and show great sadness because someone has died","c":"哀悼","s":"The whole country mourned the death of the beloved singer.","t":"舉國哀悼這位深受喜愛的歌手辭世。"},{"w":"mournful","p":"adj.","d":"very sad","c":"悲傷的","s":"The mournful sound of the temple bell at dusk made the empty street feel even lonelier than usual.","t":"黃昏時寺廟鐘聲哀傷的聲音，讓空蕩的街道顯得比平常更寂寞。"},{"w":"mourner","p":"n.","d":"a person at a funeral who is sad because someone has died","c":"弔唁者","s":"Hundreds of mourners dressed in black walked slowly behind the car that carried the coffin through the quiet streets.","t":"數百名身穿黑衣的送葬者緩緩走在載著棺木的車後面，穿過安靜的街道。"},{"w":"mourning","p":"n.","d":"the period of great sadness after someone has died","c":"哀悼","s":"The family stayed home in mourning for a week after Grandfather died, and neighbors brought them food every evening.","t":"爺爺過世後，全家在家服喪一週，鄰居每天晚上都送食物來。"},{"w":"mud","p":"n.","d":"wet, soft ground","c":"泥巴","s":"The kids came home covered in mud after playing football.","t":"孩子們踢完足球回家時全身是泥巴。"},{"w":"muddy","p":"adj.","d":"covered in mud or full of mud","c":"泥濘的","s":"After the heavy rain, the hiking trail on Yangmingshan was muddy and slippery.","t":"大雨過後，陽明山的步道又泥濘又滑。"},{"w":"muddier","p":"adj.","d":"more covered with wet earth","c":"更泥濘的","s":"The path became even muddier after the second typhoon hit.","t":"第二個颱風來襲後，小路變得更泥濘。"},{"w":"multiply","p":"v.","d":"to increase greatly in number","c":"乘；倍增","s":"If you multiply 6 by 7, you get 42.","t":"六乘以七等於四十二。"},{"w":"multiple","p":"adj.","d":"involving many people or things; more than one","c":"多重的","s":"The driver was taken to the hospital with multiple injuries after his car hit a tree on the mountain road last night.","t":"昨晚那名駕駛的車在山路上撞樹後，身上帶著多處傷被送往醫院。"},{"w":"multiplication","p":"n.","d":"adding a number to itself a certain number of times, such as 3 × 4","c":"乘法","s":"We learned multiplication tables in the second grade.","t":"我們在二年級學了九九乘法表。"},{"w":"mystery","p":"n.","d":"something strange that cannot be explained or understood.","c":"謎","s":"The disappearance of the old lighthouse keeper remains a complete mystery that no one has been able to solve.","t":"老燈塔看守人的失蹤至今仍是一個完整的謎，沒有人能夠解開。"},{"w":"mysterious","p":"adj.","d":"strange and not understood or explained","c":"神秘的","s":"Dark matter is one of the most mysterious things in science, because we know it exists but cannot see it.","t":"暗物質是科學中最神秘的東西之一，因為我們知道它存在，但卻看不到它。"},{"w":"mysteriously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is strange or secret.","c":"神秘地","s":"My bike mysteriously disappeared from the parking lot last night.","t":"我的腳踏車昨晚莫名其妙從停車場消失了。"},{"w":"nap","p":"n./v.","d":"a short sleep during the day","c":"小睡；午睡","s":"My little brother usually takes a short nap after lunch.","t":"我弟弟通常午飯後小睡片刻。"},{"w":"napped","p":"v.","d":"slept for a short time during the day","c":"nap 過去式（重複 p）","s":"My little brother usually takes a short nap after lunch.","t":"我弟弟通常午飯後小睡片刻。"},{"w":"napping","p":"v.","d":"sleeping for a short time during the day","c":"nap 現在分詞（重複 p）","s":"Shh! The baby is napping in the bedroom.","t":"噓！寶寶正在臥室裡睡覺。"},{"w":"navigate","p":"v.","d":"to find the way to a place, especially by ship or plane","c":"導航；找路","s":"Ancient sailors used the stars to navigate across the Pacific, although they had no maps or modern instruments.","t":"古代水手利用星星航行橫越太平洋,儘管他們沒有地圖或現代儀器。"},{"w":"navigation","p":"n.","d":"the skill or process of finding the way from one place to another","c":"導航","s":"Modern navigation depends on satellites, but sailors still learn to use maps in case the electronic system fails.","t":"現代導航仰賴衛星,但水手仍然學習使用地圖,以防電子系統故障。"},{"w":"navigator","p":"n.","d":"a person who plans the route of a ship, plane, or car","c":"領航員","s":"The ship's navigator checked the map carefully during the storm.","t":"暴風雨中，船上的領航員仔細查看地圖。"},{"w":"normal","p":"adj.","d":"usual or ordinary","c":"正常的；一般的","s":"It's normal to feel nervous before an exam.","t":"考試前感到緊張是正常的。"},{"w":"normally","p":"adv.","d":"usually; in the usual way","c":"通常","s":"My grandpa normally takes a walk in the park after dinner.","t":"我爺爺通常晚餐後會去公園散步。"},{"w":"abnormal","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is usual or expected, often in a bad way","c":"不正常的","s":"The doctor found something abnormal in the X-ray and asked for more tests.","t":"醫生在 X 光片中發現異常，要求做更多檢查。"},{"w":"normality","p":"n.","d":"the state of being normal","c":"常態","s":"After two years of the pandemic, life slowly returned to normality, and people travelled abroad again.","t":"經過兩年的疫情,生活慢慢恢復常態,人們又開始出國旅行。"},{"w":"nurse","p":"n./v.","d":"to feed a baby with milk from its mother","c":"護理師；照顧；看護","s":"The nurse checked my temperature and gave me some medicine.","t":"護理師量了我的體溫並給我一些藥。"},{"w":"nursing","p":"n.","d":"the job of caring for sick people","c":"護理","s":"My sister is studying nursing at university because she wants to help patients.","t":"我姐姐在大學念護理，因為她想幫助病人。"},{"w":"nursery","p":"n.","d":"a place where young children are cared for while their parents are at work","c":"托兒所；苗圃","s":"Mangrove roots are a nursery for young fish, because larger fish cannot swim between the thick roots.","t":"紅樹林的根部是幼魚的育幼場,因為較大的魚無法在茂密的根之間游動。"},{"w":"nutrition","p":"n.","d":"the food you eat and the way it affects your health","c":"營養","s":"Good nutrition is important for growing teenagers.","t":"良好的營養對成長中的青少年很重要。"},{"w":"nutritious","p":"adj.","d":"full of the things your body needs to stay healthy","c":"營養的","s":"Sweet potatoes are cheap and nutritious, so my grandmother says they helped many families survive during hard times.","t":"地瓜既便宜又有營養，所以我奶奶說它在艱困時期幫助許多家庭活了下來。"},{"w":"nutrient","p":"n.","d":"a substance in food that plants, animals, and people need to live and grow","c":"養分","s":"Plants take in each nutrient they need through their roots, so farmers test the soil to see what is missing.","t":"植物透過根部吸收所需的每一種養分，所以農民會檢測土壤，看看缺少了什麼。"},{"w":"nutritionist","p":"n.","d":"an expert on food and healthy eating","c":"營養師","s":"The school nutritionist plans healthy lunches for all students.","t":"學校營養師為所有學生規劃健康午餐。"},{"w":"obey","p":"v.","d":"to submit to the authority of someone or comply with rules","c":"服從；遵守","s":"All students must obey the school rules.","t":"所有學生都必須遵守校規。"},{"w":"obedient","p":"adj.","d":"doing what you are told to do","c":"順從的","s":"Our new puppy is very obedient; it sits down, stays, and comes back as soon as my sister calls its name.","t":"我們的新小狗非常聽話；只要我妹妹叫牠的名字，牠就會坐下、待著不動，然後跑回來。"},{"w":"obedience","p":"n.","d":"doing what you are told to do","c":"服從","s":"The dog trainer taught basic obedience to the puppies, and soon they could sit and wait on command.","t":"訓犬師教小狗們基本的服從訓練,很快牠們就能聽口令坐下和等待。"},{"w":"disobey","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to do what you are told to do","c":"違抗","s":"If you disobey your coach and skip practice again, you will not be allowed to play in the final game next week.","t":"如果你再違抗教練、不來練習，下週的決賽你就不能上場。"},{"w":"disobedient","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to do what you are told","c":"不聽話的","s":"The disobedient child refused to go to bed and kept jumping on the sofa.","t":"那個不聽話的孩子不肯上床，一直在沙發上跳。"},{"w":"observe","p":"v.","d":"to obey a rule or law; to celebrate a holiday","c":"觀察；遵守","s":"Many families gathered on rooftops to observe the full moon during the Mid-Autumn Festival.","t":"中秋節時許多家庭聚在頂樓賞月。"},{"w":"observation","p":"n.","d":"the act of watching something carefully","c":"觀察","s":"Careful observation of boiling water gave him an idea, and he started to experiment with steam power.","t":"對沸水的仔細觀察給了他一個點子,而他開始實驗蒸汽動力。"},{"w":"observant","p":"adj.","d":"good at noticing things","c":"觀察敏銳的","s":"A good detective must be very observant and notice even the smallest details.","t":"好偵探必須觀察敏銳，連最小的細節都能注意到。"},{"w":"observer","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches something carefully, often officially","c":"觀察者","s":"A careful observer will notice that each crow has a slightly different call, so you can tell them apart.","t":"一位細心的觀察者會注意到每隻烏鴉的叫聲都略有不同，所以你可以分辨牠們。"},{"w":"obvious","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see or understand","c":"明顯的","s":"The answer to the riddle seemed so obvious once our teacher explained it.","t":"老師一解釋，謎題的答案就顯得很明顯。"},{"w":"obviously","p":"adv.","d":"clearly; as anyone can see","c":"明顯地；顯然","s":"Obviously, Tom hadn't studied for the test; he left half of the answers blank.","t":"顯然湯姆沒準備考試，他有一半答案空白。"},{"w":"obviousness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being easy to see or understand","c":"明顯（少用）","s":"Obviously, Tom hadn't studied for the test; he left half of the answers blank.","t":"顯然湯姆沒準備考試，他有一半答案空白。"},{"w":"occasion","p":"n.","d":"a special social event or an explicit moment.","c":"場合；時機","s":"A wedding is a special occasion, so everyone dresses up.","t":"婚禮是特別的場合，所以大家都盛裝打扮。"},{"w":"occasional","p":"adj.","d":"happening sometimes but not often","c":"偶爾的","s":"Taiwan has occasional strong earthquakes, so families are advised to keep water and torches at home.","t":"臺灣偶爾會有強烈地震，所以家家戶戶被建議在家裡準備水和手電筒。"},{"w":"occasionally","p":"adv.","d":"sometimes but not often","c":"偶爾","s":"We occasionally eat out, but usually Mom cooks dinner at home.","t":"我們偶爾外食，但通常是媽媽在家煮晚餐。"},{"w":"occupy","p":"v.","d":"to fill a space or time; to live or work in a place","c":"佔據；使忙碌","s":"Video games occupy most of my little brother's free time these days.","t":"最近電動佔據了我弟弟大部分的空閒時間。"},{"w":"occupation","p":"n.","d":"a person's job","c":"職業；佔領","s":"On the form, please write your name, age, and occupation.","t":"請在表格上寫下姓名、年齡和職業。"},{"w":"occupied","p":"adj.","d":"being used; taken over by someone","c":"使用中的；忙碌的","s":"Sorry, this seat is occupied. My friend just went to get some drinks.","t":"抱歉，這位子有人坐，我朋友剛去買飲料。"},{"w":"offer","p":"v./n.","d":"to present something for acceptance or refusal; a proposal","c":"提供；主動提議；提議；工作邀約","s":"My uncle received a job offer from a tech company in Hsinchu.","t":"我舅舅收到新竹一家科技公司的工作邀約。"},{"w":"offering","p":"n.","d":"something that is given to a god as part of worship","c":"供品；提供物","s":"Thank you for offering to help me move this weekend.","t":"謝謝你主動說要幫我這週末搬家。"}]},{"unit":22,"theme":"operate – persuade · 15 字族 · 37 題","cards":[{"w":"operate","p":"v.","d":"to make a machine work","c":"運作；操作；動手術","s":"This machine is easy to operate; just press the green button.","t":"這台機器操作簡單，按下綠色按鈕即可。"},{"w":"operation","p":"n.","d":"the action of functioning; a medical surgery or organized process","c":"手術；運作","s":"My grandfather had an operation on his knee last month.","t":"我爺爺上個月動了膝蓋手術。"},{"w":"operator","p":"n.","d":"a person who controls a machine","c":"操作員；接線員","s":"The crane operator watched the screen carefully, because one small mistake could drop the steel on the workers below.","t":"起重機操作員仔細地看著螢幕,因為一個小錯誤就可能把鋼材掉到下面的工人身上。"},{"w":"oppose","p":"v.","d":"to disagree with something and try to stop it","c":"反對","s":"Many residents oppose the plan to build a factory near the school.","t":"許多居民反對在學校附近蓋工廠的計畫。"},{"w":"opposed","p":"adj.","d":"disagreeing strongly with something","c":"反對的","s":"A: The government plans to build a new airport runway close to several villages, so what do the local farmers think about it? B: Most of them are firmly opposed to the project, because the noise will disturb their animals, and they are afraid that they will lose part of their land without fair payment.","t":"A：政府打算在幾個村莊附近興建新的機場跑道，當地農民對此有什麼看法？ B：他們大多數人堅決【反對】這項計畫，因為噪音會干擾他們的動物，而且他們擔心會在沒有合理補償的情況下失去部分土地。"},{"w":"opposition","p":"n.","d":"strong disagreement with a plan or idea; the people who disagree","c":"反對","s":"The plan to build a new airport met strong opposition from local residents.","t":"興建新機場的計畫遭到當地居民強烈反對。"},{"w":"opponent","p":"n.","d":"a person or team you compete or fight against","c":"對手","s":"Lin beat his opponent in the final match and won the gold medal.","t":"林在決賽擊敗對手，贏得金牌。"},{"w":"opposite","p":"adj./n.","d":"completely different; on the other side","c":"相反的；對面的","s":"The post office is on the opposite side of the street from the bank, right next to the small bakery.","t":"郵局在銀行對面那一側的街上，就在小麵包店旁邊。"},{"w":"oppress","p":"v.","d":"to treat people in a cruel and unfair way, especially by using power","c":"壓迫；使煩惱","s":"The cruel king oppressed his people for many years.","t":"殘暴的國王壓迫人民多年。"},{"w":"oppression","p":"n.","d":"cruel and unfair treatment by people in power","c":"壓迫；迫害","s":"Thousands of people left the country to escape oppression, hoping to find freedom and a better life across the sea.","t":"成千上萬的人離開那個國家以逃離壓迫，希望在海的另一邊找到自由和更好的生活。"},{"w":"oppressive","p":"adj.","d":"cruel and unfair; (of weather) hot and uncomfortable","c":"壓迫的；悶熱難受的","s":"The summer heat in Kaohsiung felt so oppressive that we stayed inside with the air conditioner on.","t":"高雄夏天的酷熱令人難受，所以我們開著冷氣待在室內。"},{"w":"oppressor","p":"n.","d":"a person or group that treats others cruelly and unfairly","c":"壓迫者","s":"In the movie, the villagers finally stand together and drive away the cruel oppressor who had taxed them for twenty years.","t":"電影中，村民最終團結起來，趕走了向他們課稅二十年的殘暴壓迫者。"},{"w":"organize","p":"v.","d":"to plan and arrange something; to put things in order","c":"組織；安排","s":"Our class is going to organize a charity sale to help stray dogs.","t":"我們班要舉辦義賣幫助流浪狗。"},{"w":"organization","p":"n.","d":"an organized body of people with a particular purpose, such as a business or charity","c":"組織；機構","s":"Taiwan has been an active member of the World Trade organization and continues to expand its international business partnerships.","t":"台灣一直是世界貿易組織的活躍成員，並持續拓展其國際商業夥伴關係。"},{"w":"organizer","p":"n.","d":"a person who plans and arranges an event","c":"主辦人","s":"The organizer of the charity run thanked all three hundred volunteers who had worked at the water stations along the route.","t":"慈善路跑的主辦人感謝沿路在補水站工作的全部三百位志工。"},{"w":"organized","p":"adj.","d":"well planned; good at arranging things","c":"有條理的；有組織的","s":"My sister is so organized that she writes down every homework task in her planner and never misses a deadline.","t":"我姐姐非常有條理，她把每項作業都寫在行事曆上，從不錯過期限。"},{"w":"disorganized","p":"adj.","d":"not well planned; messy","c":"雜亂無章的","s":"My desk is so disorganized that I can never find my pens.","t":"我的書桌亂到我永遠找不到筆。"},{"w":"origin","p":"n.","d":"the place or point where something begins","c":"起源","s":"The origin of the word \"robot\" is a Czech play, but now people all over the world use it.","t":"\"robot\"這個字的起源是一齣捷克劇作,但現在全世界的人都在使用它。"},{"w":"original","p":"adj./n.","d":"new and different from anything before","c":"原本的；原作","s":"The judges wanted original designs, so they rejected any poster that looked like something on the internet.","t":"評審想要原創的設計,所以他們淘汰了任何看起來像網路上作品的海報。"},{"w":"originally","p":"adv.","d":"at first","c":"原本","s":"My family originally came from Tainan, but we moved to Taipei when I was five.","t":"我家原本來自台南，但我五歲時搬到台北。"},{"w":"originate","p":"v.","d":"to start or come from a place or time","c":"起源於","s":"The Lantern Festival is believed to originate from an ancient tradition more than two thousand years ago.","t":"元宵節據信起源於兩千多年前的古老傳統。"},{"w":"outline","p":"n./v.","d":"to describe the main points of something","c":"大綱；輪廓；概述；畫出輪廓","s":"The minister outline the new energy plan on TV, but she did not explain how much it would cost.","t":"部長在電視上概述了新的能源計畫,但她沒有說明它會花多少錢。"},{"w":"all","p":"adj./pron.","d":"every one; the whole of something","c":"全部的；全部","s":"Q: Do your classmates like the new teacher? — A: Yes, they do. All of them like her.","t":"你的同學喜歡新老師嗎？ — 是的，他們喜歡。他們全部都喜歡她。"},{"w":"overall","p":"adj./adv.","d":"including everything; considered as a whole","c":"全部的；整體的；整體而言","s":"The overall cost of the class trip is NT$3,000 per student.","t":"校外教學的總費用為每位學生新台幣三千元。"},{"w":"overalls","p":"n.","d":"loose trousers with a piece covering the chest, worn for work","c":"吊帶褲；工作服","s":"The painter put on his old blue overalls before he started work, because he knew the paint would get everywhere.","t":"油漆工開工前穿上他那件舊的藍色吊帶工作褲，因為他知道油漆會沾得到處都是。"},{"w":"overseas","p":"adj./adv.","d":"to or in a foreign country","c":"海外的；國外的；在海外；到國外","s":"After graduating, Kevin went overseas to study engineering in Germany.","t":"畢業後凱文出國到德國讀工程。"},{"w":"sea","p":"n.","d":"the salt water that covers much of the earth","c":"海","s":"Q: What can your brother do in the sea? — A: He can swim and look at the fish.","t":"你哥哥在海裡可以做什麼？ — 他可以游泳和看魚。"},{"w":"pain","p":"n.","d":"the unpleasant physical feeling caused by injury or illness","c":"疼痛；痛苦","s":"After running the marathon, Tom felt a sharp pain in his left knee.","t":"跑完馬拉松後，Tom 左膝感到一陣劇痛。"},{"w":"painful","p":"adj.","d":"causing physical pain or mental suffering","c":"痛苦的；疼痛的","s":"The deep cut on Robert's right thumb was extremely painful, but the nurse treated it gently with antiseptic cream and a clean bandage.","t":"羅伯特右手大拇指上的深傷口極為令人疼痛，但護士用消毒藥膏和乾淨繃帶溫柔地進行了處理。"},{"w":"painfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a very distressing or extremely clear manner.","c":"痛苦地","s":"It was painfully obvious to everyone in the room that the speaker had not prepared adequately for the presentation.","t":"對房間裡的每個人來說，演講者沒有充分準備這次演講是極為明顯的。"},{"w":"painless","p":"adj.","d":"causing no pain","c":"無痛的","s":"Don't worry. Getting a flu shot is quick and almost painless.","t":"別擔心，打流感疫苗很快而且幾乎不痛。"},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity","c":"參加","s":"Over 200 runners will participate in the charity race this Sunday.","t":"本週日將有超過兩百名跑者參加慈善路跑。"},{"w":"participation","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in an activity","c":"參與","s":"Class participation counts for 20% of your final grade.","t":"課堂參與占學期成績的百分之二十。"},{"w":"participant","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in an activity or event","c":"參加者","s":"Each participant in the study used an AI tutor for a month, and then they took the same English test again.","t":"研究中的每位參與者都使用人工智慧家教一個月,然後再考一次相同的英文測驗。"},{"w":"passion","p":"n.","d":"a very strong interest or love for something","c":"熱情","s":"Ever since she was little, Ella has had a real passion for drawing comics.","t":"Ella 從小就熱愛畫漫畫。"},{"w":"passionate","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing very strong feelings about something","c":"熱情的；熱衷的","s":"Our science teacher is so passionate about space that she stays after school to show us the stars through her own telescope.","t":"我們的理化老師對太空非常熱愛，她放學後留下來用她自己的望遠鏡給我們看星星。"},{"w":"passionately","p":"adv.","d":"with very strong feelings","c":"熱情地","s":"The students talked passionately about how to protect the coral reefs near Kenting.","t":"學生們熱烈討論如何保護墾丁附近的珊瑚礁。"},{"w":"perform","p":"v.","d":"to entertain an audience by acting, singing, etc.","c":"表演；執行","s":"The band will perform at the Taipei Arena next Saturday.","t":"這個樂團下週六將在台北小巨蛋演出。"},{"w":"performance","p":"n.","d":"the act of entertaining an audience","c":"表演；表現","s":"Her performance in the school play was so moving that several parents wiped tears from their eyes.","t":"她在學校話劇中的演出非常感人,好幾位家長都擦了眼淚。"},{"w":"performer","p":"n.","d":"a person who acts, sings, dances, or plays music for an audience","c":"表演者","s":"The street performer in Ximending attracted a big crowd with his magic tricks.","t":"西門町的街頭藝人用魔術吸引了一大群人。"},{"w":"performing","p":"adj.","d":"doing a show in front of people","c":"表演的","s":"The band will perform at the Taipei Arena next Saturday.","t":"這個樂團下週六將在台北小巨蛋演出。"},{"w":"permit","p":"v./n.","d":"to allow something officially","c":"允許；許可證","s":"Our school permits AI for brainstorming, but it does not allow students to copy AI answers into their essays.","t":"我們學校允許用人工智慧腦力激盪,但不准學生把人工智慧的答案抄進作文裡。"},{"w":"permission","p":"n.","d":"the official token or nod allowing an action.","c":"許可；准許","s":"You need your parents' permission to join the school trip to Penghu.","t":"參加澎湖校外教學需要家長同意。"},{"w":"permitted","p":"adj.","d":"allowed","c":"被允許的","s":"You need your parents' permission to join the school trip to Penghu.","t":"參加澎湖校外教學需要家長同意。"},{"w":"persevere","p":"v.","d":"to keep trying to do something difficult without giving up","c":"堅持不懈","s":"If you persevere with your guitar practice, you'll be able to play this song by summer.","t":"如果你持續練吉他，到夏天就能彈這首歌了。"},{"w":"perseverance","p":"n.","d":"continuing to try even when progress is slow","c":"毅力","s":"Learning a language takes perseverance, because you will make many mistakes before you speak it well.","t":"學習語言需要毅力,因為在說得流利之前你會犯很多錯。"},{"w":"persevering","p":"adj.","d":"continuing to try even when it is difficult","c":"堅忍不拔的","s":"If you persevere with your guitar practice, you'll be able to play this song by summer.","t":"如果你持續練吉他，到夏天就能彈這首歌了。"},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to make someone agree to do something","c":"說服","s":"They managed to persuade her to join the team.","t":"他們成功地說服她加入了團隊"},{"w":"persuasion","p":"n.","d":"the act of making someone agree to do something by giving good reasons","c":"說服","s":"Through gentle persuasion, he got everyone to agree.","t":"通過溫和的說服，他讓每個人都同意了。"},{"w":"persuasive","p":"adj.","d":"good at making people agree with you","c":"有說服力的","s":"His persuasive speech motivated many to take action.","t":"他有說服力的演講激勵了許多人採取行動。"},{"w":"persuasively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that makes people believe or agree","c":"有說服力地","s":"In the debate, Kevin argued persuasively and won over most of the audience.","t":"辯論時 Kevin 論述很有說服力，贏得大部分聽眾的支持。"}]},{"unit":23,"theme":"photograph – preserve · 15 字族 · 37 題","cards":[{"w":"photograph","p":"n./v.","d":"a picture made using a camera; to take a picture","c":"照片；拍照","s":"The photograph on the wall shows my grandparents on their wedding day.","t":"牆上的照片是我祖父母結婚當天。"},{"w":"photographer","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes photographs, either as a job or hobby","c":"攝影師","s":"The wildlife photographer waited patiently behind camouflage netting for six hours to take pictures of rare mountain eagles.","t":"這位野生動物攝影師在偽裝網後耐心等待了六個小時，只為拍攝稀有山雕的照片。"},{"w":"photography","p":"n.","d":"the art or job of taking photos","c":"攝影（術）","s":"Ken became interested in photography after he got his first camera.","t":"肯拿到第一台相機後開始對攝影產生興趣。"},{"w":"photographic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with photographs or taking photos","c":"攝影的","s":"He has a photographic memory, so he can remember every page of a book after reading it only once.","t":"他有攝影般的記憶力，所以一本書只讀一次就能記住每一頁。"},{"w":"pilgrim","p":"n.","d":"a person who travels a long way to a holy place for religious reasons","c":"朝聖者","s":"Every spring, thousands of pilgrims walk for nine days behind the Mazu statue from Taichung to Chiayi and back.","t":"每年春天，成千上萬的香客跟在媽祖神像後面，從台中走到嘉義再走回來，共九天。"},{"w":"pilgrimage","p":"n.","d":"a journey to a holy place","c":"朝聖之旅","s":"Every spring, thousands of people join the Dajia Mazu pilgrimage, walking for nine days.","t":"每年春天，數千人參加大甲媽祖遶境進香，徒步九天。"},{"w":"pilgrims","p":"n.","d":"people who travel to a holy place","c":"朝聖者（複數）","s":"The tired pilgrims rested at a temple before continuing their long walk.","t":"疲憊的香客們在廟裡休息後再繼續長途步行。"},{"w":"plenty","p":"n.","d":"a massive count of units ensuring zero scarcity flaws.","c":"大量","s":"Don't worry about being late; we still have plenty of time.","t":"別擔心遲到，我們還有很多時間。"},{"w":"plentiful","p":"adj.","d":"existing in large amounts; more than enough","c":"豐富的","s":"Mangoes are plentiful in Tainan in the summer, so they are cheap.","t":"台南夏天芒果產量豐富，所以很便宜。"},{"w":"plentifully","p":"adv.","d":"in large amounts","c":"大量地","s":"Mangoes are plentiful in Tainan in the summer, so they are cheap.","t":"台南夏天芒果產量豐富，所以很便宜。"},{"w":"poison","p":"n./v.","d":"a substance that causes illness or death when absorbed; to harm with it","c":"毒藥；下毒","s":"Rats can be killed with poison, but it is dangerous for pets too.","t":"老鼠可以用毒藥殺死，但對寵物也很危險。"},{"w":"poisonous","p":"adj.","d":"containing poison; able to kill or harm you","c":"有毒的","s":"Be careful! Some mushrooms in the mountains are poisonous.","t":"小心！山裡有些蘑菇有毒。"},{"w":"poisoning","p":"n.","d":"illness caused by something harmful you eat or drink","c":"中毒","s":"Dozens of students got food poisoning after eating lunch boxes from the same shop.","t":"數十名學生吃了同一家店的便當後食物中毒。"},{"w":"poisoned","p":"adj.","d":"made harmful with poison","c":"被下毒的","s":"Be careful! Some mushrooms in the mountains are poisonous.","t":"小心！山裡有些蘑菇有毒。"},{"w":"pole","p":"n.","d":"the most northern or southern point of the earth","c":"極；桿子","s":"The flag was raised to the top of the pole during the school assembly.","t":"朝會時旗子被升到旗桿頂端。"},{"w":"polar","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the North or South Pole","c":"極地的；截然相反的","s":"Scientists are worried about the melting of polar ice.","t":"科學家擔心極地冰層融化。"},{"w":"politics","p":"n.","d":"the activities associated with the governance of a country or area","c":"政治；政治學","s":"The young scholar decided to pursue a career in politics after graduating from law school.","t":"這位年輕的學者在法學院畢業後決定從事政治生涯。"},{"w":"political","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the government, public affairs, or the state of a nation","c":"政治的","s":"Some seniors started a political discussion club to talk about the coming election.","t":"幾位高三生成立了政治討論社，討論即將到來的選舉。"},{"w":"politically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that relates to the government or public affairs of a nation","c":"政治上","s":"The comedian's joke was funny, but it was not politically correct.","t":"那位喜劇演員的笑話很好笑，但在政治上並不正確。"},{"w":"politician","p":"n.","d":"a person who is professionally involved in politics, especially as an elected official","c":"政治人物","s":"Wise politicians should pay much more attention to essential environmental issues like pollution.","t":"明智的政治家應該更加關注污染等至關重要的環境議題。"},{"w":"pollute","p":"v.","d":"to make air, water, or soil dirty and harmful to life","c":"污染","s":"Chemical factories must not pollute the river with untreated waste, or thousands of fish will die in the water.","t":"化學工廠絕不可用未經處理的廢棄物污染河流，否則水中成千上萬的魚群將會死亡。"},{"w":"pollution","p":"n.","d":"damage caused to water, air, or land by harmful substances","c":"污染","s":"Heavy traffic in big cities creates severe air pollution, causing serious breathing problems for young children and elderly people.","t":"大城市的擁擠交通造成了嚴重的空氣污染，導致幼童與年長者嚴重的呼吸道問題。"},{"w":"polluted","p":"adj.","d":"made dirty and harmful","c":"受污染的","s":"Factories that release harmful pollutants into the air should be fined.","t":"排放有害污染物到空氣中的工廠應被罰款。"},{"w":"pollutant","p":"n.","d":"a substance that makes air, water or land dirty","c":"污染物","s":"The factory released a dangerous pollutant into the river, and soon the fish and frogs began to disappear.","t":"那家工廠把一種危險的汙染物排進河裡，不久之後魚和青蛙就開始消失了。"},{"w":"unpolluted","p":"adj.","d":"clean, not made dirty","c":"未受污染的","s":"We found a small, unpolluted beach where the water was still clean and clear.","t":"我們找到一處小小的、未受污染的海灘，海水依然清澈。"},{"w":"poor","p":"adj.","d":"having very little money; also said when you feel sorry for someone","c":"貧窮的；差的","s":"The charity hands out free meals to poor families in the neighborhood every weekend.","t":"這個慈善團體每週末都發放免費餐點給社區的貧困家庭。"},{"w":"poverty","p":"n.","d":"the state of being very poor","c":"貧窮","s":"Millions of children around the world still live in poverty and cannot go to school.","t":"全世界仍有數百萬兒童生活貧困、無法上學。"},{"w":"poorly","p":"adv.","d":"badly","c":"差勁地；不好地","s":"Leo did poorly on the quiz because he stayed up late playing games the night before.","t":"Leo 小考考得很差，因為前一晚熬夜打電動。"},{"w":"the poor","p":"n.","d":"poor · A 延伸義","c":"窮人","s":"Every winter our school collects warm coats and gives them to the poor in the city so they can stay warm.","t":""},{"w":"possess","p":"v.","d":"to have or own something","c":"擁有；具有","s":"Many birds possess a kind of compass in their eyes, and this helps them find their way across oceans.","t":"許多鳥類眼中擁有一種指南針，而這幫助牠們找到橫越海洋的路。"},{"w":"possession","p":"n.","d":"the state of having or owning something","c":"擁有；（常複數）財物","s":"The police found the stolen bicycle in the possession of a man who said he had bought it online.","t":"警方發現失竊的腳踏車在一名男子的持有中，他說他是在網路上買的。"},{"w":"possessive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to keep someone or something only for yourself","c":"佔有慾強的","s":"My little sister is very possessive about her toys and never lets me touch them.","t":"我妹妹對她的玩具佔有慾很強，從不讓我碰。"},{"w":"powder","p":"n.","d":"a dry substance in the form of very fine grains","c":"粉；粉末","s":"The mother mixed three spoons of milk powder with warm water to prepare a bottle for her infant baby.","t":"母親將三匙奶粉與溫水混合，為她的嬰兒準備了一瓶奶。"},{"w":"powdered","p":"adj.","d":"made into powder","c":"粉狀的","s":"Grandma mixed some powdered sugar into the cream to make the cake topping.","t":"奶奶把一些糖粉拌進鮮奶油做蛋糕的裝飾。"},{"w":"powdery","p":"adj.","d":"like powder; fine and dry","c":"粉狀的；像粉的","s":"After the snowfall, the ski slopes were covered with soft, powdery snow.","t":"下雪後，滑雪坡覆蓋著鬆軟如粉的雪。"},{"w":"practice","p":"n./v.","d":"to do something again to get better","c":"練習；實踐","s":"To become proficient, you must practice daily.","t":"要熟練，你必須每天練習。"},{"w":"practical","p":"adj.","d":"useful and suitable for real situations","c":"實用的","s":"A raincoat is more practical than an umbrella when you ride a scooter.","t":"騎機車時雨衣比雨傘更實用。"},{"w":"practically","p":"adv.","d":"almost; in a real way","c":"幾乎；實際上","s":"It rained practically every day during our trip to Yilan.","t":"我們去宜蘭玩的時候幾乎天天下雨。"},{"w":"impractical","p":"adj.","d":"not sensible or possible in real life","c":"不實際的","s":"Wearing high heels to go hiking is completely impractical.","t":"穿高跟鞋去爬山完全不實際。"},{"w":"precise","p":"adj.","d":"exact and correct in every detail","c":"精確的","s":"The scientist made precise measurements to ensure the accuracy of the experiment.","t":"為確保實驗的準確性，科學家進行了精確的測量。"},{"w":"precisely","p":"adv.","d":"exactly","c":"精確地；正是","s":"The train left at precisely 7:15, so we missed it by one minute.","t":"火車在七點十五分整準時開走，我們差一分鐘沒趕上。"},{"w":"precision","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being exact and accurate","c":"精確","s":"Watchmakers in Switzerland are known for their precision and care.","t":"瑞士的鐘錶匠以精準和細心聞名。"},{"w":"imprecise","p":"adj.","d":"not exact","c":"不精確的","s":"His directions were so imprecise that we got lost twice.","t":"他的指路非常不精確，害我們迷路兩次。"},{"w":"prefer","p":"v.","d":"to like one thing or person better than another","c":"偏好","s":"During hot summer afternoons, many office workers prefer iced green tea to hot coffee.","t":"在炎熱的夏日午後，許多上班族比起熱咖啡更喜歡冰綠茶。"},{"w":"preference","p":"n.","d":"a greater liking for one thing than another","c":"偏好","s":"Do you have any preference for dinner, Japanese or Thai food?","t":"晚餐你有什麼偏好嗎？日式還是泰式？。"},{"w":"preferable","p":"adj.","d":"more attractive or suitable; chosen over alternatives.","c":"較好的","s":"In Taipei, taking the MRT is preferable to driving because of the heavy traffic.","t":"在台北，因為交通繁忙，搭捷運比開車好。"},{"w":"preferably","p":"adv.","d":"ideally; if possible, rather than another option.","c":"最好是","s":"Please submit your assignment in digital format, preferably as a PDF file, before midnight on the due date.","t":"請在截止日期午夜前以數位格式提交作業，最好是PDF檔案。"},{"w":"present","p":"v./n.","d":"something you give to someone; a gift","c":"呈現；贈送；出示；禮物","s":"Please present your student ID card at the entrance.","t":"請在入口出示學生證。"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk in which you show and explain something to a group","c":"簡報；呈現","s":"Each group has to give a five-minute presentation in English next week.","t":"每組下週要用英文做五分鐘的報告。"},{"w":"presenter","p":"n.","d":"a person who introduces a TV or radio programme","c":"主持人；報告者","s":"The presenter of the TV cooking show is famous for her funny jokes.","t":"這個電視烹飪節目的主持人以搞笑聞名。"},{"w":"preserve","p":"v.","d":"to keep something safe or in good condition","c":"保存；保護","s":"We should preserve old buildings like Bopiliao for future generations.","t":"我們應為後代保存像剝皮寮這樣的老建築。"},{"w":"preservation","p":"n.","d":"the act of keeping something safe or in good condition","c":"保存；保護","s":"The preservation of old forests is important, because many animals cannot survive in young forests that have just been planted.","t":"老森林的保護很重要，因為許多動物無法在剛種植的年輕森林中生存。"},{"w":"preserved","p":"adj.","d":"kept in good condition","c":"保存完好的","s":"The ancient temple in Lukang is still well preserved.","t":"鹿港的古廟至今仍保存完好。"},{"w":"preservative","p":"n.","d":"a chemical added to food to stop it from going bad","c":"防腐劑","s":"This bread contains no preservative, so it goes mouldy after three days, but my family thinks it tastes much fresher.","t":"這種麵包不含防腐劑，所以三天後就會發霉，但我們家覺得它吃起來新鮮多了。"}]},{"unit":24,"theme":"prevent – proper · 15 字族 · 40 題","cards":[{"w":"prevent","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening","c":"預防；阻止","s":"Wearing a helmet can prevent serious head injuries.","t":"戴安全帽可以預防嚴重的頭部傷害。"},{"w":"prevention","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping something bad from happening","c":"預防","s":"The prevention of diabetes is cheaper than treatment, so the government pays for free health checks.","t":"預防糖尿病比治療便宜,所以政府支付免費健康檢查的費用。"},{"w":"preventable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be stopped before it happens","c":"可預防的","s":"Many traffic accidents would be preventable if drivers were more careful.","t":"如果駕駛更小心，許多車禍是可以避免的。"},{"w":"preventive","p":"adj.","d":"intended to stop something bad before it happens","c":"預防性的","s":"preventive medicine saves money in the long run, because treating serious diseases is very expensive.","t":"預防醫學長期來看能省錢,因為治療重大疾病非常昂貴。"},{"w":"previous","p":"adj.","d":"happening before","c":"先前的","s":"My new phone is much faster than my previous one.","t":"我的新手機比之前那支快得多。"},{"w":"previously","p":"adv.","d":"before now; earlier","c":"先前","s":"The singer had previously performed in Taipei twice before this concert.","t":"這位歌手在這場演唱會之前已在台北表演過兩次。"},{"w":"previous to","p":"prep.","d":"before","c":"在…之前","s":"The singer had previously performed in Taipei twice before this concert.","t":"這位歌手在這場演唱會之前已在台北表演過兩次。"},{"w":"pride","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of pleasure about what you or people close to you have done","c":"驕傲；自尊","s":"The farmers in Chishang take great pride in the rice they grow.","t":"池上的農民對自己種的米很自豪。"},{"w":"proud","p":"adj.","d":"feeling good about what you or others did","c":"驕傲的；自豪的","s":"My parents were so proud of me when I got into my first-choice school.","t":"我考上第一志願時，爸媽非常以我為傲。"},{"w":"proudly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you are pleased with what you or others have done","c":"驕傲地","s":"Little Ken proudly showed his grandparents the medal he had won at the swimming race.","t":"小 Ken 驕傲地把游泳比賽贏得的獎牌給祖父母看。"},{"w":"take pride in","p":"phr.","d":"pride · C 固定搭配","c":"以…為傲","s":"Little Ken proudly showed his grandparents the medal he had won at the swimming race.","t":"小 Ken 驕傲地把游泳比賽贏得的獎牌給祖父母看。"},{"w":"primary","p":"adj.","d":"main; most important","c":"主要的；初級的","s":"Our primary goal this semester is to improve our reading skills.","t":"我們這學期的主要目標是提升閱讀能力。"},{"w":"primarily","p":"adv.","d":"mainly","c":"主要地","s":"The island's economy depends primarily on tourism, so the volcano is both a danger and a valuable attraction.","t":"這座島的經濟主要仰賴觀光，所以那座火山既是危險，也是珍貴的觀光景點。"},{"w":"prime","p":"adj.","d":"most important; of the best quality","c":"首要的","s":"The prime reason for his visit was to discuss the new contract.","t":"他訪問的主要原因是討論新合同。"},{"w":"principal","p":"n./adj.","d":"the head of a school","c":"校長；主要的","s":"Our principal gave a short speech to welcome the new students.","t":"我們校長致簡短歡迎詞歡迎新生。"},{"w":"principally","p":"adv.","d":"mainly","c":"主要地","s":"The town's economy depends principally on tourism and tea farming.","t":"這個小鎮的經濟主要依賴觀光和茶葉種植。"},{"w":"principle","p":"n.","d":"a basic rule or belief","c":"原則（易混淆字）","s":"He lives by the principle of honesty.","t":"他按照誠實的原則生活。"},{"w":"prison","p":"n.","d":"a building to which people are legally committed as a punishment for crimes","c":"監獄","s":"The thief was sent to prison for three years.","t":"那名小偷被判入獄三年。"},{"w":"prisoner","p":"n.","d":"a person locked up inside a cell room.","c":"囚犯","s":"The prisoner had been serving a twelve-year sentence and was finally granted early release for good behaviour.","t":"這名囚犯已服滿十二年的刑期，終於因表現良好而獲得提前釋放。"},{"w":"imprison","p":"v.","d":"to put someone in prison","c":"監禁","s":"The activist was imprisoned for two years after publicly speaking out against the government's unfair housing policies.","t":"這名社運人士在公開反對政府不公平的住房政策後被監禁了兩年。"},{"w":"imprisonment","p":"n.","d":"the state of being kept in prison","c":"監禁","s":"The judge gave him a sentence of five years' imprisonment.","t":"法官判他五年徒刑。"},{"w":"private","p":"adj.","d":"only for one person or group and not for public use","c":"私人的","s":"My sister goes to a private high school in Taichung.","t":"我姐姐就讀台中一所私立高中。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone and not watched or bothered by others","c":"隱私","s":"Many parents worry about their children's privacy, because some apps collect photos and locations without asking clearly.","t":"許多家長擔心孩子的隱私,因為有些應用程式在沒有清楚詢問的情況下收集照片和位置。"},{"w":"privately","p":"adv.","d":"owned by a person, not the government","c":"私下地","s":"Can I talk to you privately after class?","t":"下課後我可以私下跟你談談嗎？。"},{"w":"privatize","p":"v.","d":"to sell a company or service owned by the government to private owners","c":"民營化","s":"The government decided to privatize the national airline, and a large company bought it for several billion dollars.","t":"政府決定將國家航空公司民營化，一家大公司以數十億元買下了它。"},{"w":"produce","p":"v.","d":"to make or manufacture from components or raw materials; fresh food","c":"生產","s":"The fertile agricultural valley can produce tons of fresh sweet melons each summer, which are shipped to supermarkets nationwide.","t":"這座肥沃的農業山谷每年夏天都能______數噸新鮮甜瓜，並運往全國各地的超市。"},{"w":"product","p":"n.","d":"something that is made or grown to be sold","c":"產品","s":"The software company launched an innovative new product that helps high school students practice spoken English.","t":"這家軟體公司推出了一款創新的新產品，幫助高中生練習英語口說。"},{"w":"production","p":"n.","d":"the action of manufacturing from raw materials, or a theatrical work","c":"生產；製作","s":"The local car factory temporarily stopped automobile production because of a severe worldwide shortage of essential computer chips.","t":"這家本地汽車工廠暫時停止了汽車______，因為全球嚴重短缺關鍵電腦晶片。"},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"making or achieving a lot","c":"有生產力的；有成效的","s":"I had a very productive morning and finished three assignments before lunch.","t":"我早上很有效率，午餐前就完成三份作業。"},{"w":"productivity","p":"n.","d":"the rate at which work is done or things are made","c":"生產力","s":"Office productivity rose after the team began using AI to write reports, so the manager gave everyone a shorter Friday.","t":"團隊開始用人工智慧寫報告後,辦公室的生產力提升了,所以經理讓大家星期五提早下班。"},{"w":"producer","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that makes goods or movies.","c":"生產者；製作人","s":"The film producer spent three years raising funds and assembling the cast before shooting could finally begin.","t":"這位電影製作人花了三年時間籌募資金、組建演員陣容，才終於能夠開拍。"},{"w":"profession","p":"n.","d":"a job that needs special training, such as teaching or medicine","c":"職業","s":"Teaching is a profession that needs a lot of patience.","t":"教書是一個需要很多耐心的職業。"},{"w":"professional","p":"adj./n.","d":"connected with a job that needs special training; done for money","c":"專業的；專業人士","s":"Her professional attitude impressed everyone at the conference.","t":"她在會議上的專業態度給大家留下了深刻的印象。"},{"w":"professionally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows skill and training","c":"專業地","s":"Everyone in the hotel was dressed professionally for the meeting.","t":"飯店裡每個人都為會議穿著得很專業。"},{"w":"profit","p":"n./v.","d":"money you earn after paying costs","c":"利潤；獲利","s":"The small shop made a profit of fifty thousand dollars last year.","t":"這家小店去年獲利五萬元。"},{"w":"profitable","p":"adj.","d":"making money; bringing an advantage","c":"有利潤的","s":"Selling cheap cotton shirts was very profitable, so more and more mills opened in northern England.","t":"販賣便宜的棉襯衫非常賺錢,所以越來越多工廠在英格蘭北部開設。"},{"w":"unprofitable","p":"adj.","d":"not making a profit","c":"無利可圖的","s":"The small café was unprofitable, so the owner decided to close it.","t":"那間小咖啡店不賺錢，所以老闆決定收掉。"},{"w":"nonprofit","p":"adj.","d":"not run in order to make money, but to help people or society","c":"非營利的","s":"Andy works for a nonprofit organization that helps stray dogs.","t":"安迪在一個幫助流浪狗的非營利組織工作。"},{"w":"progress","p":"n./v.","d":"forward movement toward a destination or goal","c":"進步；進展","s":"Kevin has made great progress in math this semester.","t":"凱文這學期數學進步很多。"},{"w":"progressive","p":"adj.","d":"supporting new ideas and social change; happening gradually","c":"進步的；漸進的","s":"Taiwan is seen as a progressive society in Asia because of its open laws.","t":"台灣因其開放的法律被視為亞洲進步的社會。"},{"w":"progressively","p":"adv.","d":"gradually, step by step","c":"逐漸地","s":"The weather got progressively worse as we climbed higher.","t":"我們爬得越高，天氣就越來越糟。"},{"w":"promise","p":"n./v.","d":"to say that you will certainly do something","c":"承諾；保證","s":"I can't promise anything, but I'll try my best to come to your party.","t":"我不能保證什麼，但會盡量去參加你的派對。"},{"w":"promising","p":"adj.","d":"likely to be successful in the future","c":"有前途的","s":"The new medicine has shown promising results in early tests.","t":"新藥在初期試驗中顯示出可望成功的結果。"},{"w":"promised","p":"v.","d":"said that you would surely do something","c":"承諾（過去式）","s":"Dad promised to take us to Kenting if we did well on our exams.","t":"爸爸答應如果我們考得好就帶我們去墾丁。"},{"w":"promote","p":"v.","d":"to help something grow; to give a higher job","c":"升遷；推廣","s":"The city government is trying to promote local tourism by holding a lantern festival.","t":"市政府試圖藉由舉辦燈會推廣在地觀光。"},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"a move to a higher or more important job","c":"升職；促銷；推廣","s":"After years of hard work, she finally received a promotion at her job.","t":"在多年的努力工作之後，她終於在工作中得到了晉升。"},{"w":"promoted","p":"adj.","d":"given a higher job","c":"被升職的","s":"Ms. Lin was promoted to head of the English department last year.","t":"林老師去年升任英文科主任。"},{"w":"promoter","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps make something popular","c":"推廣者","s":"Ms. Lin was promoted to head of the English department last year.","t":"林老師去年升任英文科主任。"},{"w":"prompt","p":"adj./v.","d":"done quickly and without delay","c":"迅速的；促使","s":"The accident prompted the city to put up a traffic light.","t":"這起事故促使市府設置紅綠燈。"},{"w":"promptly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly and without delay","c":"迅速地；準時地","s":"Class starts promptly at 8 a.m., so please don't be late.","t":"課程八點準時開始，請不要遲到。"},{"w":"promptness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of doing something quickly or on time","c":"迅速；準時","s":"Class starts promptly at 8 a.m., so please don't be late.","t":"課程八點準時開始，請不要遲到。"},{"w":"proper","p":"adj.","d":"correct or acceptable for a specific scenario.","c":"適當的","s":"It is important to wear proper safety equipment when cycling on busy roads to protect yourself from accidents.","t":"在繁忙的道路上騎自行車時，穿戴適當的安全裝備以保護自己免受意外傷害是很重要的。"},{"w":"properly","p":"adv.","d":"correctly, in a right way, or suitably.","c":"適當地；正確地","s":"If you don't hold your chopsticks properly, the food will keep falling.","t":"如果你筷子拿得不對，食物會一直掉。"},{"w":"improper","p":"adj.","d":"not right or suitable for the situation","c":"不適當的","s":"It is improper to talk loudly on the phone on the MRT.","t":"在捷運上大聲講電話是不恰當的。"}]},{"unit":25,"theme":"prosper – reduce · 15 字族 · 35 題","cards":[{"w":"prosper","p":"v.","d":"to be successful, especially by making money","c":"繁榮；興旺","s":"Small shops near the new MRT station began to prosper.","t":"新捷運站附近的小店開始興旺起來。"},{"w":"prosperous","p":"adj.","d":"rich and successful","c":"繁榮的","s":"The port town became prosperous when the factory opened, and many families could afford new homes.","t":"工廠開設後這座港口小鎮變得繁榮，而許多家庭有能力買新房子。"},{"w":"prosperity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being successful and having a lot of money","c":"繁榮","s":"People hang red decorations during Lunar New Year to wish for prosperity.","t":"人們在農曆新年掛紅色裝飾，祈求興旺。"},{"w":"protest","p":"n./v.","d":"a strong public complaint against something","c":"抗議","s":"Thousands of students joined the climate protest on Friday, and they carried signs asking leaders to act now.","t":"數千名學生參加了星期五的氣候抗議活動,他們舉著標語要求領袖們立即行動。"},{"w":"protester","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a protest","c":"抗議者","s":"The protesters held up signs and sang songs, and the police made sure that everything stayed peaceful.","t":"抗議者舉著標語唱歌，警察則確保一切保持和平。"},{"w":"prove","p":"v.","d":"to use facts to show that something is true","c":"證明；結果是","s":"The experiment proved his theory to be correct.","t":"實驗證明他的理論是正確的。"},{"w":"proof","p":"n.","d":"facts that show something is true","c":"證據","s":"Do you have any proof that you bought this phone here, such as a receipt?","t":"你有任何在這裡買手機的證明嗎，例如收據？。"},{"w":"proven","p":"adj.","d":"tested and shown to be true or good","c":"經證實的","s":"It has been proved that getting enough sleep improves memory.","t":"睡眠充足能增進記憶力已經被證實。"},{"w":"psychology","p":"n.","d":"the study of the mind and how people behave","c":"心理學","s":"Studying psychology helps us understand why people act the way they do.","t":"學習心理學能幫助我們了解人為何會有那樣的行為。"},{"w":"psychological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the mind and the way people think and feel","c":"心理的","s":"Losing a pet can cause real psychological pain, so parents should talk with their children about their feelings.","t":"失去寵物可能造成真正的心理痛苦，所以父母應該和孩子談談他們的感受。"},{"w":"psychologist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies the mind and helps people with their feelings","c":"心理學家","s":"My sister wants to become a school psychologist to help students with stress.","t":"我姊姊想成為學校心理師，幫助有壓力的學生。"},{"w":"psychologically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with the mind","c":"心理上","s":"After the accident, she was psychologically affected and couldn't drive for months.","t":"車禍後她在心理上受到影響，好幾個月不敢開車。"},{"w":"publish","p":"v.","d":"to print a book, magazine, or article for people to buy or read","c":"出版；刊登","s":"They plan to publish the book next month.","t":"他們計劃下個月出版這本書。"},{"w":"publisher","p":"n.","d":"a company or person that prints and sells books","c":"出版者；出版社","s":"The publisher has rights to print the novel overseas.","t":"出版商有權在海外印刷這部小說。"},{"w":"publication","p":"n.","d":"the act of printing a book or article so people can read it; a book or magazine","c":"出版；出版品","s":"The publication of her first comic book made Amy the proudest student in our class.","t":"第一本漫畫出版讓艾咪成為我們班上最自豪的學生。"},{"w":"publishing","p":"n.","d":"the business of producing books, magazines, and newspapers","c":"出版業","s":"The magazine stopped publishing paper copies last year and is now only online.","t":"那本雜誌去年停止出版紙本，現在只有線上版。"},{"w":"punish","p":"v.","d":"to inflict a penalty or sanction on someone for an offense","c":"處罰","s":"Parents shouldn't punish their children by hitting them.","t":"父母不應該用打的來處罰孩子。"},{"w":"punishment","p":"n.","d":"something bad that is done to a person because they broke a rule or law","c":"處罰","s":"A: What will happen to the employees who shared private customer information on social media without permission? B: The company is still deciding on their punishment, but the human resources director said they will probably lose their bonus this year and must attend extra training about data protection.","t":"A：那些未經許可在社群媒體上分享客戶私人資料的員工會怎麼樣？ B：公司仍在決定對他們的【懲罰】，但人資主管說他們今年可能會失去獎金，而且必須參加額外的資料保護訓練。"},{"w":"punished","p":"adj.","d":"made to suffer for doing wrong","c":"受罰的","s":"The students were punished for cheating on the exam.","t":"那些學生因考試作弊而受罰。"},{"w":"purchase","p":"v./n.","d":"to buy something","c":"購買；購買的物品","s":"I decided to purchase a new car.","t":"我決定購買一輛新車。"},{"w":"purchased","p":"adj.","d":"bought","c":"購得的","s":"All purchased items can be returned within seven days.","t":"所有購買的商品都可在七天內退貨。"},{"w":"purchasing","p":"n.","d":"the act of buying things","c":"採購","s":"Purchasing a used scooter can save you a lot of money.","t":"買二手機車可以幫你省很多錢。"},{"w":"purpose","p":"n.","d":"the reason for which something is done or created","c":"目的","s":"The primary purpose of this community health seminar is to teach residents how to prepare balanced and nutritious meals.","t":"本社區健康研討會的主要目的是教導居民如何準備均衡且營養的餐點。"},{"w":"purposely","p":"adv.","d":"on purpose, not by accident","c":"故意地","s":"The rude comment was clearly no accident; Kevin said it on purpose to hurt his sister.","t":"那句無禮的話顯然不是意外，Kevin 是故意說來傷害他妹妹的。"},{"w":"purposeful","p":"adj.","d":"done with a clear aim","c":"有目標的；果斷的","s":"Her quick, purposeful steps showed that she knew exactly where she was going.","t":"她快速而堅定的步伐顯示她很清楚要去哪裡。"},{"w":"on purpose","p":"phr.","d":"purpose · C 固定搭配","c":"故意地","s":"The rude comment was clearly no accident; Kevin said it on purpose to hurt his sister.","t":"那句無禮的話顯然不是意外，Kevin 是故意說來傷害他妹妹的。"},{"w":"pursue","p":"v.","d":"to try hard to achieve something over a long time","c":"追求；追趕","s":"Many young people move to Taipei to pursue their dreams.","t":"許多年輕人搬到台北追求夢想。"},{"w":"pursuit","p":"n.","d":"the act of trying to get something","c":"追求；追趕","s":"The pursuit of happiness is considered an inalienable right.","t":"追求幸福被認為是不可剝奪的權利。"},{"w":"pursuer","p":"n.","d":"a person who chases someone","c":"追趕者","s":"Many young people move to Taipei to pursue their dreams.","t":"許多年輕人搬到台北追求夢想。"},{"w":"race","p":"n.","d":"a game to see who is the fastest","c":"種族；賽跑","s":"Q: What do Tom and Ben usually do in their free time? — A: They practice running for the race on sports day.","t":"湯姆和班空閒時通常做什麼？ — 他們練跑步，準備運動會的賽跑。"},{"w":"racial","p":"adj.","d":"related to a person's race","c":"種族的","s":"The new law protects workers from racial discrimination.","t":"新法保護勞工免受種族歧視。"},{"w":"racism","p":"n.","d":"unfair treatment of people because of their race","c":"種族歧視","s":"Martin Luther King Jr. spent his life fighting against racism in America.","t":"金恩博士一生都在對抗美國的種族歧視。"},{"w":"racist","p":"n./adj.","d":"showing unfair treatment of people because of their race","c":"種族主義者；種族歧視的","s":"The company fired the manager who made racist jokes about his coworkers at the office party.","t":"公司開除了那位在辦公室派對上對同事開種族歧視玩笑的經理。"},{"w":"react","p":"v.","d":"to behave in a specific way due to something.","c":"反應","s":"It is important to stay calm and not react angrily when someone criticizes your work in front of others.","t":"當有人當著他人面前批評你的工作時，保持冷靜、不要憤怒回應是很重要的。"},{"w":"reaction","p":"n.","d":"behavior or feelings caused by an action or event.","c":"反應","s":"What was your mom's reaction when you showed her your report card?","t":"你給媽媽看成績單時，她的反應是什麼？。"},{"w":"recognize","p":"v.","d":"to know who someone is or what something is because you have seen or heard them before","c":"認出；認可","s":"I didn't recognize my old classmate at first because she had cut her hair short.","t":"我一開始沒認出老同學，因為她剪了短髮。"},{"w":"recognition","p":"n.","d":"the act of knowing who or what something is because you have seen it before","c":"認出；認可","s":"His recognition of the suspect was crucial to the investigation.","t":"他對嫌疑人的辨認對調查至關重要。"},{"w":"recognizable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to know or identify","c":"可認出的","s":"Her voice is recognizable even in a noisy room.","t":"她的聲音在嘈雜的房間裡也是可以辨認的。"},{"w":"unrecognizable","p":"adj.","d":"changed so much that no one knows it","c":"認不出的","s":"After the fire, the old house was completely unrecognizable.","t":"火災之後，那棟老房子已經完全認不出來了。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to get well again; to get something back","c":"恢復；康復","s":"It took Daniel three weeks to fully recover from his broken ankle.","t":"Daniel 花了三週才從腳踝骨折中完全康復。"},{"w":"recovery","p":"n.","d":"the process of getting better after an illness or injury","c":"康復；恢復","s":"The patient made a full recovery after the surgery.","t":"病人在手術後完全恢復了。"},{"w":"recoverable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be taken out or got back","c":"可恢復的","s":"Experts say only half of the oil in the field is recoverable, because the rest is trapped too deep in the rock.","t":"專家說這座油田只有一半的石油可開採，因為其餘的被困在岩層太深處。"},{"w":"recycle","p":"v.","d":"to treat used materials so that they can be used again","c":"回收","s":"Students are encouraged to recycle used paper and plastic bottles, which greatly helps reduce garbage in our school.","t":"學生們受到鼓勵要回收廢紙與塑膠瓶，這極大有助於減少我們學校裡的垃圾量。"},{"w":"recycling","p":"n.","d":"treating used things so they can be used again","c":"回收","s":"recycling old phones keeps valuable metals in use, and it also stops toxic materials from ending up in landfill.","t":"回收舊手機能讓珍貴金屬持續被利用，也能防止有毒物質最後進入掩埋場。"},{"w":"recycled","p":"adj.","d":"used again after being made into something new","c":"回收再製的","s":"Our school recycled over two tons of paper last year.","t":"我們學校去年回收了超過兩噸的紙。"},{"w":"recyclable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be recycled","c":"可回收的","s":"Make sure you put only recyclable items in the blue bin.","t":"確定藍色桶子裡只放可回收的物品。"},{"w":"reduce","p":"v.","d":"to make something smaller or less","c":"減少","s":"We should reduce the amount of sugar we eat every day.","t":"我們應該減少每天吃的糖量。"},{"w":"reduction","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something smaller or less","c":"減少","s":"The new law led to a large reduction in smoking, so fewer people now suffer from lung disease.","t":"新法律使吸菸人口大幅減少,所以現在罹患肺病的人變少了。"},{"w":"reduced","p":"adj.","d":"smaller or less than before","c":"減少的；降價的","s":"The price of the jacket has been reduced by 30 percent.","t":"這件外套已經降價三成。"}]},{"unit":26,"theme":"reflect – require · 15 字族 · 38 題","cards":[{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to send back light, heat, or an image from a surface","c":"反射；反映；反思","s":"After the exam, take some time to reflect on what you did wrong.","t":"考完試後花點時間反省自己哪裡做錯。"},{"w":"reflection","p":"n.","d":"an image that you see in a mirror, glass, or water","c":"倒影；反思","s":"The cat saw its own reflection in the window and jumped back, thinking there was another cat outside.","t":"那隻貓看到窗戶上自己的倒影就往後跳，以為外面有另一隻貓。"},{"w":"reflective","p":"adj.","d":"able to send back light; thinking deeply","c":"反光的；沉思的","s":"Runners should wear reflective vests at night so that drivers can see them.","t":"跑者晚上應穿反光背心讓駕駛看得到。"},{"w":"refuse","p":"v.","d":"to say you will not do or accept something","c":"拒絕","s":"It's hard to refuse an invitation from your grandma.","t":"奶奶的邀請很難拒絕。"},{"w":"refusal","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying that you will not do or accept something","c":"拒絕","s":"His refusal to take the medicine worried his family, so they asked the doctor to talk to him.","t":"他拒絕吃藥讓家人很擔心,所以他們請醫生和他談談。"},{"w":"refused","p":"v.","d":"said no to something","c":"拒絕（過去式）","s":"Tom refused to lend me his notes, so I had to borrow Amy's.","t":"湯姆拒絕借我筆記，所以我只好借艾咪的。"},{"w":"regulate","p":"v.","d":"to control something by rules or laws","c":"管制；調節","s":"Sweating helps regulate body temperature in hot weather.","t":"流汗有助於在炎熱天氣中調節體溫。"},{"w":"regulation","p":"n.","d":"an official rule that controls how something is done","c":"規定；管制","s":"There are certain regulation one must follow in the lab.","t":"實驗室中必須遵循某些規定。"},{"w":"regulated","p":"adj.","d":"controlled by rules","c":"受管制的","s":"Sweating helps regulate body temperature in hot weather.","t":"流汗有助於在炎熱天氣中調節體溫。"},{"w":"relate","p":"v.","d":"to find or show a connection","c":"有關；產生共鳴","s":"Teenagers can easily relate to the main character in this movie.","t":"青少年很容易對這部電影的主角產生共鳴。"},{"w":"related","p":"adj.","d":"connected","c":"相關的","s":"Many of my relatives live in Tainan, so we visit them every Lunar New Year.","t":"我很多親戚住在台南，所以每年過年都去拜訪。"},{"w":"relation","p":"n.","d":"the way in which two things are connected","c":"關係","s":"The relation between these two events is not immediately clear, but further investigation may reveal a connection.","t":"這兩個事件之間的關係並不立即清楚，但進一步的調查可能會揭示一種聯繫。"},{"w":"relationship","p":"n.","d":"the way two people or things are connected or behave toward each other","c":"關係","s":"He has built a close relationship with his teammates, which helps them overcome numerous challenges in life.","t":"他和隊友建立起了密切的關係，這幫助他們克服了生活中的眾多挑戰。"},{"w":"relative","p":"n./adj.","d":"a person connected by blood or marriage; comparative","c":"親戚；相對的","s":"During the Lunar New Year holidays, dozens of distant relatives gather at our ancestral home to share a festive reunion dinner.","t":"在農曆新年假期期間，數十位遠房親戚聚集在我們祖厝，共同享用豐盛的團圓晚餐。"},{"w":"relatively","p":"adv.","d":"compared with other things","c":"相對地","s":"The changes needed are relatively simple, but they require people to give up some old habits.","t":"所需的改變相對簡單,但它們需要人們放棄一些舊習慣。"},{"w":"release","p":"v./n.","d":"the act of making something available","c":"釋放；發行","s":"The singer's release of her new song was the top news on social media.","t":"那位歌手新歌的發行是社群媒體上的頭條。"},{"w":"released","p":"adj.","d":"made available to the public","c":"已發行的；被釋放的","s":"The zoo released the rescued sea turtle back into the ocean last week.","t":"動物園上週把獲救的海龜放回大海。"},{"w":"new release","p":"n.","d":"a new film, song or product that has just come out","c":"新發行作品","s":"The zoo released the rescued sea turtle back into the ocean last week.","t":"動物園上週把獲救的海龜放回大海。"},{"w":"relieve","p":"v.","d":"to make pain or a bad feeling less strong","c":"減輕；緩解","s":"Volunteers sent food and water to relieve the suffering of the flood victims.","t":"志工送去食物和水以減輕水災災民的苦難。"},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"help such as food and money for people in need","c":"寬慰；緩解","s":"Many countries sent relief to the flood victims.","t":"許多國家送救援物資給水災災民。"},{"w":"relieved","p":"adj.","d":"feeling happy because something bad did not happen","c":"鬆了一口氣的","s":"Amy was relieved to find her lost wallet in the classroom.","t":"艾咪在教室找到遺失的錢包，鬆了一口氣。"},{"w":"religion","p":"n.","d":"a systematic belief in and worship of a god or a higher spiritual power","c":"宗教","s":"Freedom of religion is protected by law in Taiwan.","t":"在台灣，宗教自由受法律保障。"},{"w":"religious","p":"adj.","d":"relating to religion, or showing a strong dedication to a spiritual belief","c":"宗教的；虔誠的","s":"The historic temple is of great importance to the country's religious heritage and ancient traditions.","t":"這座歷史悠久的寺廟對該國的宗教遺產與古代傳統具有極大的重要性。"},{"w":"religiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is about religion; very regularly","c":"虔誠地；嚴格地","s":"My grandmother religiously visits the temple on the first day of every lunar month.","t":"我奶奶每逢農曆初一都一定會去廟裡。"},{"w":"reluctant","p":"adj.","d":"not wanting to do something and slow to do it","c":"不情願的","s":"Most kids are reluctant to go to bed early on the night before a holiday.","t":"大部分孩子在放假前一晚都不太想早睡。"},{"w":"reluctantly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you don't want to","c":"不情願地","s":"Jay reluctantly turned off the TV and started doing his homework.","t":"Jay 不情願地關掉電視開始寫作業。"},{"w":"reluctance","p":"n.","d":"not wanting to do something","c":"不情願","s":"Despite her reluctance to speak in public, Lily agreed to host the class party.","t":"儘管 Lily 不太願意在公開場合講話，她還是答應主持班會派對。"},{"w":"rely","p":"v.","d":"to depend on someone or something","c":"依賴","s":"Many farmers rely on rain to water their fields.","t":"許多農民依靠雨水灌溉田地。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be trusted","c":"可靠的","s":"We need a more reliable method to collect data.","t":"我們需要一種更可靠的方法來收集數據。"},{"w":"unreliable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be trusted","c":"不可靠的","s":"The bus in this village is so unreliable that I never know when it will come.","t":"這個村子的公車很不可靠，我永遠不知道它何時會來。"},{"w":"reliance","p":"n.","d":"the state of depending on someone or something","c":"依賴","s":"Our heavy reliance on cars makes air pollution worse.","t":"我們對汽車的高度依賴讓空氣污染更嚴重。"},{"w":"rent","p":"v./n.","d":"to pay money to use a house or car; the money paid","c":"租用；租金","s":"The rent for this small apartment is NT$15,000 a month.","t":"這間小公寓的租金是每月一萬五千元。"},{"w":"rental","p":"adj./n.","d":"the act of renting; something you rent; the money paid for renting","c":"出租的；租賃","s":"We picked up our rental car at the airport and drove straight to the beach.","t":"我們在機場取了租來的車，直接開到海邊。"},{"w":"replace","p":"v.","d":"to take the place of someone or something","c":"取代；更換","s":"Robots may replace some jobs in the future.","t":"未來機器人可能會取代一些工作。"},{"w":"replacement","p":"n.","d":"a new part that takes the place of an old one","c":"替代品；替換","s":"My grandmother had a knee replacement last spring, and now she can walk to the market without pain.","t":"我奶奶去年春天做了膝關節置換手術,現在她走路去市場都不會痛了。"},{"w":"replaceable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be replaced","c":"可替換的","s":"The phone's battery is easily replaceable, so you can buy a new one instead of throwing the whole phone away.","t":"這支手機的電池很容易替換，所以你可以買新電池，而不必丟掉整支手機。"},{"w":"irreplaceable","p":"adj.","d":"too special or rare to be replaced","c":"無可取代的","s":"A mother's love is irreplaceable; nothing can take its place.","t":"母愛是無可取代的；沒有任何東西能代替它。"},{"w":"reply","p":"v./n.","d":"to answer","c":"回覆；答覆","s":"Please reply to my e-mail before Friday.","t":"請在週五前回覆我的電子郵件。"},{"w":"replied","p":"v.","d":"answered","c":"reply 過去式","s":"Mark hasn't replied to my LINE message yet.","t":"馬克還沒回我的LINE訊息。"},{"w":"replies","p":"n./v.","d":"answers","c":"回覆（複數）；回覆（三單）","s":"I sent out ten job applications but got only two replies.","t":"我寄出十份求職信，卻只收到兩封回覆。"},{"w":"represent","p":"v.","d":"to speak or act officially on behalf of a team.","c":"代表；象徵","s":"Jenny was chosen to represent our school in the English speech contest.","t":"珍妮被選為代表學校參加英語演講比賽。"},{"w":"representative","p":"n./adj.","d":"typical of a larger group","c":"代表；有代表性的","s":"This rock is representative of the whole area, so studying it tells us a lot about the history of the region.","t":"這塊岩石對整個地區具有代表性，所以研究它能讓我們了解許多這個區域的歷史。"},{"w":"representation","p":"n.","d":"a picture or description that shows what something is like","c":"代表；描繪","s":"Many people feel that women's representation in leadership roles has improved significantly over the past twenty years.","t":"許多人認為女性在領導角色中的代表性在過去二十年中已顯著提升。"},{"w":"request","p":"n./v.","d":"the act of asking for something politely or formally","c":"要求；請求","s":"The radio DJ played my favorite song after I sent in a request by text message.","t":"我傳簡訊點歌後，電台 DJ 播了我最愛的歌。"},{"w":"requested","p":"adj.","d":"asked for","c":"被要求的","s":"The school library has requested that all students return borrowed books before the summer break.","t":"學校圖書館要求所有學生在暑假前歸還借閱的書。"},{"w":"on request","p":"phr.","d":"request · C 固定搭配","c":"應要求","s":"The radio DJ played my favorite song after I sent in a request by text message.","t":"我傳簡訊點歌後，電台 DJ 播了我最愛的歌。"},{"w":"require","p":"v.","d":"to need something","c":"需要；要求","s":"This task will require your full attention.","t":"這項任務需要你的全部注意力。"},{"w":"requirement","p":"n.","d":"something that you must have or do","c":"必要條件","s":"Passing a swimming test is a graduation requirement at some universities.","t":"在一些大學，通過游泳測驗是畢業條件之一。"},{"w":"required","p":"adj.","d":"needed; must be done","c":"必修的；必需的","s":"Wearing a helmet is required by law for all scooter riders in Taiwan.","t":"在台灣，法律規定所有機車騎士都要戴安全帽。"}]},{"unit":27,"theme":"research – rob · 15 字族 · 36 題","cards":[{"w":"research","p":"n./v.","d":"careful study to find out new facts","c":"研究","s":"Before buying a new laptop, Jack did a lot of research online.","t":"Jack 買新筆電前在網路上做了很多研究。"},{"w":"researcher","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to study something carefully","c":"研究員","s":"The researcher spent years in the Amazon studying plant life.","t":"研究員在亞馬遜研究植物生活多年。"},{"w":"researched","p":"adj.","d":"carefully studied","c":"經研究的","s":"The report was carefully researched, with data from over twenty countries.","t":"這份報告經過仔細研究，包含二十多國的數據。"},{"w":"resemble","p":"v.","d":"to look like or be similar to someone or something","c":"像；類似","s":"She closely resembles her mother, especially when she smiles.","t":"她長得很像媽媽，尤其笑起來時。"},{"w":"resemblance","p":"n.","d":"the fact of looking like someone or something","c":"相似","s":"The desert in Chile has a strong resemblance to the surface of Mars, so space agencies test their rovers there.","t":"智利的沙漠與火星表面非常相似，所以太空機構在那裡測試他們的探測車。"},{"w":"resembles","p":"v.","d":"looks like","c":"像（第三人稱單數）","s":"Lucy strongly resembles her mother; they have the same eyes and smile.","t":"露西長得很像她媽媽；她們有一樣的眼睛和笑容。"},{"w":"reserve","p":"v.","d":"to book in advance; to keep for later use","c":"預訂；保留","s":"Mom called the hot spring hotel in Beitou to reserve a room for Grandpa's birthday.","t":"媽媽打電話給北投的溫泉旅館，替爺爺的生日訂一間房。"},{"w":"reservation","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to keep a seat, room, or table for you","c":"預訂","s":"I made a reservation for four people at the Italian restaurant, so we should arrive there before seven o'clock.","t":"我在那家義大利餐廳訂了四個人的位子，所以我們應該在七點前到達那裡。"},{"w":"reserved","p":"adj.","d":"not showing your feelings or opinions easily","c":"已預訂的；內向的","s":"Sorry, you can't sit here. These front-row seats are reserved for the guests of honor.","t":"抱歉，您不能坐這裡，前排座位是保留給貴賓的。"},{"w":"reservedly","p":"adv.","d":"in a quiet way that does not show feelings","c":"含蓄地","s":"Sorry, you can't sit here. These front-row seats are reserved for the guests of honor.","t":"抱歉，您不能坐這裡，前排座位是保留給貴賓的。"},{"w":"reside","p":"v.","d":"to live in a particular place","c":"居住","s":"Her family has resided in this small town for three generations.","t":"她家已在這個小鎮住了三代。"},{"w":"resident","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives in a particular place","c":"居民","s":"The local resident were upset about the construction noise.","t":"當地居民對建築噪音感到不滿。"},{"w":"residence","p":"n.","d":"the place where someone lives, especially a large house","c":"住所；居住","s":"Their residence is near the beach.","t":"他們的住所靠近海灘。"},{"w":"residential","p":"adj.","d":"related to homes; where people live","c":"住宅的","s":"Factories are not allowed in this quiet residential area.","t":"這個安靜的住宅區不准設工廠。"},{"w":"resist","p":"v.","d":"to fight against; to stop yourself from doing something","c":"抵抗；忍住","s":"I couldn't resist eating another piece of chocolate cake.","t":"我忍不住又吃了一塊巧克力蛋糕。"},{"w":"resistance","p":"n.","d":"the act of fighting against or refusing something","c":"抵抗","s":"Taking antibiotics too often can lead to resistance, so the medicine may not work when you really need it.","t":"太常服用抗生素會導致抗藥性,所以當你真正需要時藥可能就沒效了。"},{"w":"resistant","p":"adj.","d":"not harmed or changed by something","c":"抵抗的；耐…的","s":"This watch is water-resistant, so you can wear it while swimming.","t":"這支錶防水，游泳時也能戴。"},{"w":"irresistible","p":"adj.","d":"too attractive or strong to say no to","c":"無法抗拒的","s":"The smell of fried chicken from the night market was irresistible.","t":"夜市飄來的炸雞香味讓人無法抗拒。"},{"w":"respond","p":"v.","d":"to react to something","c":"回應；反應","s":"Please respond to the party invitation by Friday.","t":"請在週五前回覆派對邀請。"},{"w":"response","p":"n.","d":"an answer or reaction","c":"回應；反應","s":"The teacher asked a difficult question, and the only response from the class was a long and uncomfortable silence.","t":"老師問了一個困難的問題，全班唯一的回應是一陣漫長又不自在的沉默。"},{"w":"responsive","p":"adj.","d":"reacting quickly and positively","c":"反應迅速的","s":"Babies are very responsive to their mother's voice, and they often stop crying when they hear her.","t":"嬰兒對媽媽的聲音反應非常靈敏，而且他們聽到媽媽的聲音時常常會停止哭泣。"},{"w":"responsible","p":"adj.","d":"having the obligation to take care of something; reliable","c":"負責的","s":"Every driver is personally responsible for following traffic regulations, so you must always stop when the traffic light turns red.","t":"每位駕駛人都有責任遵守交通法規，因此當交通號誌變紅時，你必須隨時停車。"},{"w":"responsibility","p":"n.","d":"a specific duty or burden that an agent must track.","c":"責任","s":"It is the responsibility of every citizen to vote in elections and make sure their voice is heard by the government.","t":"每個公民有責任在選舉中投票，確保政府聽到他們的聲音。"},{"w":"irresponsible","p":"adj.","d":"not thinking enough about the results of your actions","c":"不負責任的","s":"It was irresponsible of you to leave the door unlocked all night.","t":"你整晚沒鎖門真是太不負責任了。"},{"w":"responsibly","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful and sensible way","c":"負責任地","s":"Teenagers should learn to use social media responsibly.","t":"青少年應該學習負責任地使用社群媒體。"},{"w":"restrict","p":"v.","d":"to limit something","c":"限制","s":"The law will restrict the sale of alcohol.","t":"法律將限制酒精的銷售。"},{"w":"restriction","p":"n.","d":"a rule that limits what you can do","c":"限制","s":"There are certain restriction on freedom of speech.","t":"言論自由有某些限制。"},{"w":"restricted","p":"adj.","d":"limited; only for some people","c":"受限制的","s":"This area is restricted; only staff members are allowed to enter.","t":"此區域為管制區，只有工作人員可以進入。"},{"w":"restrictive","p":"adj.","d":"limiting what people can do","c":"限制性的","s":"Some students feel the dress code is too restrictive and want more freedom.","t":"有些學生覺得服裝規定太嚴格，想要更多自由。"},{"w":"review","p":"v./n.","d":"to look at again; a report giving an opinion","c":"複習；評論","s":"Let's review the last chapter before the test.","t":"考試前我們來複習最後一章吧。"},{"w":"reviewer","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes opinions about books, films, etc.","c":"評論者","s":"According to one reviewer, the new ramen shop near the station has the best broth in town.","t":"根據一位評論者，車站附近的新拉麵店湯頭是全城最好的。"},{"w":"preview","p":"v./n.","d":"a chance to see something before it is shown to the public","c":"預習；預告","s":"We were invited to a special preview of the new exhibition, two days before it opened to the general public.","t":"我們受邀參加新展覽的特別預展，比對一般大眾開放早了兩天。"},{"w":"revolution","p":"n.","d":"a time when people change the government by force; a complete change","c":"革命；重大變革","s":"The Industrial Revolution began in Britain in the 18th century.","t":"工業革命於十八世紀始於英國。"},{"w":"revolutionary","p":"adj.","d":"completely new and causing great change","c":"革命性的","s":"The telescope was a revolutionary invention, because it allowed Galileo to see the moons of Jupiter for the first time.","t":"望遠鏡是一項革命性的發明，因為它讓伽利略第一次看到木星的衛星。"},{"w":"revolutionize","p":"v.","d":"to change something completely","c":"徹底改變","s":"The internet has revolutionized the way we shop, since we can now buy almost anything without leaving our homes.","t":"網路徹底改變了我們購物的方式，因為現在我們不用出門幾乎什麼都能買到。"},{"w":"reward","p":"n./v.","d":"something good you get for doing something well or helpful","c":"獎賞；報酬；獎勵","s":"The owner is offering a big reward to anyone who finds her lost cat.","t":"主人提供一大筆賞金給找到她走失貓咪的人。"},{"w":"rewarding","p":"adj.","d":"giving you a good feeling because it is useful or important","c":"有收穫的；值得的","s":"Teaching young kids can be tiring, but it is also very rewarding.","t":"教小朋友可能很累，但也很有成就感。"},{"w":"rewarded","p":"adj.","d":"given something for good work","c":"得到回報的","s":"Hard work is usually rewarded in the end.","t":"努力最後通常會得到回報。"},{"w":"rhetoric","p":"n.","d":"speech or writing meant to persuade, often without real meaning","c":"修辭；修辭學","s":"Politicians use a lot of rhetoric about better schools, but teachers want to see real money and action.","t":"政客們發表許多關於改善學校的漂亮話，但老師想看到真正的經費和行動。"},{"w":"rhetorical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with persuasive speech; asked only for effect","c":"修辭的","s":"\"Who doesn't love bubble tea?\" is a rhetorical question; you don't need to answer it.","t":"「誰不愛珍奶？」是個反問句，你不用回答。"},{"w":"rhetorically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is about the skill of speaking or writing","c":"修辭上地","s":"\"Who doesn't love bubble tea?\" is a rhetorical question; you don't need to answer it.","t":"「誰不愛珍奶？」是個反問句，你不用回答。"},{"w":"right","p":"adj./n.","d":"the side opposite to left","c":"正確的；權利","s":"Q: How do I get to the train station? — A: Go straight for two blocks. It's on your right.","t":"我要怎麼去火車站？ — 直走兩個街區，它在你的右邊。"},{"w":"rightly","p":"adv.","d":"correctly; for a good reason","c":"正確地；理所當然地","s":"Many people believe, rightly, that education is the key to a better future.","t":"許多人理所當然地相信，教育是通往美好未來的關鍵。"},{"w":"rightful","p":"adj.","d":"legally or morally correct","c":"合法的；應得的","s":"The stolen painting was finally returned to its rightful owner.","t":"被偷的畫終於歸還給它的合法擁有者。"},{"w":"upright","p":"adj./adv.","d":"straight up; not bent or lying down","c":"直立的；挺直地；正直的","s":"Please keep your seat in the upright position during takeoff and landing.","t":"起飛和降落時請將座椅豎直。"},{"w":"risk","p":"n./v.","d":"to put something valuable in a situation where it could be lost or harmed","c":"風險；冒…的風險","s":"He decided to risk a large portion of his savings by investing in a volatile market.","t":"他決定冒險把大部分積蓄投資在波動的市場上。"},{"w":"risky","p":"adj.","d":"involving the possibility of something bad happening","c":"危險的","s":"Riding a scooter without a helmet is very risky.","t":"騎機車不戴安全帽非常危險。"},{"w":"riskier","p":"adj.","d":"more dangerous","c":"更危險的","s":"Investing all your money in one company is riskier than saving it in a bank.","t":"把所有錢投資在一家公司比存在銀行更有風險。"},{"w":"rob","p":"v.","d":"to take money or things from a person or place, often by force","c":"搶劫","s":"Two men robbed the bank and escaped in a car.","t":"兩名男子搶劫銀行後開車逃逸。"},{"w":"robber","p":"n.","d":"a person who steals money or things, often using force","c":"強盜；搶匪","s":"The bank robber escaped on a scooter but was caught an hour later.","t":"銀行搶匪騎機車逃逸，但一小時後被捕。"},{"w":"robbery","p":"n.","d":"the crime of stealing from a person or place","c":"搶劫案","s":"There was a robbery at the jewelry shop last night, and the thieves took rings worth over a million dollars.","t":"珠寶店昨晚發生了一起搶案，小偷拿走了價值超過一百萬元的戒指。"}]},{"unit":28,"theme":"routine – significant · 15 字族 · 37 題","cards":[{"w":"routine","p":"n./adj.","d":"a sequence of actions regularly followed; a fixed program","c":"例行公事；日常作息；例行的","s":"Brushing my teeth before bed is part of my daily routine.","t":"睡前刷牙是我日常作息的一部分。"},{"w":"routinely","p":"adv.","d":"as a normal part of a process","c":"例行地；慣常地","s":"Students' bags are routinely checked before they enter the exam room.","t":"學生進考場前書包會被例行檢查。"},{"w":"royal","p":"adj.","d":"of or related to a king or queen","c":"皇家的","s":"Millions of people watched the royal wedding on TV.","t":"數百萬人在電視上觀看皇室婚禮。"},{"w":"royalty","p":"n.","d":"kings, queens, and members of their families","c":"王室成員；版稅","s":"The inventor received a royalty for every machine sold, so he earned money for many years.","t":"發明家每賣出一台機器就收到一筆權利金,所以他好多年都持續有收入。"},{"w":"royally","p":"adv.","d":"in a grand way, like a king or queen","c":"盛大地","s":"The guests were treated royally at the five-star hotel.","t":"賓客在五星級飯店受到極盡隆重的款待。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v./n.","d":"to spoil or destroy something completely","c":"毀掉；毀滅；破產","s":"Staying up late every night will ruin your health.","t":"每晚熬夜會毀了你的健康。"},{"w":"ruins","p":"n.","d":"the parts of a building or city that are left after it is destroyed","c":"廢墟；遺跡","s":"Every year, millions of tourists visit the ancient ruins in Rome.","t":"每年都有數百萬觀光客造訪羅馬的古蹟遺址。"},{"w":"ruined","p":"adj.","d":"destroyed or badly damaged","c":"毀壞的","s":"The heavy rain ruined our picnic at Daan Park last Sunday.","t":"上週日的大雨毀了我們在大安公園的野餐。"},{"w":"sail","p":"v./n.","d":"to travel on water in a boat","c":"航行；帆","s":"Q: Can your uncle sail a boat? — A: Yes, he can. He often takes us out on the lake.","t":"你叔叔會駕船嗎？ — 是的，他會。他常帶我們到湖上。"},{"w":"sailor","p":"n.","d":"a person who works on a ship","c":"水手","s":"The old sailor told us stories about his years at sea.","t":"那位老水手跟我們講他在海上那些年的故事。"},{"w":"sailing","p":"n.","d":"the sport or activity of traveling in a boat with sails","c":"帆船運動；航行","s":"We went sailing on a small boat along the coast of Penghu last summer.","t":"去年夏天我們搭小船沿澎湖海岸航行。"},{"w":"sample","p":"n./v.","d":"a small amount of a substance showing what the whole is like","c":"樣品；樣本；品嘗；抽樣","s":"The doctor took a blood sample to check for any infection.","t":"醫生抽了一管血樣檢查是否有感染。"},{"w":"sampler","p":"n.","d":"a set of small amounts of different things","c":"綜合樣品；試吃組","s":"The shop sells a chocolate sampler box with twelve different flavors.","t":"這家店賣一盒有十二種口味的巧克力綜合禮盒。"},{"w":"satisfy","p":"v.","d":"to meet the expectations, needs, or desires of someone","c":"使滿意；滿足","s":"It is almost impossible to satisfy greedy individuals because they always demand more than they actually need.","t":"要滿足貪婪的人幾乎是不可能的，因為他們索取的總是遠多於他們實際所需。"},{"w":"satisfied","p":"adj.","d":"pleased because you got what you wanted","c":"感到滿意的","s":"Were you satisfied with the service at the hotel?","t":"你對飯店的服務滿意嗎？。"},{"w":"satisfying","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel pleased and happy","c":"令人滿意的","s":"Nothing is more satisfying than finishing a hard puzzle by yourself.","t":"沒有什麼比自己完成一個難的拼圖更讓人滿足。"},{"w":"satisfaction","p":"n.","d":"the good feeling you have when you get what you wanted","c":"滿意","s":"Finishing a difficult puzzle gives me a sense of satisfaction, and it also helps me forget about my worries.","t":"完成一個困難的拼圖帶給我一種滿足感,也能幫助我忘掉煩惱。"},{"w":"satisfactory","p":"adj.","d":"good enough; acceptable","c":"令人滿意的；尚可的","s":"Your grades this semester were satisfactory, but I know you can do even better.","t":"你這學期的成績還算令人滿意，但我知道你能更好。"},{"w":"dissatisfied","p":"adj.","d":"not happy with something","c":"不滿意的","s":"dissatisfied customers often tell their friends about bad service, so the shop trains its staff to solve problems quickly.","t":"不滿意的顧客常會把糟糕的服務告訴朋友，所以這家店訓練員工迅速解決問題。"},{"w":"scare","p":"v.","d":"to make someone afraid","c":"驚嚇","s":"The sudden noise from the kitchen scared the cat, and it ran under the bed.","t":"廚房突然傳來的聲響嚇到貓，牠跑到床底下。"},{"w":"scared","p":"adj.","d":"afraid of something","c":"害怕的","s":"My friend jumped out from behind the classroom door and scared me on purpose this morning.","t":"今天早上我朋友故意從教室門後跳出來嚇我。"},{"w":"scary","p":"adj.","d":"frightening; causing fear","c":"嚇人的","s":"Walking alone through the old hospital at night was really scary.","t":"晚上獨自走過那間老醫院真的很可怕。"},{"w":"scarecrow","p":"n.","d":"a figure dressed in old clothes to frighten birds away from crops","c":"稻草人","s":"The children made a funny scarecrow for the school garden, but the clever birds soon realised it was not a real person.","t":"孩子們為學校菜園做了一個好笑的稻草人，但聰明的鳥兒很快就發現它不是真人。"},{"w":"scream","p":"v./n.","d":"to give a long, loud, piercing cry expressing extreme emotion or alarm","c":"尖叫；尖叫聲","s":"My sister let out a loud scream when she saw a cockroach in the kitchen.","t":"我妹妹在廚房看到蟑螂時大叫了一聲。"},{"w":"screaming","p":"n./v.","d":"shouting loudly in a high voice","c":"尖叫","s":"My sister let out a loud scream when she saw a cockroach in the kitchen.","t":"我妹妹在廚房看到蟑螂時大叫了一聲。"},{"w":"seal","p":"n./v.","d":"to close something tightly; an official mark","c":"印章；封條；海豹；密封","s":"Please seal the envelope before you put it in the mailbox.","t":"請在投入郵筒前把信封封好。"},{"w":"sealed","p":"adj.","d":"Closed securely so that nothing can get in or out.","c":"密封的","s":"Keep the cookies in a sealed jar so they stay crispy.","t":"把餅乾放在密封罐裡才能保持酥脆。"},{"w":"segregate","p":"v.","d":"to separate one group of people from others","c":"隔離；分開","s":"Our principal does not want to segregate students into classes by test scores.","t":"我們校長不想依考試成績把學生分班。"},{"w":"segregated","p":"adj.","d":"kept apart from others","c":"隔離的","s":"Until the 1950s, many schools in the American South were segregated by race.","t":"直到 1950 年代，美國南方許多學校仍依種族隔離。"},{"w":"segregation","p":"n.","d":"the act of keeping groups separate","c":"隔離","s":"The museum shows how racial segregation affected people's daily lives.","t":"這間博物館展示種族隔離如何影響人們的日常生活。"},{"w":"settle","p":"v.","d":"to pay money that you owe","c":"定居；解決","s":"After moving to Tainan, it took our family a few months to settle in.","t":"搬到台南後，我們家花了幾個月才安頓下來。"},{"w":"settled","p":"adj.","d":"calm and comfortable; already decided","c":"安定的；已解決的","s":"Once the argument was settled, the two friends shook hands and laughed.","t":"爭執一解決，兩個朋友就握手大笑。"},{"w":"settlement","p":"n.","d":"a place where people have come to live","c":"協議；定居地","s":"The remains of a small settlement were found by the lake, and it included ten round houses and a well.","t":"在湖邊發現了一個小聚落的遺跡,包括十座圓形房屋和一口井。"},{"w":"settler","p":"n.","d":"a person who goes to live in a new place where few people have lived before","c":"移居者；拓荒者","s":"The first settler on the island built their homes near the beach, because the land inland was rocky.","t":"島上的第一批移居者把家建在海灘附近,因為內陸的土地多岩石。"},{"w":"shame","p":"n.","d":"a painful feeling that you have done something wrong or silly","c":"羞恥；可惜的事","s":"It's a shame that the night market is closed tonight; I really wanted some stinky tofu.","t":"真可惜夜市今晚沒開，我好想吃臭豆腐。"},{"w":"ashamed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling bad because you did something wrong","c":"感到羞愧的","s":"Kevin felt deeply ashamed after he shouted at his little sister for no reason.","t":"凱文無緣無故對妹妹大吼之後，感到非常羞愧。"},{"w":"shameful","p":"adj.","d":"so bad that people should feel ashamed of it","c":"可恥的","s":"Cheating on a test is shameful behavior.","t":"考試作弊是可恥的行為。"},{"w":"shameless","p":"adj.","d":"not feeling ashamed even though you should","c":"無恥的","s":"The shameless salesman kept calling my grandmother every day even after she had told him many times to stop.","t":"那個無恥的推銷員即使在我奶奶多次要他停止之後，仍然每天打電話給她。"},{"w":"shift","p":"v./n.","d":"to move or change something from one place or position to another","c":"轉移；改變；轉變；輪班","s":"She has the night shift at the hospital.","t":"她在醫院有夜班。"},{"w":"shifting","p":"adj.","d":"changing from one thing to another","c":"變動的","s":"Last year, the bakery shifted its focus from cakes to bread.","t":"去年那家麵包店把重心從蛋糕轉移到麵包。"},{"w":"sigh","p":"v./n.","d":"to emit a long, deep, audible breath expressing sadness, relief, or tiredness","c":"嘆氣；嘆息","s":"\"I have so much homework,\" Ben said with a deep sigh.","t":"「我好多功課喔。」班深深嘆了一口氣說。"},{"w":"sighing","p":"n.","d":"the sound of breathing out deeply","c":"嘆息聲","s":"Stop sighing and start doing your work!","t":"別再唉聲嘆氣了，開始做事吧！。"},{"w":"significant","p":"adj.","d":"large or important","c":"重要的；顯著的","s":"There has been a significant increase in sales.","t":"銷售額有了顯著增長。"},{"w":"significance","p":"n.","d":"the importance or meaning of something","c":"重要性","s":"The significance of this discovery cannot be understated.","t":"這一發現的重要性不可低估。"},{"w":"significantly","p":"adv.","d":"by an important amount","c":"顯著地","s":"Vegetable prices rose significantly after the typhoon.","t":"颱風過後菜價大幅上漲。"},{"w":"insignificant","p":"adj.","d":"too small or unimportant to matter","c":"微不足道的","s":"Don't worry about such an insignificant mistake; it won't affect your grade.","t":"別擔心這麼微不足道的錯誤；不會影響你的成績。"}]},{"unit":29,"theme":"similar – splendor · 15 字族 · 38 題","cards":[{"w":"similar","p":"adj.","d":"looking or being almost, but not exactly, the same","c":"相似的","s":"Your phone is very similar to mine; we even have the same case.","t":"你的手機跟我的很像，我們連手機殼都一樣。"},{"w":"similarly","p":"adv.","d":"in the same way","c":"同樣地","s":"Taiwanese students study hard for exams; similarly, students in Korea spend long hours in cram schools.","t":"台灣學生為考試用功；同樣地，韓國學生也在補習班待很久。"},{"w":"similarity","p":"n.","d":"the way in which things are alike","c":"相似之處","s":"There is a strong similarity between the rocks in Scotland and Canada, so scientists believe the two areas were once joined.","t":"蘇格蘭和加拿大的岩石之間有很強的相似性，所以科學家相信這兩個地區曾經相連。"},{"w":"sincere","p":"adj.","d":"honest, genuine, and not pretending","c":"真誠的","s":"He wrote a very sincere apology letter to his best friend, and she happily forgave him for his thoughtless mistake.","t":"他給最好的朋友寫了一封非常真誠的道歉信，她高興地原諒了他輕率的錯誤。"},{"w":"sincerely","p":"adv.","d":"honestly; used at the end of a formal letter","c":"真誠地","s":"I sincerely hope that you will enjoy your stay in Taiwan.","t":"我衷心希望你在台灣過得愉快。"},{"w":"sincerity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being honest and meaning what you say","c":"真誠","s":"The audience could feel the sincerity in his songs, because he wrote them about his own difficult childhood.","t":"觀眾能感受到他歌曲中的真誠,因為他寫的是自己艱辛的童年。"},{"w":"insincere","p":"adj.","d":"not honest; not meaning what you say","c":"不真誠的","s":"His apology sounded insincere because he was smiling and checking his phone the whole time.","t":"他的道歉聽起來不真誠，因為他全程都在笑和看手機。"},{"w":"situate","p":"v.","d":"to build or place something in a particular position","c":"使位於","s":"The ancient people chose to situate their village on a hill, because it was safer from floods and enemies.","t":"古人選擇把他們的村莊建在山丘上,因為那裡比較不會受洪水和敵人侵擾。"},{"w":"situated","p":"adj.","d":"in a particular place","c":"位於…的","s":"Our hotel is situated right next to the Tamsui River.","t":"我們的飯店就位在淡水河旁邊。"},{"w":"situation","p":"n.","d":"a set of conditions or state of affairs at a time.","c":"情況；處境","s":"The situation became worse when the typhoon cut off the power.","t":"颱風造成停電後情況變得更糟。"},{"w":"skill","p":"n.","d":"an ability to do an activity or job well, especially that is learned","c":"技能","s":"Learning carpentry requires both creative patience and the practical skill to use specialized hand tools.","t":"學習木工既需要創造性的耐心，也需要使用專業手工具的實用技能。"},{"w":"skillful","p":"adj.","d":"good at doing something","c":"熟練的","s":"He is very skillful with his hands.","t":"他的手很靈巧。"},{"w":"skillfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows great ability","c":"熟練地","s":"The chef skillfully cut the fish into thin slices.","t":"廚師熟練地把魚切成薄片。"},{"w":"skilled","p":"adj.","d":"having the training to do a job well","c":"有技術的","s":"The company needs skilled workers who can repair robots, but it is hard to find enough of them.","t":"公司需要能修理機器人的有技術的工人,但很難找到足夠的人手。"},{"w":"slave","p":"n.","d":"a person who is owned by another person and must work for them","c":"奴隸","s":"Don't let yourself become a slave to your smartphone.","t":"別讓自己變成手機的奴隸。"},{"w":"slavery","p":"n.","d":"the system of owning people and forcing them to work","c":"奴隸制度","s":"Abraham Lincoln is famous for helping to end slavery in the United States.","t":"林肯以協助終結美國奴隸制度聞名。"},{"w":"enslave","p":"v.","d":"To make someone a slave.","c":"奴役","s":"The aggressive invading army managed to capture and brutally enslave hundreds of innocent villagers during the violent and chaotic attack.","t":"具攻擊性的入侵軍隊不幸地在暴力且混亂的攻擊中，成功俘虜並殘忍地奴役了數百名無辜的村民。"},{"w":"enslaved","p":"adj.","d":"made into a slave","c":"被奴役的","s":"Millions of Africans were enslaved and shipped to the Americas.","t":"數百萬非洲人被奴役並被運往美洲。"},{"w":"slight","p":"adj.","d":"small and not important or serious","c":"輕微的","s":"Even a slight change in water temperature can harm coral reefs.","t":"即使水溫只有些微變化也可能傷害珊瑚礁。"},{"w":"slightly","p":"adv.","d":"a little","c":"稍微","s":"The new phone is slightly more expensive than the old one.","t":"新手機比舊的稍微貴一點。"},{"w":"slightest","p":"adj.","d":"smallest","c":"最輕微的","s":"There isn't the slightest chance that it will snow in Kaohsiung.","t":"高雄下雪的機率是零。"},{"w":"slip","p":"v./n.","d":"to slide accidentally, causing a fall; a small piece of paper","c":"滑倒；溜走；紙條；失誤","s":"The elderly man happened to slip on the wet kitchen tiles this morning, and he unfortunately bruised his left knee.","t":"那位年邁的先生今天早上碰巧在濕滑的廚房磁磚上【滑倒】，不幸挫傷了他的左膝蓋。"},{"w":"slippery","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to hold firmly or walk on; unreliable or elusive","c":"滑的","s":"Be careful! The bathroom floor is very slippery.","t":"小心！浴室地板很滑。"},{"w":"slipper","p":"n.","d":"a soft shoe worn at home","c":"拖鞋","s":"Be careful! The bathroom floor is very slippery.","t":"小心！浴室地板很滑。"},{"w":"smooth","p":"adj./v.","d":"flat and even with no rough parts","c":"平滑的；使平順","s":"The workers used a machine to smooth the surface of the new road.","t":"工人用機器把新道路的路面弄平。"},{"w":"smoothly","p":"adv.","d":"flawlessly; without any problem or complication.","c":"順利地","s":"Thanks to careful planning, the school concert went very smoothly.","t":"多虧仔細規劃，學校音樂會進行得非常順利。"},{"w":"smoothness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being even with no rough parts","c":"平滑","s":"Thanks to careful planning, the school concert went very smoothly.","t":"多虧仔細規劃，學校音樂會進行得非常順利。"},{"w":"smuggle","p":"v.","d":"to take things or people into or out of a country illegally","c":"走私；偷運","s":"The man tried to smuggle rare birds into the country in his suitcase.","t":"那人試圖把稀有鳥類藏在行李箱中走私入境。"},{"w":"smuggler","p":"n.","d":"a person who smuggles goods illegally","c":"走私者","s":"The police arrested a smuggler at the harbour, because he was hiding hundreds of parrots in small plastic tubes.","t":"警方在港口逮捕了一名走私者，因為他把數百隻鸚鵡藏在小塑膠管裡。"},{"w":"smuggling","p":"n.","d":"the crime of taking things into or out of a country illegally","c":"走私","s":"Drug smuggling is a very serious crime in Taiwan, and the signs at the airport warn travelers about it in several languages.","t":"毒品走私在台灣是非常嚴重的罪行，機場的標示用好幾種語言警告旅客。"},{"w":"solve","p":"v.","d":"to find an answer to, explanation for, or means of dealing with a problem","c":"解決","s":"Dedicated environmental engineers are working hard to solve the serious groundwater pollution problem in this industrial town.","t":"敬業的環境工程師們正努力工作，以【解決】這個工業城鎮嚴重的地下水污染問題。"},{"w":"solution","p":"n.","d":"a means of solving a problem or dealing with a difficult situation","c":"解決辦法；解答","s":"Installing solar panels on the school roof provided an eco-friendly and cost-effective solution for high electricity bills.","t":"在學校屋頂安裝太陽能電池板，為高昂的電費帳單提供了一個環保且具成本效益的【解決方法】。"},{"w":"solvable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be solved","c":"可解決的","s":"Don't panic. Most problems are solvable if you stay calm and think them through.","t":"別慌，只要冷靜思考，大部分問題都能解決。"},{"w":"sort","p":"v./n.","d":"to put things into groups by type, size, date, etc.","c":"分類；整理；種類","s":"Please sort your trash into paper, plastic and food waste.","t":"請將垃圾分成紙類、塑膠和廚餘。"},{"w":"sorting","p":"n.","d":"putting things into groups","c":"分類","s":"Volunteers spent the afternoon sorting donated clothes by size.","t":"志工花了一下午依尺寸整理捐贈的衣服。"},{"w":"sparkle","p":"v./n.","d":"to shine with small bright flashes of light","c":"閃耀；光彩","s":"Every evening, the lights of Taipei 101 sparkle against the dark sky.","t":"每天晚上，台北101的燈光在夜空中閃耀。"},{"w":"sparkling","p":"adj.","d":"shining brightly with small flashes of light","c":"閃閃發亮的；氣泡的","s":"Her sparkling eyes revealed her excitement.","t":"她閃閃發光的眼睛透露出她的興奮。"},{"w":"sparkly","p":"adj.","d":"shining with small points of light","c":"閃亮的","s":"Every evening, the lights of Taipei 101 sparkle against the dark sky.","t":"每天晚上，台北101的燈光在夜空中閃耀。"},{"w":"special","p":"adj.","d":"different from others in a good way","c":"特別的","s":"Q: Which day is the most special to you? — A: My birthday is the most special day of the year.","t":"對你來說哪一天最特別？ — 我的生日是一年中最特別的一天。"},{"w":"specialty","p":"n.","d":"a food or product that a place is famous for; something you are very good at","c":"專長；特產","s":"Stinky tofu is a famous specialty of Shenkeng.","t":"臭豆腐是深坑著名的特產。"},{"w":"specialize","p":"v.","d":"to spend most of your time on one subject or activity","c":"專攻","s":"This restaurant specializes in seafood, so you should try the fish and shrimp rather than the beef.","t":"這家餐廳專做海鮮，所以你應該嘗嘗魚和蝦，而不是牛肉。"},{"w":"specialist","p":"n.","d":"a person who knows a lot about one subject","c":"專家","s":"The doctor sent me to an eye specialist for further checks.","t":"醫生把我轉介給眼科專家做進一步檢查。"},{"w":"specially","p":"adv.","d":"for a special purpose","c":"特別地","s":"Stinky tofu is a famous specialty of Shenkeng.","t":"臭豆腐是深坑著名的特產。"},{"w":"spirit","p":"n.","d":"the non-physical part of a person; mood; courage and enthusiasm","c":"精神；靈魂","s":"Despite losing the first game, the team kept up their fighting spirit and won the next two.","t":"雖然輸了第一場，球隊保持鬥志並贏下接下來兩場。"},{"w":"spiritual","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the human spirit or with religion, not with the body","c":"精神上的；心靈的","s":"For many people, temple music has a spiritual meaning, and it helps them feel calm and connected to their ancestors.","t":"對許多人來說,廟宇音樂具有心靈上的意義,它幫助他們感到平靜並與祖先相連。"},{"w":"spirited","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and strong feeling","c":"充滿活力的","s":"The players gave a spirited performance and the crowd cheered them on until the end.","t":"球員們表現得生氣勃勃，觀眾一路為他們加油到最後。"},{"w":"spiritually","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with the spirit or religion","c":"精神上","s":"Many people say that hiking in the mountains makes them feel spiritually refreshed.","t":"很多人說在山裡健行讓他們心靈煥然一新。"},{"w":"splendor","p":"n.","d":"great beauty that impresses people","c":"壯麗；輝煌","s":"We were amazed by the splendor of the Forbidden City.","t":"我們對紫禁城的壯麗感到驚嘆。"},{"w":"splendid","p":"adj.","d":"excellent; very beautiful or impressive","c":"壯麗的；極好的","s":"From the hotel window we had a splendid view of the harbor, with hundreds of boats and the mountains behind them.","t":"從飯店的窗戶我們可以看到港口壯麗的景色，有數百艘船和後面的山。"},{"w":"splendidly","p":"adv.","d":"in an excellent or impressive way","c":"極好地","s":"The young pianist played splendidly and received a standing ovation.","t":"年輕鋼琴家演奏得極為出色，全場起立鼓掌。"}]},{"unit":30,"theme":"stable – suspect · 15 字族 · 37 題","cards":[{"w":"stable","p":"adj.","d":"not likely to change","c":"穩定的","s":"The economy has remained stable despite global challenges.","t":"儘管面臨全球挑戰，經濟仍然保持穩定。"},{"w":"stability","p":"n.","d":"the state of being steady and not changing","c":"穩定","s":"Most people want a job that offers stability and a good salary.","t":"大多數人都想要一份穩定且薪水好的工作。"},{"w":"unstable","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change suddenly","c":"不穩定的","s":"The old ladder is unstable, so please don't climb it.","t":"那把舊梯子不穩，所以請不要爬。"},{"w":"stabilize","p":"v.","d":"to become steady or make something steady","c":"使穩定","s":"The doctors worked all night to stabilize the patient's condition after the serious car accident.","t":"嚴重車禍後，醫生們整夜努力穩定病人的狀況。"},{"w":"strike","p":"v./n.","d":"to hit forcibly; an organized refusal to work by employees","c":"打；襲擊；罷工","s":"The bus drivers went on strike for higher pay.","t":"公車司機為了加薪而罷工。"},{"w":"struck","p":"v.","d":"hit; past form of strike","c":"strike 的過去式/過去分詞","s":"The bus drivers went on strike for higher pay.","t":"公車司機為了加薪而罷工。"},{"w":"striking","p":"adj.","d":"very unusual or attractive, so people notice it","c":"引人注目的","s":"The new museum has a striking design that looks like a giant wave.","t":"新博物館的設計很吸睛，看起來像一道巨浪。"},{"w":"strive","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to achieve something","c":"努力；奮鬥","s":"You should always strive to do your best, even when it is hard.","t":"即使很難，你也該總是努力做到最好。"},{"w":"striving","p":"n.","d":"trying very hard","c":"努力","s":"Our school strives to give every student a chance to shine.","t":"我們學校努力讓每個學生都有發光的機會。"},{"w":"strove","p":"v. (past)","d":"tried very hard (past)","c":"努力（過去式）","s":"The team strove for victory but lost in the final seconds.","t":"球隊奮力爭取勝利，卻在最後幾秒輸掉。"},{"w":"striven","p":"v. (p.p.)","d":"tried very hard (past participle)","c":"努力（過去分詞）","s":"Our school strives to give every student a chance to shine.","t":"我們學校努力讓每個學生都有發光的機會。"},{"w":"strong","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of power in your body","c":"強壯的；強烈的","s":"Q: Do you feel good after swimming? — A: Yes, I do. I swim every day, so I feel strong.","t":"你游泳後覺得很好嗎？ — 是的，我覺得很好。我每天游泳，所以我覺得很強壯。"},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"the physical power or durability of an object.","c":"力量；優點","s":"Lifting weights twice a week can improve your strength.","t":"每週舉重兩次可以增強你的力量。"},{"w":"strengthen","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger","c":"加強","s":"The government wants to strengthen safety rules for drones, because several have crashed into homes this year.","t":"政府想要加強無人機的安全規範,因為今年已有好幾架撞進民宅。"},{"w":"strongly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very firm or powerful way","c":"強烈地","s":"I strongly believe that every student should learn to swim.","t":"我堅信每個學生都應該學游泳。"},{"w":"stun","p":"v.","d":"to surprise or shock someone so much that they cannot speak or react","c":"使震驚","s":"The news of the school's closing seemed to stun the teachers, and nobody said a word for almost a minute.","t":"學校即將關閉的消息似乎震驚了老師們，將近一分鐘沒有人說一句話。"},{"w":"stunned","p":"adj.","d":"very surprised or shocked","c":"震驚的","s":"The stunned audience sat in silence for a moment when the magician made the whole car disappear from the stage.","t":"當魔術師讓整輛車從舞台上消失時，震驚的觀眾安靜地坐了一會兒。"},{"w":"stunning","p":"adj.","d":"extremely beautiful or impressive","c":"極美的；驚人的","s":"The view of Sun Moon Lake at sunrise is absolutely stunning.","t":"日月潭日出的景色美得令人驚嘆。"},{"w":"stunningly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very beautiful or surprising way","c":"驚人地","s":"The actress looked stunningly beautiful on the red carpet.","t":"那位女演員在紅毯上美得驚人。"},{"w":"substance","p":"n.","d":"a particular type of solid, liquid or gas","c":"物質；實質內容","s":"The candidate's speech sounded nice, but it had little real substance.","t":"那位候選人的演講聽起來不錯，卻沒什麼實質內容。"},{"w":"substantial","p":"adj.","d":"large in amount or importance","c":"相當大的；實質的","s":"The school spent a substantial amount of money on new tablets, but many teachers still prefer paper and pens.","t":"學校花了可觀的金額購買新平板,但許多老師仍偏好紙筆。"},{"w":"substantially","p":"adv.","d":"by a large amount","c":"大幅地","s":"Thanks to the new bus route, the trip to school has been substantially shortened.","t":"多虧新的公車路線，上學的路程大幅縮短了。"},{"w":"succeed","p":"v.","d":"to do what you tried to do","c":"成功","s":"With enough effort, you can succeed in achieving your goals.","t":"通過足夠的努力，您可以在實現目標方面取得成功。"},{"w":"success","p":"n.","d":"getting what you want","c":"成功","s":"Hard work and determination are key factors for success.","t":"努力和決心是成功的關鍵因素。"},{"w":"successful","p":"adj.","d":"having good results","c":"成功的","s":"The successful entrepreneur shared his journey and experiences in a recent interview.","t":"成功的企業家最近在一次訪談中分享了他的旅程和經歷。"},{"w":"successfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that achieves what you wanted","c":"成功地","s":"The rocket was launched successfully from the space center this morning.","t":"今天早上火箭從太空中心成功發射。"},{"w":"unsuccessful","p":"adj.","d":"not getting the result you wanted","c":"不成功的","s":"After three unsuccessful attempts, Amy finally passed her driving test.","t":"經過三次失敗的嘗試，Amy 終於通過駕照考試。"},{"w":"suit","p":"v./n.","d":"a jacket with matching pants or skirt; to be right for someone","c":"適合；西裝","s":"The job suits her well because she loves talking to people.","t":"這份工作很適合她，因為她喜歡和人聊天。"},{"w":"suitable","p":"adj.","d":"right for a purpose","c":"合適的","s":"The beach was no longer suitable for nesting, because hotels had been built along the sand.","t":"這片海灘已不再適合築巢，因為沙灘沿岸已經蓋了飯店。"},{"w":"unsuitable","p":"adj.","d":"not right for a purpose","c":"不合適的","s":"This hiking trail is unsuitable for small children because it is steep and slippery.","t":"這條登山步道又陡又滑，不適合小孩。"},{"w":"summary","p":"n.","d":"a short statement of the main points","c":"摘要","s":"Please write a short summary of the article in no more than fifty words.","t":"請用不超過五十字寫一段文章摘要。"},{"w":"summarize","p":"v.","d":"to give the main points of something in a short form","c":"總結；摘要","s":"He was able to summarize the lengthy report in just a few sentences.","t":"他能夠用幾句話總結那份冗長的報告。"},{"w":"in summary","p":"phr.","d":"summary · C 固定搭配","c":"總之","s":"Please write a short summary of the article in no more than fifty words.","t":"請用不超過五十字寫一段文章摘要。"},{"w":"superior","p":"adj./n.","d":"better than others in quality","c":"較好的；上司","s":"The camera on this phone is superior to the one on the older model.","t":"這支手機的相機比舊款的好。"},{"w":"superiority","p":"n.","d":"the state of being better, stronger, or more important than others","c":"優越；優勢","s":"The home team showed clear superiority and won the game 10 to 0.","t":"主隊展現明顯優勢，以十比零贏得比賽。"},{"w":"superiors","p":"n.","d":"people with higher positions at work","c":"上司（複數）","s":"Workers should report any safety problems to their superiors.","t":"員工應向上司報告任何安全問題。"},{"w":"supply","p":"v./n.","d":"an amount of something available for use; to provide","c":"供應；供給","s":"The international charity delivered an urgent supply of clean drinking water and canned food to the disaster zone.","t":"國際慈善機構向災區運送了緊急的純淨飲用水與罐頭食品物資（供應）。"},{"w":"supplies","p":"n.","d":"things that people need, like food or tools","c":"補給品","s":"Before the typhoon, people rushed to buy supplies such as instant noodles and bottled water.","t":"颱風來襲前，民眾搶購泡麵、瓶裝水等物資。"},{"w":"supplier","p":"n.","d":"a company that provides goods to another company","c":"供應商","s":"Taiwan is a major supplier of computer chips to the world.","t":"台灣是全球主要的電腦晶片供應國。"},{"w":"support","p":"v./n.","d":"to help someone emotionally or practically; to hold up physically","c":"支持；支撐","s":"Parents should always provide loving support and encouragement when their children face difficult challenges.","t":"當孩子面臨艱難挑戰時，父母應始終給予充滿愛意的支持與鼓勵。"},{"w":"supporter","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps or likes a person, group, or idea","c":"支持者","s":"A: How did the small bookstore on Park Road manage to stay open after the rent increased so much last year? B: One loyal supporter who had shopped there for twenty years organized a fundraising event, and many neighbors donated money and bought books to help the owner pay the bills.","t":"A：公園路上那家小書店在去年房租大漲之後，是怎麼繼續營業的？ B：一位在那裡購物二十年的忠實【支持者】籌辦了一場募款活動，許多鄰居捐錢並買書，幫助老闆支付帳單。"},{"w":"supportive","p":"adj.","d":"giving help and encouragement","c":"支持的；給予鼓勵的","s":"Luckily, my friends were very supportive when I decided to change schools.","t":"幸好我決定轉學時，朋友們都很支持我。"},{"w":"surround","p":"v.","d":"to move all the way around an entry to close it in.","c":"包圍；環繞","s":"Tall buildings surround our school, so we can't see the mountains.","t":"高樓環繞我們學校，所以看不到山。"},{"w":"surrounding","p":"adj.","d":"existing entirely around a central point or object.","c":"周圍的","s":"Sun Moon Lake and the surrounding mountains look beautiful at sunrise.","t":"日月潭和周圍的山在日出時很美。"},{"w":"surroundings","p":"n.","d":"everything that is around you in a place","c":"環境（複數）","s":"It took her a few weeks to get used to her new surroundings after moving to the countryside from the busy city.","t":"從繁忙的城市搬到農村後，她花了幾週時間才適應新的環境。"},{"w":"surrounded","p":"adj.","d":"having things or people all around","c":"被包圍的","s":"Taiwan is surrounded by the sea.","t":"台灣四面環海。"},{"w":"survive","p":"v.","d":"to stay alive","c":"存活；倖存","s":"Cactuses can survive for months without water.","t":"仙人掌沒水也能存活好幾個月。"},{"w":"survival","p":"n.","d":"staying alive","c":"存活","s":"The survival of the fittest is a concept derived from evolutionary theory.","t":"適者生存是從進化理論中得出的概念。"},{"w":"survivor","p":"n.","d":"a person who stays alive after danger","c":"倖存者","s":"The survivor of the accident were rescued and provided medical attention.","t":"事故的生還者得到了救援並得到了醫療照顧。"},{"w":"surviving","p":"adj.","d":"still alive","c":"倖存的","s":"Only three people survived the plane crash.","t":"只有三人在空難中生還。"},{"w":"suspect","p":"v./n.","d":"to think that someone is guilty of a major felony.","c":"懷疑；嫌疑犯","s":"The investigators began to suspect that the fire had been started deliberately after finding traces of accelerant at the scene.","t":"調查人員在現場發現助燃劑的痕跡後，開始懷疑火災是故意放火引起的。"},{"w":"suspicion","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that someone has done something wrong","c":"懷疑","s":"The man was arrested on suspicion of stealing a car.","t":"那名男子因涉嫌偷車而被捕。"},{"w":"suspicious","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that someone may be doing something wrong; making people feel this way","c":"可疑的","s":"Call the police if you see any suspicious packages at the station.","t":"如果在車站看到任何可疑的包裹，請報警。"}]},{"unit":31,"theme":"sustain – tragedy · 15 字族 · 38 題","cards":[{"w":"sustain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something going over a long time; to support","c":"維持；支撐","s":"The city has been trying to sustain its historic landmarks for future generations.","t":"該城市一直在努力維護其歷史地標，以供後代參觀。"},{"w":"sustainable","p":"adj.","d":"able to continue for a long time without harming the environment","c":"永續的","s":"sustainable farming practices are vital for protecting the environment.","t":"可持續的農業實踐對於保護環境至關重要。"},{"w":"sustainably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that can continue for a long time","c":"永續地","s":"Fishing sustainably helps make sure there will be enough fish in the future.","t":"永續捕魚有助於確保未來有足夠的魚。"},{"w":"sustainability","p":"n.","d":"the ability to continue without harm","c":"永續性","s":"The company is trying to improve its sustainability by using recycled materials.","t":"這家公司正試著透過使用回收材料提升永續性。"},{"w":"swift","p":"adj.","d":"happening quickly","c":"迅速的","s":"The company's swift reply to the complaint impressed the customer, so she gave it five stars online.","t":"公司對投訴的迅速回覆讓顧客印象深刻，所以她在網路上給了五顆星。"},{"w":"swiftly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly","c":"迅速地","s":"The cat moved swiftly and caught the mouse.","t":"貓迅速移動，抓住了老鼠。"},{"w":"swiftness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being fast","c":"迅速","s":"The rescue team was praised for the swiftness of its response.","t":"救難隊因反應迅速而受到讚揚。"},{"w":"switch","p":"v./n.","d":"a small button or lever that turns a light or machine on and off","c":"轉換；切換；開關","s":"Please flip the switch to turn on the light.","t":"請切換開關打開燈。"},{"w":"symbol","p":"n.","d":"a sign or picture that stands for something","c":"象徵；符號","s":"The plum blossom is Taiwan's national flower and a symbol of strength.","t":"梅花是台灣的國花，也是堅毅的象徵。"},{"w":"symbolic","p":"adj.","d":"representing something important, such as an idea or feeling","c":"象徵性的","s":"Planting a tree together at the start of the school year has become a symbolic gesture representing growth and learning.","t":"在學年開始時一起種樹已成為一種象徵成長與學習的象徵性姿態。"},{"w":"symbolize","p":"v.","d":"to be a sign of something; to represent an idea","c":"象徵","s":"Doves are often used to symbolize peace.","t":"鴿子常被用來象徵和平。"},{"w":"technology","p":"n.","d":"science used to make machines and tools","c":"科技","s":"The impact of technology on society is undeniable.","t":"技術對社會的影響是不可否認的。"},{"w":"technological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with technology","c":"科技的","s":"The technological advancements in the last decade have been remarkable.","t":"過去十年的科技進步非常引人注目。"},{"w":"technologically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with technology","c":"科技上","s":"Taiwan is known as a technologically advanced island because of its computer chip industry.","t":"台灣因晶片產業而以科技先進的島嶼聞名。"},{"w":"technician","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to work with or repair machines and equipment","c":"技術人員","s":"My cousin works as a lab technician at a hospital in Taichung.","t":"我表哥在台中一家醫院當檢驗技術員。"},{"w":"tend","p":"v.","d":"to take care of something or someone","c":"傾向；照料","s":"People tend to eat more when they are stressed or bored.","t":"人在壓力大或無聊時往往吃得比較多。"},{"w":"tendency","p":"n.","d":"the way a person or thing is likely to behave or happen","c":"傾向","s":"Tom has a tendency to leave everything until the last minute, so his teacher helped him make a weekly plan.","t":"湯姆有把每件事都拖到最後一刻的傾向,所以老師幫他擬定每週計畫。"},{"w":"tender","p":"adj.","d":"(of meat) soft and easy to cut; painful when touched","c":"溫柔的；嫩的","s":"The beef was so tender that it fell apart in my mouth.","t":"牛肉嫩到在嘴裡化開。"},{"w":"terrify","p":"v.","d":"to make someone extremely frightened","c":"使驚恐","s":"Loud fireworks terrify my dog every Lunar New Year.","t":"每年農曆新年，響亮的鞭炮聲都嚇壞我的狗。"},{"w":"terrified","p":"adj.","d":"extremely frightened","c":"感到驚恐的","s":"She was terrified of the dark as a child, so her parents always left a small lamp on in the hallway.","t":"她小時候非常害怕黑暗，所以父母總是在走廊留一盞小燈。"},{"w":"terrifying","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel extremely frightened","c":"令人驚恐的","s":"Riding the roller coaster at night was a terrifying experience.","t":"晚上搭雲霄飛車是很嚇人的經驗。"},{"w":"terror","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great fear","c":"恐懼","s":"The children screamed in terror when the lights suddenly went out during the ghost story at the summer camp.","t":"夏令營講鬼故事時燈突然熄滅，孩子們驚恐地尖叫。"},{"w":"theory","p":"n.","d":"an idea that explains why something happens","c":"理論","s":"Einstein's theory of relativity changed the way we see the universe.","t":"愛因斯坦的相對論改變了我們看宇宙的方式。"},{"w":"theoretical","p":"adj.","d":"based on ideas rather than practice or experience","c":"理論上的","s":"His approach is more theoretical than practical.","t":"他的方法更加理論化，而不是實際的。"},{"w":"theoretically","p":"adv.","d":"according to theory, but not yet proven in practice","c":"理論上","s":"Theoretically, the plan should work, but we haven't tested it yet.","t":"理論上這個計畫應該行得通，但我們還沒測試過。"},{"w":"thought","p":"n.","d":"an idea, opinion, or mental consideration","c":"想法；思考","s":"After giving careful thought to the job offer in Singapore, David decided to accept it to broaden his international horizons.","t":"在對新加坡的工作錄取進行慎重考慮之後，戴維決定接受它以拓展自己的國際視野。"},{"w":"thoughtful","p":"adj.","d":"kind and thinking about what other people need; quiet and thinking deeply","c":"體貼的；深思的","s":"It was thoughtful of you to bring me soup when I was sick.","t":"我生病時你帶湯來給我，真是體貼。"},{"w":"thoughtless","p":"adj.","d":"not thinking about how your actions affect other people","c":"不體貼的","s":"Forgetting to thank your host is a thoughtless thing to do.","t":"忘了向主人道謝是很不體貼的行為。"},{"w":"thoughtfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind way; in a way that shows deep thinking","c":"體貼地；沉思地","s":"The old man looked out of the window thoughtfully, remembering his youth.","t":"老人若有所思地望向窗外，回想著年輕時光。"},{"w":"threat","p":"n.","d":"something that may cause harm or danger","c":"威脅","s":"Plastic waste is a serious threat to sea turtles and other ocean animals.","t":"塑膠垃圾對海龜和其他海洋動物是嚴重威脅。"},{"w":"threaten","p":"v.","d":"to put something in danger","c":"威脅","s":"Rising sea levels threaten the nesting beaches of sea turtles, and some beaches may disappear completely in the future.","t":"海平面上升威脅到海龜的築巢海灘，而有些海灘未來可能會完全消失。"},{"w":"threatening","p":"adj.","d":"Having a hostile or deliberately frightening quality.","c":"威脅的；險惡的","s":"Dark, threatening clouds gathered over the mountains, so we turned back.","t":"山上聚集了險惡的烏雲，所以我們折返了。"},{"w":"torture","p":"n./v.","d":"the act of causing great pain to someone, often as a punishment","c":"折磨；酷刑","s":"Waiting a whole week for the exam results was torture for me.","t":"等了整整一週的考試成績，對我來說是種折磨。"},{"w":"tortured","p":"adj.","d":"hurt very badly on purpose","c":"受折磨的","s":"In the past, prisoners of war were often tortured to make them give away secrets.","t":"過去戰俘常遭酷刑逼供。"},{"w":"torturing","p":"v.","d":"hurting someone very badly on purpose","c":"折磨（V-ing）","s":"Stop torturing yourself over that small mistake; everyone makes them.","t":"別再為那個小錯誤折磨自己了；每個人都會犯錯。"},{"w":"tour","p":"n./v.","d":"a trip visiting several places","c":"旅遊；巡迴","s":"Our guide took us on a two-hour tour of the old town.","t":"導遊帶我們參觀老城區兩小時。"},{"w":"tourist","p":"n.","d":"a person who visits a place for fun","c":"觀光客","s":"The city is full of tourists.","t":"這個城市充滿了遊客。"},{"w":"tourism","p":"n.","d":"the business or activity of people traveling for pleasure.","c":"觀光業","s":"Tourism plays a significant role in the economy of many countries, attracting visitors from around the world and generating revenue.","t":"旅遊在許多國家的經濟中扮演重要角色，吸引世界各地的遊客並產生收入。"},{"w":"trace","p":"n./v.","d":"a small sign that something was there","c":"痕跡；微量；追蹤；描摹","s":"Archaeologists found trace of ancient civilizations at the site.","t":"考古學家在該地點找到了古文明的痕迹。"},{"w":"traceable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be followed back to its origin","c":"可追溯的","s":"All the timber in the shop is traceable, so customers can check which forest the wood came from.","t":"店裡所有的木材都是可追溯的,所以顧客可以查到木頭來自哪一片森林。"},{"w":"tradition","p":"n.","d":"a custom passed down from the past","c":"傳統","s":"Eating mooncakes during the Moon Festival is a Taiwanese tradition.","t":"中秋節吃月餅是台灣的傳統。"},{"w":"traditional","p":"adj.","d":"following old customs","c":"傳統的","s":"They wore traditional costumes for the festival.","t":"他們穿傳統服裝參加節日。"},{"w":"traditionally","p":"adv.","d":"according to old customs that have existed for a long time","c":"傳統上","s":"Traditionally, red envelopes are given to children during the Lunar New Year.","t":"傳統上，過年時會給小孩紅包。"},{"w":"tragedy","p":"n.","d":"a very sad event, especially one in which people die","c":"悲劇","s":"The bus accident on the highway was a terrible tragedy.","t":"高速公路上的巴士事故是一場可怕的悲劇。"},{"w":"tragic","p":"adj.","d":"very sad, often because someone dies or suffers","c":"悲慘的","s":"It was tragic that the young singer died in a car crash just one week before her first big concert.","t":"那位年輕歌手在她第一場大型演唱會前一週死於車禍，真是悲慘。"},{"w":"tragically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is very sad","c":"悲慘地","s":"The young singer tragically died in a car accident at the age of 27.","t":"那位年輕歌手在27歲時不幸死於車禍。"}]},{"unit":32,"theme":"transform – valid · 15 字族 · 36 題","cards":[{"w":"transform","p":"v.","d":"to change something completely, usually in a good way","c":"轉變","s":"The renovation will transform the old building into a modern workspace.","t":"裝修將把老建築變成現代化的工作空間。"},{"w":"transformation","p":"n.","d":"a complete change in the form or appearance of something","c":"轉變","s":"The transformation of the city's skyline over the decades is remarkable.","t":"數十年來，城市天際線的轉變非常顯著。"},{"w":"transformed","p":"adj.","d":"completely changed","c":"煥然一新的","s":"The old warehouse has been transformed into a popular café.","t":"那間舊倉庫已改建成一家熱門咖啡廳。"},{"w":"translate","p":"v.","d":"to change words from one language into another","c":"翻譯","s":"Tourists can now translate menus by pointing their phone camera at them, so ordering food abroad is much easier.","t":"遊客現在只要把手機鏡頭對準菜單就能翻譯,所以在國外點餐容易多了。"},{"w":"translation","p":"n.","d":"words that have been changed from one language into another","c":"翻譯；譯文","s":"The English translation on the noodle shop's menu was so funny that tourists took photos of it.","t":"麵店菜單上的英文翻譯太好笑了，觀光客都拍照留念。"},{"w":"translator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to change written words into another language","c":"譯者","s":"The translator spent two years on the Harry Potter books, because she wanted every joke and name to work in Chinese.","t":"這位譯者花了兩年翻譯哈利波特系列，因為她希望每個笑話和名字在中文裡都行得通。"},{"w":"transport","p":"v./n.","d":"a system for moving people or goods","c":"運輸；運送；運輸（英式）","s":"The city's transport system is well-developed, with numerous buses, trains, and subway lines.","t":"該市的運輸系統非常發達，有許多公共汽車、火車和地鐵線路。"},{"w":"transportation","p":"n.","d":"the system of moving people or goods from one place to another","c":"交通運輸","s":"The MRT is the most convenient form of public transportation in Taipei.","t":"捷運是台北最方便的大眾運輸方式。"},{"w":"transporter","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle that carries things","c":"運輸工具","s":"Fresh fruit from Pingtung is transported to Taipei markets by truck every night.","t":"屏東的新鮮水果每晚用卡車運送到台北的市場。"},{"w":"trap","p":"n./v.","d":"to catch an animal in a trap; a device for catching animals","c":"陷阱；困住；捕捉","s":"The farmer set a trap to catch the wild boar that ate his crops.","t":"農夫設下陷阱要抓吃他農作物的山豬。"},{"w":"trapped","p":"adj.","d":"not able to escape","c":"被困住的","s":"The farmer set a trap to catch the wild boar that ate his crops.","t":"農夫設下陷阱要抓吃他農作物的山豬。"},{"w":"treasure","p":"n./v.","d":"valuable things such as gold or gems; to cherish something deeply","c":"寶藏；珍寶；珍惜","s":"The pirate captain buried his iron chest full of gold treasure on a remote desert island where no explorer could ever find it.","t":"海盜船長將裝滿黃金寶藏的鐵箱埋在一個沒有探險家能找到的偏僻荒島上。"},{"w":"treasured","p":"adj.","d":"very valuable and loved","c":"珍貴的","s":"This old watch from my grandfather is my most treasured possession.","t":"爺爺留下的這只舊錶是我最珍貴的東西。"},{"w":"treat","p":"v./n.","d":"something nice that someone buys for you","c":"對待；治療；請客；款待；零食","s":"Always treat others the way you want to be treated.","t":"永遠用你希望被對待的方式對待別人。"},{"w":"treatment","p":"n.","d":"medical care given to a patient for an illness or injury","c":"治療；對待","s":"The patient responded remarkably well to the physical therapy treatment, and she was able to walk without crutches in a month.","t":"這位病患對物理治療【療程】反應極佳，不到一個月她就能不用拐杖行走了。"},{"w":"tremendous","p":"adj.","d":"very great in amount, size, or degree","c":"巨大的；極好的","s":"Running a full marathon requires a tremendous amount of training.","t":"跑全程馬拉松需要大量訓練。"},{"w":"tremendously","p":"adv.","d":"very much; extremely","c":"非常；極大地","s":"The movie was tremendously popular among teenagers.","t":"這部電影在青少年之間非常受歡迎。"},{"w":"tremble","p":"v.","d":"to shake slightly because you are cold, afraid, or excited","c":"顫抖（同源字）","s":"My hands began to tremble when I opened the envelope with my test results, but I was relieved to see a good score.","t":"我打開裝著考試成績的信封時,雙手開始顫抖,但看到好成績我就鬆了一口氣。"},{"w":"tribe","p":"n.","d":"a group of families with the same customs and leader","c":"部落","s":"The Amis tribe holds its harvest festival every summer.","t":"阿美族每年夏天舉行豐年祭。"},{"w":"tribal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a tribe or tribes","c":"部落的","s":"The museum shows tribal clothing and tools from the past.","t":"博物館展示了過去的部落服飾和工具。"},{"w":"tribesman","p":"n.","d":"a man who belongs to a tribe","c":"部落成員","s":"There are sixteen officially recognized indigenous tribes in Taiwan.","t":"台灣有十六個官方認定的原住民族群。"},{"w":"tribes","p":"n. pl.","d":"groups of people with the same language and customs","c":"部落","s":"There are sixteen officially recognized indigenous tribes in Taiwan.","t":"台灣有十六個官方認定的原住民族群。"},{"w":"typical","p":"adj.","d":"usual or normal for a person, thing, or situation.","c":"典型的","s":"Stinky tofu is a typical snack you can find at almost any night market in Taiwan.","t":"臭豆腐是在台灣幾乎每個夜市都找得到的典型小吃。"},{"w":"typically","p":"adv.","d":"usually","c":"通常；典型地","s":"Female cats typically have four to six kittens, and the mother looks after them for about two months.","t":"母貓通常會生四到六隻小貓，而貓媽媽會照顧牠們大約兩個月。"},{"w":"atypical","p":"adj.","d":"not usual or normal","c":"非典型的","s":"Stinky tofu is a typical snack you can find at almost any night market in Taiwan.","t":"臭豆腐是在台灣幾乎每個夜市都找得到的典型小吃。"},{"w":"ultimate","p":"adj.","d":"final; happening at the end of a long process","c":"最終的；極致的","s":"Climbing Jade Mountain is the ultimate challenge for many hikers in Taiwan.","t":"攀登玉山是台灣許多登山客的終極挑戰。"},{"w":"ultimately","p":"adv.","d":"in the end","c":"最終；根本上","s":"The coach believes hard work will ultimately lead to success.","t":"教練相信努力最終會帶來成功。"},{"w":"ultimatum","p":"n.","d":"a final warning with a demand","c":"最後通牒","s":"The coach believes hard work will ultimately lead to success.","t":"教練相信努力最終會帶來成功。"},{"w":"unite","p":"v.","d":"to join together","c":"聯合；團結","s":"They decided to unite their efforts to achieve the objective.","t":"他們決定團結起來努力實現目標。"},{"w":"united","p":"adj.","d":"joined together as one","c":"團結的","s":"People from all over the country united to help the earthquake victims.","t":"全國各地的人團結起來幫助地震災民。"},{"w":"unity","p":"n.","d":"being together as one","c":"團結；統一","s":"The coach stressed the importance of team unity.","t":"教練強調團隊團結的重要。"},{"w":"reunite","p":"v.","d":"to bring people together again after a long time","c":"重聚","s":"The lost dog was finally reunited with its owner after a kind student found it and posted a photo online.","t":"一位好心的學生找到那隻走失的狗並在網路上貼了照片後，牠終於和主人重聚了。"},{"w":"reunion","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people who have not seen each other for a long time","c":"團聚","s":"Our family has a big reunion dinner on Lunar New Year's Eve.","t":"我們家除夕夜會吃豐盛的團圓飯。"},{"w":"universe","p":"n.","d":"all existing matter, energy, and space considered as a whole; cosmos","c":"宇宙","s":"Scientists believe the universe is about 13.8 billion years old.","t":"科學家相信宇宙大約有138億年的歷史。"},{"w":"universal","p":"adj.","d":"true or existing everywhere or for everyone","c":"普遍的；全世界的","s":"Access to clean drinking water should be a universal right, but millions of people around the world still lack it.","t":"獲得乾淨飲用水應是普遍的權利，但全世界仍有數百萬人缺乏這項資源。"},{"w":"universally","p":"adv.","d":"by everyone or everywhere","c":"普遍地","s":"Music is universally loved; people in every culture enjoy it.","t":"音樂受到普遍喜愛；每個文化的人都喜歡。"},{"w":"upset","p":"v./adj.","d":"unhappy or worried because something bad happened","c":"使難過；使不安（三態同形）；難過的","s":"The news of the typhoon damage upset everyone in the village yesterday.","t":"颱風災情的消息昨天讓全村的人都很難過。"},{"w":"upsetting","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel sad or worried","c":"令人難過的","s":"It was really upsetting to see my favorite team lose in the final.","t":"看到我最愛的隊伍在決賽輸掉真令人難過。"},{"w":"urge","p":"v./n.","d":"to try hard to persuade someone to do something","c":"催促；力勸；衝動；強烈慾望","s":"Late at night, I suddenly had a strong urge to eat fried chicken.","t":"深夜我突然很想吃炸雞。"},{"w":"urgent","p":"adj.","d":"needing to be dealt with immediately","c":"緊急的","s":"I have an urgent message for Mr. Wang. Can I talk to him now?","t":"我有緊急訊息要給王先生，現在可以跟他說話嗎？。"},{"w":"urgently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that needs immediate action","c":"緊急地","s":"The hospital urgently needs blood donors after the big accident.","t":"大車禍後醫院急需捐血者。"},{"w":"urgency","p":"n.","d":"the need to do something very quickly","c":"緊急","s":"Young people speak about climate change with real urgency, because they will live with the results for the longest time.","t":"年輕人談論氣候變遷時帶著真切的急迫感,因為他們將承受後果最久。"},{"w":"valid","p":"adj.","d":"legally or officially acceptable; still able to be used","c":"有效的；合理的","s":"The offer is no longer valid as it expired last month.","t":"由於上個月已過期，該優惠不再有效。"},{"w":"invalid","p":"adj.","d":"not legally or officially acceptable","c":"無效的","s":"Your student ID card is invalid without this year's sticker, so you can't borrow books.","t":"學生證沒有貼今年的貼紙就無效，所以你不能借書。"},{"w":"validity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being valid","c":"有效性；正確性","s":"Scientists doubted the validity of the survey because only twenty people took part.","t":"科學家懷疑這份調查的正確性，因為只有二十人參與。"}]},{"unit":33,"theme":"value – worth · 10 字族 · 27 題","cards":[{"w":"value","p":"n./v.","d":"the worth of something in money or importance; to appreciate","c":"價值；重視","s":"I really value my friendship with Amy.","t":"我真的很珍惜和艾美的友誼。"},{"w":"valuable","p":"adj.","d":"very useful or important","c":"貴重的；寶貴的","s":"Old museum specimens are valuable to scientists, because their DNA shows how species have changed.","t":"博物館的舊標本對科學家很寶貴，因為它們的DNA顯示了物種是如何改變的。"},{"w":"valuables","p":"n.","d":"valuable · A 延伸義","c":"貴重物品","s":"Please don't leave your valuables in the classroom during PE class.","t":"體育課時請別把貴重物品留在教室。"},{"w":"invaluable","p":"adj.","d":"extremely useful; too valuable to be measured","c":"非常寶貴的","s":"Your advice was invaluable; without it, I would have failed the interview.","t":"你的建議非常寶貴，沒有它我面試就失敗了。"},{"w":"vary","p":"v.","d":"to change or be different","c":"變化；不同","s":"Prices vary from store to store, so compare them before you buy.","t":"各店價格不同，買前先比較。"},{"w":"various","p":"adj.","d":"many different kinds of","c":"各種的","s":"The exhibition showcased various types of artwork.","t":"展覽展示了各種各樣的藝術品。"},{"w":"variety","p":"n.","d":"a number of different types of things","c":"多樣性；種類","s":"Night markets in Taiwan offer a wide variety of snacks.","t":"台灣夜市提供各式各樣的小吃。"},{"w":"varied","p":"adj.","d":"including many different kinds","c":"多樣的","s":"Try to eat a varied diet with lots of fruit and vegetables.","t":"盡量吃多樣化、有大量蔬果的飲食。"},{"w":"variation","p":"n.","d":"a change or difference in amount or level","c":"變化","s":"There is a large variation in temperature on the moon, because the days are very hot and the nights are freezing.","t":"月球上的溫度變化很大，因為白天非常熱而夜晚極度寒冷。"},{"w":"violate","p":"v.","d":"to break a law, rule, or agreement","c":"違反；侵犯","s":"Drivers who violate the speed limit will get a heavy fine.","t":"超速的駕駛會被重罰。"},{"w":"violation","p":"n.","d":"an action that breaks a law or rule","c":"違反","s":"The violation of privacy is a serious offense.","t":"侵犯隱私是嚴重的犯罪。"},{"w":"violator","p":"n.","d":"a person who breaks a rule or law","c":"違規者","s":"Drivers who violate the speed limit will get a heavy fine.","t":"超速的駕駛會被重罰。"},{"w":"violent","p":"adj.","d":"very strong and dangerous","c":"暴力的；猛烈的","s":"Some video games are too violent for young children.","t":"有些電玩對小孩來說太暴力了。"},{"w":"violence","p":"n.","d":"actions that hurt or kill people","c":"暴力","s":"Schools should teach students to solve problems without violence.","t":"學校應教學生不用暴力解決問題。"},{"w":"violently","p":"adv.","d":"with great force; in a way that hurts people","c":"猛烈地","s":"The ship shook violently during the storm.","t":"暴風雨中船劇烈搖晃。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"a picture of the future you hope for","c":"視力；遠見","s":"His vision for the company's future included expanding into new markets.","t":"他對公司未來的視覺包括擴展到新市場。"},{"w":"visual","p":"adj.","d":"connected with seeing or sight","c":"視覺的","s":"Charts and pictures are useful visual aids in a presentation.","t":"圖表和圖片是簡報中有用的視覺輔助。"},{"w":"visible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be seen","c":"看得見的","s":"The top of the mountain was not visible because of the thick fog.","t":"因為濃霧，山頂看不見。"},{"w":"invisible","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be seen","c":"看不見的","s":"In the story, the boy puts on a magic coat and becomes invisible.","t":"故事裡男孩穿上魔法外套就隱形了。"},{"w":"warn","p":"v.","d":"to inform someone in advance of an impending danger, threat, or problem","c":"警告","s":"Signs along the trail warn hikers about snakes in the area.","t":"步道沿途的告示提醒登山客此區有蛇。"},{"w":"warning","p":"n.","d":"a statement or event that informs someone of a potential danger or problem","c":"警告","s":"The weather bureau issued a severe storm warning for all coastal areas of the island.","t":"氣象局對該島的所有沿海地區發布了嚴重的暴風雨警告。"},{"w":"forewarn","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone about a problem before it happens","c":"預先警告","s":"The doctor forewarn her that recovery would be slow, so she was not shocked when progress took months.","t":"醫生事先警告她復原會很慢，所以當進展花了好幾個月時她並不驚訝。"},{"w":"wealth","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of money and things that someone owns","c":"財富","s":"Grandpa always says that health is more important than wealth.","t":"爺爺總說健康比財富重要。"},{"w":"wealthy","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of money","c":"富有的","s":"In the 1960s, only the wealthy could afford to own a car in Taiwan.","t":"1960 年代的台灣，只有富人買得起汽車。"},{"w":"the wealthy","p":"n.","d":"wealthy · A 抽象/延伸義","c":"富人","s":"Grandpa always says that health is more important than wealth.","t":"爺爺總說健康比財富重要。"},{"w":"widow","p":"n.","d":"a woman whose husband has died and who has not married again","c":"寡婦","s":"After her husband died, the widow ran the small farm by herself.","t":"丈夫過世後，這位寡婦獨自經營小農場。"},{"w":"widower","p":"n.","d":"a man whose wife has died and who has not married again","c":"鰥夫","s":"Mr. Lin has been a widower since his wife died of cancer.","t":"林先生自從妻子死於癌症後就一直是鰥夫。"},{"w":"widowed","p":"adj.","d":"having lost your husband or wife through death","c":"喪偶的","s":"My widowed aunt moved in with us last year, and the house feels livelier now that she bakes cookies with my little sister.","t":"我喪偶的阿姨去年搬來和我們一起住，現在她會和我妹妹一起烤餅乾，家裡感覺更熱鬧了。"},{"w":"witness","p":"n./v.","d":"a person who sees an event happen, especially a crime or accident","c":"目擊者；目擊；見證","s":"The police asked the only witness to describe the driver.","t":"警方請唯一的目擊者描述駕駛的樣貌。"},{"w":"witnesses","p":"n. pl.","d":"people who see something happen","c":"目擊者們","s":"Several people witnessed the car accident at the crossroads.","t":"好幾個人目擊了十字路口的車禍。"},{"w":"worth","p":"adj./n.","d":"having a certain value; good enough to do","c":"值得的；價值","s":"This museum is worth visiting if you like history.","t":"如果你喜歡歷史，這間博物館值得一去。"},{"w":"worthy","p":"adj.","d":"deserving respect, praise, or attention","c":"值得的","s":"Her idea is worthy of serious discussion.","t":"她的想法值得認真討論。"},{"w":"worthless","p":"adj.","d":"having no value or use","c":"無價值的","s":"The old coins turned out to be completely worthless; nobody wanted to buy them.","t":"那些舊硬幣結果一文不值，沒人想買。"},{"w":"worthwhile","p":"adj.","d":"useful or important enough to spend time, money, or effort on","c":"值得做的","s":"Volunteering at the animal shelter is a worthwhile way to spend your summer vacation.","t":"在動物收容所當志工是度過暑假很值得的方式。"}]}];
